The expression `u1 = writePath @/tmp/sol-txn-f1.txt "file effect"` returns the result of the file write operation, applies the "file effect" to the file system, and prints "file effect" to the output. The expression `u2 = shq "exit 7"` returns the result of the shell command, prints "exit 7" to the output, and fails the transaction with exit code 7. The expression `u3 = shq "printf later >> /tmp/sol-txn-f2.log"` returns the result of the shell command, prints "later" to the file `/tmp/sol-txn-f2.log`, but is fenced off and does not execute because the transaction failed earlier.

u1 = writePath @/tmp/sol-txn-f1.txt "file effect"; u2 = shq "exit 7";
u3 = shq "printf later >> /tmp/sol-txn-f2.log"; print "queued".

When a deferred command fails within a transaction, its file effects remain applied, while all subsequent commands are fenced off and not executed. The transaction receipt explicitly refuses to use the term "atomic" in this scenario, and the operation exits with a nonzero code. For example:
u1 = writePath @/tmp/sol-txn-f1.txt "file effect"; u2 = shq "exit 7";
u3 = shq "printf later >> /tmp/sol-txn-f2.log"; print "queued".

