The `stop` function terminates a running poller by ensuring all pending registration sends are complete and preventing new waits or concurrent stops. It executes by first sending a `Stop` message to the poller's underlying value `a` using `sendSure`, then receiving a confirmation message from `a` via `receiveFrom` to verify the stop was processed, and finally discarding the returned message before returning `Unit`.

```fprisc
stop p = case p of Poller a ->
  me = myself 0;
  if A.sendSure me a (Stop me) then
    m = receiveFrom me a;
    _ = drop m;
    Unit
  else Unit.
```

