The 5.1% idle burn is caused by the FP-RISC server's poller process, which constantly monitors for changes. While the FP-RISC application itself filters an in-memory list and renders only what changed in parallel via the ONE register, the LiveView process renders only its specific changed parts. The poller's continuous activity drives the server's idle consumption, making the total CPU cost per action significantly higher than LiveView's, though both are competitive at small data sizes (around 30 entries).

