// With CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_MADVISE=y, subsequent faults avoid the 27% cost
```

Enabling `CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_MADVISE` prevents performance penalties during memory allocation by avoiding the cost of zeroing 2 MiB pages on every fault that occurs when transparent huge pages are handed back and refaulted. With this setting, allocation performance levels with the rest of the system, whereas having THP set to `always` incurs a 27% buildroot overhead due to the repeated faulting and zeroing process.

```sol
// Example Sol code demonstrating memory allocation where THP behavior impacts faulting
let pool = allocPool(1024);
// With CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_MADVISE=y, faults do not incur the 27% overhead
// seen when THP is always active and pages are re-zeroed on reset.
```

