The `logged` function acts as a middleware wrapper that intercepts every incoming HTTP request, executes the actual handler, and then logs the outcome based on the response status code. It constructs a log record containing the HTTP method, path, status code, and response body size. If the response status is 400 or higher, it logs a warning indicating a failure; otherwise, it logs an info message. Finally, it returns the modified response.

```sol
logged log handler req =
  resp = handler req;
  fields = ("method", req.method) :: ("path", req.path) :: ("status", str resp.status) :: ("bytes", str (strlen resp.body)) :: Nil;
  _ = (case resp.status >= 400 of True -> Log.warn log "request failed" fields | False -> Log.info log "request" fields);
  resp.
```

