To spawn a timer actor, use the `spawn` function with the name of the actor module (e.g., `TM.actor`) to create a new thread. This actor must then be passed as a value to the `caps` parameter when calling `Svc.write`, which establishes the capability-gated connection. The timer actor receives the write request and, once the elapsed time matches the requested duration, sends a `TFire` message back to the caller's mailbox.

