If an actor admitted but not yet popped is added to the backlog, it can receive a stale push from a waker, resulting in two run queue entries where the second points to itself, causing the hart to spin indefinitely in the dequeue loop. The memory actor prevents this by enforcing a guard that forbids adding any actor currently in the run queue to the backlog again, ensuring stale pushes are ignored.

