When a `FPut` request arrives, the function calculates the shard index by dividing the key by the configuration span. If the index already exists, it retrieves the existing shard and sends an `SPut` request; if not, it spawns a new shard and inserts it into the shard map. After receiving a confirmation of the new count, the function updates the global counts map and sends a `FDone` message with the updated total to the caller.

```fpr
idx = (cfg.key x) / cfg.span;
(sh, shards2) = (case M.get idx shards of
    O.Some s -> (s, shards)
  | O.None -> s = spawnShard cfg idx; (s, M.insert idx s shards));
r = A.askSure self sh (SPut x);
n = (case r of SCountIs c -> c | _ -> 0);
_ = drop r;
counts2 = M.insert idx n counts;
_ = A.sendSure self from (FDone (total counts2));
```

When a `FPut` request arrives, the function calculates the shard index using the key and configuration span. If the index is not found in the shards map (`O.None`), it spawns a new shard via `spawnShard`, inserts it into the map, and then asks that new shard to perform the `SPut` operation. The function records the count of successful operations in the shard and updates the total counts before sending a completion message to the caller.

```fprisc
idx = (cfg.key x) / cfg.span;
(sh, shards2) = (case M.get idx shards of
    O.None -> s = spawnShard cfg idx; (s, M.insert idx s shards));
r = A.askSure self sh (SPut x);
n = (case r of SCountIs c -> c | _ -> 0);
counts2 = M.insert idx n counts;
```

