The `orbit` function recursively calculates the next position and velocity of a point moving under a specific force field, defined by the formula $a = -0.02 \cdot \vec{r} / |\vec{r}|^3$. It includes a point in the resulting list only if the current step index `k` is a multiple of the `every` parameter, effectively filtering the trajectory for visualization.

```sol
orbit k every x y vx vy | k <= 0 = [].
orbit k every x y vx vy =
  r2 = x * x + y * y;
  r3 = r2 * Num.sqrt r2;
  vx2 = vx - x / r3 * 0.02;
  vy2 = vy - y / r3 * 0.02;
  x2 = x + vx2 * 0.02;
  y2 = y + vy2 * 0.02;
  rest = orbit (k - 1) every x2 y2 vx2 vy2;
  case (k % every) == 0 of
    True -> (x, y) :: rest
  | False -> rest.
```

