The register is designed as a single actor to ensure every event serializes through it, which simplifies the runtime model. However, this design causes every broadcast to copy the entire model once per session, creating significant overhead during high-concurrency events like a login burst at 512 sessions. To mitigate this, applications should implement state per session actor and use diffs on the broadcast rather than relying on the runtime's global model copying.

```sol
// Example of state per session actor pattern to avoid full model broadcast copies
actor session_state {
    let data: Map<SessionId, State> = new Map();

    // Instead of broadcasting the whole model, broadcast only the delta
    func update(key: SessionId, delta: State) {
        data[key] = data.get(key) or new State();
        data[key] = data[key] + delta;
        broadcast(diff(data)); // Broadcast only the difference
    }
}
```

