  let x = 42;
  print(x);
}
```

The `grownSlack` function calculates the amount of unused space along a specific axis (width for rows, height for columns) that should be distributed equally among all `Grow` children in a list. It first determines the total width or height of the children and the total gap space between them, then subtracts these used dimensions from the container's available space. If any children have the `Grow` attribute, the remaining slack is divided by the count of those children; otherwise, it returns zero.

```fpr
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

