A single byte transfer is defined by the `xferByte` function, which invokes `xbGo` to iterate 8 times, shifting the accumulator left and incorporating the received bit on each cycle. The SPI operates in Mode 0 with the clock idle low; data is written to the MOSI pin while the clock is low, and the clock transitions high on the rising edge for both sides to sample the miso signal. The clock then transitions low on the falling edge to allow the next bit to change.

```sol
xferByte bus b = xbGo bus b 7 0.
xbGo bus b i acc =
  case i < 0 of
    True -> acc
  | False -> xbBit bus b i acc.
xbBit bus b i acc =
  Bus pinW pinR sck mosi miso = bus;
  _ = pinW mosi (bitOf b i);
  _ = pinW sck 1;
  r = pinR miso;
  _ = pinW sck 0;
  xbGo bus b (i - 1) (acc * 2 + r).
```

