In the QOS-x86_64 target (`--target=qx64`), the three thread-local cells (`fpr_posix_hart`, `fpr_x64_a6/a7`) used by hosted lowering are implemented as plain globals loaded RIP-relative rather than dynamic TLS blocks. This design choice exists because a loaded app is single-hart (one hart equals one writer, making a global correct) and the fixed-slot image lacks a dynamic loader to register a TLS block; using `@tpoff` constants would incorrectly index the host's `%fs` TCB.

```sol
