The `jobWait` function initiates a non-blocking Wi-Fi or BLE operation by first allocating a job slot via `Esp.jobNew` and binding its interrupt handler to the calling actor using `Sys.irqBind`. It then spawns a helper task to asynchronously execute the specified action (`start`), waits for the result via `receive`, and finally sends the result text back to the caller as an `Ok` or `Err` value. This mechanism ensures that the calling actor does not block while waiting for the ESP-IDF job to complete.

```sol
jobWait boss start self =
  slot = Esp.jobNew Unit;
  _ = Sys.irqBind slot self;
  r = (case start slot of
      0 -> m = receive self; _ = drop m; Esp.jobResult slot
    | _ -> _ = Esp.jobResult slot; "error\tthe job queue is full");
  _ = send boss (Ok r);
  Unit.
```

