The `mMul` function computes the product of two matrices `a` (dimensions `r1 x k`) and `b` (dimensions `k x c`) by first validating their dimensions and then delegating the core computation to the native `Vec.mmul` function. It returns a new matrix of dimensions `r1 x c` containing the result, along with the original input matrices as arguments. The function ensures type safety by checking that the inner dimensions match and returns a tuple of the resulting matrix and the two input matrices.

```sol
mMul a b =
  (ra, ka, a2) = mDims a;
  (kb, cb, b2) = mDims b;
  u = mMulGuard ra ka kb cb;
  Mat r1 c1 va = a2;
  Mat r2 c2 vb = b2;
  (vo, va2, vb2) = Vec.mmul ra ka cb va vb;
  (Mat ra cb vo, Mat r1 c1 va2, Mat r2 c2 vb2).
```

