When a backlog exceeds the `DONATE_HI` threshold, the oldest entry is donated to a single machine-wide FIFO under a global lock, preserving its original stamp and age. This ensures that donated actors do not reset their aging; instead, the steal FIFO serves them in oldest-donated-first order, which tightens the admission bound. Consequently, the wait time for an actor `a` is bounded by `Wait(a) <= tau * T_slot + A * T_slot`, where `A` represents ready actors on the hart, because migration never invalidates the priority established by the actor's timestamp.

```fpr
// Example logic for donating and popping in the steal discipline
if (backlog_size > DONATE_HI) {
    // Donate oldest entry while preserving its stamp (age)
    donated_actor = deq(backlog_fifo); 
    enqueue(machine_steal_fifo, donated_actor);
}

// Idle hart pops head from steal FIFO before sleeping
if (idle) {
    actor = deq(machine_steal_fifo); 
    // actor retains its original age; no rescheduling reset
    sleep(actor); 
}
```

