In QOS, the host application's memory growth is managed via a growth callback that acts as the analogue to the Memory.qa process tier. This callback receives buddy grants from the host arena and is invoked whenever the application needs additional memory. Since there is only one program running, the traditional multi-tier process model is replaced by this direct callback mechanism, allowing the application to request and receive memory grants without a separate system process.

```fprisc
// Example of a growth callback in Sol (FPRISC)
// Called by the host when the app requests more memory
fn grow_memory (requested_size: u64) -> u64 {
  // Request grant from host arena via HAL
  let grant = hal_request_grant(requested_size)
  if grant.is_valid {
    return grant.size
  } else {
    return 0 // Failure case
  }
}
```

