The `rowStr` function takes an unsafe framebuffer, the y-buffer offset, pixel width, starting x-coordinate, and an initial accumulator string. It recursively processes the framebuffer in 8-character chunks, converting pixel values to ANSI escape codes for color and background, until the row is complete or the x-coordinate exceeds the pixel width.

```sol
rowStr fb yb pw x acc | x >= pw = (fb, acc);
rowStr fb yb pw x acc =
