answer:
Arguments passed to HAL functions are borrowed; the callee must not decrement their reference count and must increment (promote) any data it stores beyond the call boundary, such as in send or spawn operations. Return values are owned by the caller's actor slab. Failure to promote retained pointers constitutes a use-after-death bug during actor teardown.

