The code calculates sine and cosine values for the yaw angle, then combines the forward and right distances to determine the new velocity components in the x and z axes, which are added to the current velocity before returning the updated model state.

```sol
moveByV : unsafe Mdl -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Int -> Mdl .
moveByV (Mdl (Bd px py pz vx vy vz g) yaw pit sel act) f r =
  sw = sinA yaw;
  cw = cosA yaw;
  nvx = (f * sw + r * cw) * moveV / fx;
  nvz = (f * cw - r * sw) * moveV / fx;
  Mdl (Bd px py pz (vx + nvx) vy (vz + nvz) g) yaw pit sel "move".
```

