```sol
moveBy (Mdl (Bd px py pz vx vy vz g) yaw pit sel act) f r =
  sw = sinA yaw; cw = cosA yaw;
  nvx = (f * sw + r * cw) * moveV / fx;
  nvz = (f * cw - r * sw) * moveV / fx;
  Mdl (Bd px py pz (vx + nvx) vy (vz + nvz) g) yaw pit sel "move".
```

The `moveBy` function calculates new velocity by applying trigonometric functions to the yaw angle to determine the sine and cosine components, which are then used to mix the forward and right movement vectors. Specifically, it computes `sw` and `cw` as the sine and cosine of the yaw, and derives the new velocity changes (`nvx`, `nvz`) by combining the forward distance `f` and right distance `r` with these trigonometric values, scaling the result by the move velocity and dividing by the frame size.

```fprisc
sw = sinA yaw; cw = cosA yaw;
nvx = (f * sw + r * cw) * moveV / fx;
nvz = (f * cw - r * sw) * moveV / fx;
```

