The `ticker` function defines a periodic task that runs asynchronously for a specific message key within a codec. It sleeps for a duration determined by the message interval (`ms`), then checks if the task is still desired by querying the system state (`A.askSure`). If the system confirms the task is wanted, it recursively calls itself to repeat the cycle; otherwise, it terminates. This mechanism allows the system to handle time-sensitive operations without blocking the main application thread.

```fprisc
ticker reg ms key self =
  _ = Sys.sleepUs (ms * 1000);
  r = A.askSure self reg (TickDue ms key);
  again = (case r of Wanted True -> True | _ -> False);
  _ = drop r;
  (if again then ticker reg ms key self else Unit).
```

