The `check_arc.py` suite validates FP-RISC's ownership management and garbage collection by executing stress tests such as 10,000 sharing/escape cycles, tail calls, and the destruction of large graphs (e.g., 12,000 nodes) under sanitizers. It confirms that memory destruction follows only managed ownership edges, ensuring zero live allocations remain after these operations.

```fprisc
// Example demonstrating tail call and graph destruction
fn main() -> Result {
    let mut stack = Stack::new();
    let mut graph = Graph::new();

    // Perform tail calls to exhaust recursion limits safely
    loop {
        stack.push(1);
        if stack.len() > 1000 {
            break;
        }
        stack.pop();
    }

    // Construct and destroy a large graph
    for i in 0..12000 {
        graph.add_node(i);
    }
    graph.destroy(); // Ensures zero live allocations

    Ok(())
}
```

