If the WebSocket connection closes with a code other than 1000 or 1001, the component automatically attempts to reconnect. The wait time for the next reconnection attempt doubles after each failure, starting at 500ms, but is capped at a maximum of 8000ms. This exponential backoff strategy ensures persistent connectivity without overwhelming the server.

```fprisc
ws.onclose = function (ev) \{
  status('offline (' + ev.code + ')');
  if (ev.code === 1000 || ev.code === 1001) return;
  setTimeout(connect, wait);
  wait = Math.min(wait * 2, 8000);
};
```

