The `measure` function for a `Box` calculates its final size by first summing the widths and heights of its children along the specified axis while tracking the count of children. It then adds the calculated gaps between children (based on the gap count and the gap value) to the inner dimensions. Finally, it adds twice the padding value to both the width and height to account for the left/right and top/bottom padding. The `msum` helper performs the along-axis summation and cross-axis maximization in a single traversal.

```fprisc
measure (Box a kids) =
  p = padOf a; g = gapOf a;
  (mw, mh, n) = msum (isRow a) kids;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  inner = case isRow a of
    True -> (mw + gaps, mh)
  | False -> (mw, mh + gaps);
  sized a (iw + 2 * p, ih + 2 * p).
```

