// Subsequent usage must respect the linear lifecycle phases of the handle
```

The QOS system enforces permissions by requiring the application to declare its needs in a manifest using capability names (e.g., "uart"). During the load process, the host checks this manifest against granted permissions (up to 32 per app) and either grants the capability or refuses the load. Any subsequent call outside of the granted capability results in a refusal error explicitly naming the capability that was denied.

```fprisc
// Application manifest declaring a need for the uart service
