The `frameWorker` function establishes a recursive loop that continuously polls for new input using `pollInput` with a 64-unit timeout, calculates the next player position based on key inputs via the `move` function, and renders the updated scene by calling `renderFrame`. After rendering, it constructs a new `Frame` record containing the updated coordinates and input state, sends this record back to the parent process via `send`, and resets the system pool before recursing to maintain the animation loop.

```fprisc
frameWorker parent self =
  message = receiveFrom self parent;
  Frame x z keys buttons yaw pitch = message;
  _ = drop message;
  Input nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch =
    pollInput (Input keys buttons yaw pitch) 64;
  (nextX, nextZ) = move x z nextKeys;
  _ = renderFrame nextX nextZ nextYaw nextPitch;
  reply = Frame nextX nextZ nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch;
  _ = send parent reply;
  _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
  frameWorker parent self.
```

