// If needed, it will double automatically
qa_t.perms = double_heap_array(qa_t.perms);
```

The system no longer uses a fixed 4096-byte buffer or a 32-capability limit; instead, `qa_t.perms` is implemented as a heap array that dynamically doubles to accommodate the grants. When serializing capabilities, the serializer now sizes the output buffer exactly to fit the granted permissions rather than returning early upon buffer overflow, ensuring all grants reach the application.

```sol
// Example: Dynamic allocation for capabilities
let perms = new_array<perm_t>();
while (grant_count > perms.length) {
    perms.resize(perms.length * 2);
}
// Serialize exactly to the granted count
let serialized = serialize_grants(perms, grant_count);
```

