sys.hart(1).gpio_set(26, 1);

// POSIX style: Process abstraction, OS manages resources
process.main() {
    thread t1 = spawn("led1");
    thread t2 = spawn("led2");
    // t1 and t2 are isolated processes managed by the OS
}
```

The ESP-IDF port manages memory like a bare-metal system but lacks the virtual memory guard pages and process isolation of POSIX. It assumes the runtime owns the heap and both cores, taking all RAM from linker symbols to drive hardware peripherals like GPIO and the radio directly without an operating system file system or threads.

```sol
