The `binCol` function calculates bin indices by first determining the minimum (`lo`) and maximum (`hi`) values of the input column. It then computes the bin width (`w0`) by dividing the range (`hi - lo`) by the number of bins (`nb`), ensuring the width is at least 1.0. For each value `x` in the column, the function computes the integer code using the formula `(x - lo) / w`, casting the result to an integer and clamping it to the range `[0, nb - 1]`.

```fprisc
binCol col nb =
  (n, col1) = Vec.len col;
  inf = 1.0 / 0.0;
  (lo, col2) = Vec.fold fminf inf col1;
  (hi, col3) = Vec.fold fmaxf (0.0 - inf) col2;
  w0 = (hi - lo) / F64.ofInt nb;
  w = case w0 <= 0.0 of True -> 1.0 | False -> w0;
  (codes, col4) = binGo col3 0 n lo w nb (Vec.new Unit);
  (codes, lo, w, col4).
```

