The `grownSlack` function calculates the available space by subtracting the used dimensions of children and gaps from the container's inner size, then divides the result evenly among all `Grow` children. It first sums the widths or heights of the children and multiplies the gap size by the number of gaps (which is one less than the number of children if there are multiple). It determines the available space by accounting for padding on both sides, and finally uses integer division to allocate the slack equally to each `Grow` child, returning zero if no `Grow` children exist or if the result is non-positive.

```fprisc
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

The `grownSlack` function calculates the total available space along an axis by subtracting twice the padding (`p`) from the container's dimension (`w` or `h`). It determines the space used by `Grow` children by summing their measured sizes and adding the gaps between them (`gapOf a * (n - 1)`), while ignoring non-`Grow` children. The remaining slack is divided equally among all children possessing the `grow` attribute using integer division (`idiv`); if no children have the `grow` attribute, the result is zero.

```sol
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

