The implementation defines the SPI bus as a 5-slot constructor `Bus pinW pinR sck mosi miso` and executes a full duplex transfer by iterating over bits from most to least significant. For each bit, it sets the MOSI pin to the extracted bit value, drives the clock high (rising edge) to sample the MISO pin, and drives the clock low (falling edge) to prepare for the next bit, accumulating the result in the accumulator.

```sol
xbBit bus b i acc =
  Bus pinW pinR sck mosi miso = bus;
  _ = pinW mosi (bitOf b i);
  _ = pinW sck 1;
  r = pinR miso;
  _ = pinW sck 0;
  xbGo bus b (i - 1) (acc * 2 + r).
```

