The PLIC implements a CLAIM-THEN-MASK strategy to prevent storms. When an interrupt source is claimed, the PLIC immediately masks it; the actor then services the device and re-arms the source via Sys.irqAck. If the interrupt line remains high after re-arming, the PLIC will pend the interrupt again for a fresh, exactly-once delivery.

