The platform distinguishes these by intent: an operation belongs in the language specification (`L_n`) if implementing it as an ordinary library abstraction cannot preserve its intended meaning or guarantees, such as when it requires defining syntax, evaluation rules, ownership checks, or primitive effect mechanisms. Conversely, the Base standard library (`S_n`) provides the canonical types, operations, and minimal environmental interfaces that programmers should not have to redefine, effectively completing the language into an immediately usable system.

