```fprisc
serve self h st =
  m = receive self;
  (rt, q) = m;
  (st2, r) = h st q;
  _ = send rt r;
  _ = drop m;
  serve self h st2.
```

The `drop` function discards the message `m` received from the runtime after it has been processed by the handler, ensuring that the message is not sent back to the caller and that the runtime does not attempt to deliver it again. This is critical because the runtime owns the roots of the message, meaning the drop operation is safe and the message cannot be lost or re-delivered.

