In the FP-RISC QOS environment, an application can poll a UART receive buffer by repeatedly calling the `U.readRx` function from the `std/uart` module, checking the string length, and using a recursive `nap` function to wait for a timeout if the buffer is empty. Once data is available, the first character of the received string is extracted using the `charAt` function on the first index of the string.

```fpr
U = use "std/uart";

-- Poll until data arrives or timeout (dl) passes
waitRx u dl =
  (s, u2) = U.readRx u;
  if strlen s > 0 then (s, u2)
  else nap dl >> waitRx u2 dl;

-- Non-blocking wait with timeout
