```

In FP-RISC, the `moveBy` function updates a model's velocity based on the current yaw angle. To move forward, you use the sine of the yaw; to move right, you use the cosine. The implementation calculates new velocity components by combining the forward distance (`f`) and right distance (`r`) with trigonometric functions of the yaw, then adds these to the existing velocity vector.

```fprisc
moveBy (Mdl (Bd px py pz vx vy vz g) yaw pit sel act) f r =
  sw = sinA yaw; cw = cosA yaw;
  nvx = (f * sw + r * cw) * moveV / fx;
  nvz = (f * cw - r * sw) * moveV / fx;
  Mdl (Bd px py pz (vx + nvx) vy (vz + nvz) g) yaw pit sel "move".
```

