```

The `pAnim` function creates an SVG polyline that morphs through a list of frames using SMIL interpolation, with axes automatically calculated from the combined bounds of all frames. It constructs the animation by first determining the axis bounds, then generating a continuous string of points for the `<animate>` element, and finally wrapping the result in an SVG structure.

```sol
pAnim title dur frames =
  bx = allBounds frames;
  b = axes bx (svgOpen title (BStr.new Unit));
  vals = BStr.toStr (valsGo bx frames (BStr.new Unit));
  first = ptsS bx (frames ! 1);
