The `init` command configures the SCL pin to a high level and the SDO pin to a low level, followed by a high pulse on SCL. To trigger a bit read, the `rmBit` function asserts the SCL pin low to generate a falling edge, which causes the chip to shift the next bit onto the SDO pin, before asserting SCL high again.

```sol
init pinM scl sdo =
  _ = pinM scl 1;
  _ = pinM sdo 0;
  pinM scl 1.

rmBit pinW pinR scl sdo i acc =
  _ = pinW scl 0;
  b = pinR sdo;
  _ = pinW scl 1;
```

