```

The `waking` function in the Poller actor acts as a loop to process incoming messages until the interrupt is cleared. It receives a message, checks if it is zero (indicating the interrupt is done), and if so, unbinds the IRQ, sends a `WakerStopped` signal, and terminates. Otherwise, it acknowledges the interrupt (`Sys.irqAck`) and re-sends the `Woke` signal to continue waiting.

```sol
fn waking poller irq self =
  m = receive self;
  done = m == 0;
  if done then
    unbind irq;
    A.sendSure self poller WakerStopped;
    Unit
  else
    Sys.irqAck irq;
    A.sendSure self poller Woke;
    waking poller irq self.
```

The `waking` function implements a polling loop that waits for an interrupt signal to be acknowledged by the OS. It receives a message from the actor, checks if it is a zero-value signal indicating completion, and either unbinds the IRQ and signals a stopped state if done, or acknowledges the interrupt and loops back to wait for the next signal.

```fpr
waking : unsafe Int -> Int -> Int -> Unit .
waking poller irq self =
  m = receive self;
  done = m == 0;
  _ = drop m;
  if done then
    _ = unbind irq;
    _ = A.sendSure self poller WakerStopped;
    Unit
  else
    _ = Sys.irqAck irq;
    _ = A.sendSure self poller Woke;
    waking poller irq self.
```

