In the linear regime, `alloc` performs a grow-by-doubling strategy when the buffer needs to expand, and the memory is released entirely at once via `dealloc` at the single consume point.
```sol
// Linear regime example: growth is doubling, release is all-at-once
let v = alloc(Vec, 1024);
v.push(1); v.push(2);
// ... later, when capacity is exceeded ...
v = realloc(v, 2048); // Growth: doubling
// ... eventually ...
