The `grownSlack` function calculates the amount of extra space available to be distributed equally among `Grow` children within a container. It first determines the total width and height of the children and the number of gaps between them based on the container's axis. It then computes the available space by subtracting the total used width or height (including gaps) from the container's inner dimension, accounting for padding. Finally, it divides this remaining space by the count of `Grow` children to determine the slack per child, returning zero if there are no `Grow` children or if the available space is non-positive.

```fprisc
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

The function `grownSlack` returns the integer amount of slack space to be distributed among the children. For the specified scenario, it calculates the available width as `w - 2 * p` and the used width as `w` (since `n=2` results in `gaps = 0`), yielding a difference of `2 * p - w`. This value is then divided by the count of `Grow` children (`n-1` in this case, which is 1), resulting in the integer `2 * p - w` (or 0 if negative due to the `idiv` guard).

```sol
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

The function `grownSlack` calculates the slack by first summing the measures of all children in the given row or column. It determines the gap between children using `gapOf` and multiplies it by the number of children minus one if there is more than one child. The available space is derived by subtracting twice the padding from the container's dimension along that axis. Finally, if any children are marked to grow, the remaining space is divided equally among them using `idiv`.

```sol
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

