The `kpScan1` function returns an `Int` representing the result of the hardware scan operation performed by `MK.scan`. Within its logic, `rows` is defined as the first four elements of the provided pin list `ps` (representing the keypad rows), while `cols` is defined as the remaining four elements of `ps` (representing the keypad columns). These two lists are subsequently passed to `MK.init` to initialize the pin mode before triggering the scan.

