The `connModel` function iterates through the application model using `connLoop` and invokes `G.render` to generate a new state (`s2`) and delta (`d2`). It compares the new state's statics against the previous ones using `G.sameStatics`. If the statics are identical, it sends a delta containing only the data changes via `pushDelta`. If the statics have changed, it sends a full render containing both the new state and the delta in a JSON frame.

```sol
pushOne st =
  Cs reg port cfg app cid mode buf sid ls ld model = st;
  App ini upd vw sbs = app;
  (s2, d2) = G.render (vw sid model);
  _ = case G.sameStatics ls s2 of
      True -> pushDelta cid (G.deltaJson ld d2)
    | False -> _ = netWrite cid (wsFrame 1 "\{\"s\":{G.jarr s2},\"d\":{G.jarr d2}}"); 0;
  Cs reg port cfg app cid mode buf sid s2 d2 model.
```

The `pushOne` function executes a single render cycle for a specific session by updating the model, rendering the view, and determining the appropriate data transmission strategy. It extracts the current application state, calls the render function to generate a new view and delta, and then checks if the static layout has changed. If the layout is identical, it sends a delta; otherwise, it sends a full JSON representation of the state. The function returns a new session context containing the updated view and delta, which is then passed to `connLoop` for the next iteration.

