The `leadSlack` function calculates the space available for growth along a specific axis when no children are growing. It first computes the total width or height of the children and gaps, then determines the available space by subtracting padding and the used dimensions from the container's dimension. If any child is set to grow, it returns 0; otherwise, it returns half the difference between the available space and the used space.

```fpr
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

