The Sol scripting profile specifies a contract covering entry sequencing, imports, resource ownership, transaction boundaries, and host facilities, which the program must adhere to. While the implementation may choose internal techniques like JIT thresholds or memory management, it must preserve these observable guarantees and behaviors. The Sol profile acts as the required surface and execution guarantees, distinct from the underlying FP-RISC language or the host runtime.

