The file `fprisc/std/mvu.fpr` defines the core logic for the MVU (Model-View-Update) rendering engine within the FP-RISC QOS operating system. It implements the `renderWorker` function, which manages the asynchronous rendering pipeline by receiving input from a parent, invoking the application's `vals` function to compute the view model, and synchronizing updates via `svcCall`. The file also provides timing utilities like `waitTick` and `napTick` to handle event pacing and frame boundaries using the system's millisecond timer (`mt`), ensuring the application runs at the configured tick rate without stalling the core.

```sol
renderWorker parent render env vl self =
  m = receiveFrom self parent;
  Rq st model vw vh sc fr = m;
  vs = vl self env (vw, vh) model;
  r = svcCall self render (Render st vs sc fr);
  _ = send parent r;
  _ = drop r;
  _ = drop m;
  _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
  renderWorker parent render env vl self;
```

