The system enforces a concurrency control mechanism where only one process can successfully execute the write operation on a given path at a time; any process that detects a conflict must retry its transaction. This is demonstrated by the `sleepMs` delay allowing another process to acquire the lock, followed by a successful `writePath` operation that updates the file content.

