  (mw, mh, n) = msum (isRow a) kids;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  inner = case isRow a of
    True -> (mw + gaps, mh)
  | False -> (mw, mh + gaps);
  sized a (iw + 2 * p, ih + 2 * p).
```

The `measure` function for a `Box` calculates its total width and height by first using `msum` to sum the widths of children along the row axis and the maximum height across all children, accounting for gaps and padding. The `msum` function performs a single walk through the children list, accumulating the sum of widths (`kw + sw`) and the maximum height (`imax kh sh`) depending on whether the box is a row or column. Finally, `measure` adds twice the padding to both the resulting width and height to determine the final size.

```fprisc
Box a kids =
  p = padOf a; g = gapOf a;
  (mw, mh, n) = msum (isRow a) kids;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  inner = case isRow a of
    True -> (mw + gaps, mh)
  | False -> (mw, mh + gaps);
  sized a (inner.1 + 2 * p, inner.2 + 2 * p).
```

