Currently, the launcher resolves the manifest `entry` symbol against apps co-compiled into System.qa and dispatches them by name (e.g., `Apps.entry` -> `Apps.run`). When the real ELF-in-ELF loader is implemented, only the `runEntry` function changes; it adds a `LaunchElf` branch to map the `.qa` ELF section into a fresh process and jump to its entry with the same capabilities. This architecture ensures that no app, manifest, or permission flow changes are required during the transition.

```fprisc
// Conceptual example of the runEntry function modification
fn runEntry caps = {
    if (isELFReady) {
        LaunchElf(caps) // Maps .qa ELF section and jumps to entry
    } else {
        // Current behavior: dispatch by name
        Apps.run(caps) 
    }
}
```

