The application structure relies on a recursive `frameWorker` function that continuously polls for new input and renders the scene. The `pollInput` function gathers updated key, button, and camera state every 64 milliseconds, which are then used to calculate the next player position via `move` and trigger a `renderFrame` call. After rendering, the updated state is packaged into a new `Frame` message and sent back to the parent process to drive the next iteration of the loop.

```fprisc
frameWorker parent self =
  message = receiveFrom self parent;
  Frame x z keys buttons yaw pitch = message;
  _ = drop message;
  Input nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch =
    pollInput (Input keys buttons yaw pitch) 64;
  (nextX, nextZ) = move x z nextKeys;
  _ = renderFrame nextX nextZ nextYaw nextPitch;
  reply = Frame nextX nextZ nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch;
  _ = send parent reply;
  _ = drop reply;
  _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
  frameWorker parent self.
```

