The `grownSlack` function calculates the slack available along an axis (width for rows, height for columns) after accounting for padding and gaps between children. It determines the total space consumed by the children's measured sizes plus the gaps required between them, then divides the remaining difference evenly among all Grow children if any exist. If no children are marked as Grow, the result is zero.

```fprisc
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

Leftover space, or slack, is calculated by determining the available dimension (width or height) minus the sum of all children's measured sizes and the gaps between them. This total slack is then divided equally among all children that have the Grow attribute. The distribution function `grownSlack` computes the number of gaps between children, sums their widths and heights, and uses integer division to allocate the remainder to each Grow child.

```fprisc
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

