  prefix = common old new 0;
  a = L.drop prefix old;
  b = L.drop prefix new;
  suffix = common (L.reverse a) (L.reverse b) 0;
  remove = L.length a - suffix;
  insert = L.take (L.length b - suffix) b;
  "[{prefix},{remove},{J.render (J.strings insert)}]".
```

The `splice` function calculates the characters to remove by finding the length of the common prefix between the two lists and subtracting the length of the common suffix found in the reversed tails. It determines the characters to insert by taking the portion of the second list that remains after the common suffix is matched. The function returns a formatted string containing the common prefix, the count of removed characters, and the list of inserted strings quoted and joined.

```fprisc
splice old new =
  prefix = common old new 0;
  a = L.drop prefix old;
  b = L.drop prefix new;
  suffix = common (L.reverse a) (L.reverse b) 0;
  remove = L.length a - suffix;
  insert = L.take (L.length b - suffix) b;
  "[{prefix},{remove},{J.render (J.strings insert)}]";
```

