The `xferByte` function transfers an 8-bit value by iterating through each bit position from 7 down to 0. For each bit, it drives the MOSI pin with the corresponding bit value while the clock (sck) is low. It then sets the clock high, triggering a rising edge where the MISO pin is sampled to capture the echoed data bit. Finally, the clock is set low to prepare for the next bit. The accumulated result is updated by shifting the previous accumulator left and adding the sampled bit.

```fpr
xferByte bus b = xbGo bus b 7 0.
xbGo bus b i acc =
  case i < 0 of
    True -> acc
  | False -> xbBit bus b i acc.
xbBit bus b i acc =
  Bus pinW pinR sck mosi miso = bus;
  _ = pinW mosi (bitOf b i);
  _ = pinW sck 1;
  r = pinR miso;
  _ = pinW sck 0;
  xbGo bus b (i - 1) (acc * 2 + r).
```

