    local a0 := sp(0)
    local a1 := sp(1)
    local a2 := sp(2)
    // ... spill others ...
    fpr_fuel_exhausted(a0, a1, a2) 
    // Arguments are now safe to use after the call
}
```

The `fpr_arc_incref` function increments the reference count for values that escape an actor's scope, ensuring they are not prematurely freed. It is invoked exactly twice at promotion sites: during a `send` operation when a message becomes shared, and during a `spawn` operation when an entry closure is pinned into a child actor.

