The QOS Loader reassembles the live set of code from records stored on the disk during the next boot, allowing hot-swapped applications to survive a reboot without explicit recompilation or reloading. This persistence occurs because the Loader reads the `sys/live` record chain upon startup and reconstructs the live environment directly from these stored records.

