A QOS driver is a software component for a single device that forms a closed algebra, directly using the QOS HAL API to interact with hardware, whereas everything above it is application or library code and everything below it is the HAL implementation. Misclassifying these components leads to architectural violations where non-driver code improperly accesses the HAL, or where drivers are treated as standalone executables rather than library code providing standardized interfaces.

```sol
