The system will fail to fuse the mask as a lane select, resulting in a data-dependent branch inside the hot loop instead of a single branch-light pass. To maintain performance and avoid this, `Vec.filter` must be used such that the predicate is evaluated branchlessly (e.g., via `cmov` or SIMD-select) to produce a MASK column, followed by an explicit `Vec.compact` or a frame-boundary `Sys.poolReset` to restore density.

```fprisc
// Incorrect: branching per element inside the loop
