// Correct: branchless mask followed by compaction
let mask = Vec.map (fun x -> x > 0) v
let good = Vec.compact mask v
```

`Vec.filter` slides kept rows down in place using two cursors to shrink the length without allocation, keeping the vector dense for subsequent passes. To avoid branching per element, it evaluates the predicate branchlessly to write a MASK column, which is then fused as a lane select to restore density via an explicit `Vec.compact` or automatic compaction at `Sys.poolReset`.

```fprisc
let v = Vec.filter (fun x -> x > 0) [1; -1; 2; -2; 3]
