    stamp = 100;
    age = 200;
}

actor new_actor {
    stamp = 200;
    age = 50;
}

// When old_actor is stolen, it retains stamp=100.
// The steal FIFO serves it before new_actor (stamp=200),
// ensuring Wait(old_actor) <= tau * T_slot + A * T_slot
// holds tighter than if aging were reset upon migration.
```

When an actor's age exceeds tau, it outranks all un-aged actors on its hart and is served oldest-first among aged actors, with only earlier-stamped actors admitted ahead of it. This deterministic behavior ensures that donation and stealing preserve the actor's stamp and age, preventing migration from resetting the aging process and maintaining consistent worst-case wait times. The system uses a machine-wide FIFO under a single lock to manage these transfers, avoiding randomness or victim scanning.

```fpr
