An application implements frame pacing by calculating the time until the next tick using `tickWait` and then sleeping for that duration with `napTick` to ensure the next frame is delivered exactly when the timer expires. The `dueTick` function manages the interval logic by comparing the current time against the last delivery time and the requested tick interval, returning an event to trigger the render worker only when the interval has elapsed.

```sol
import Sys

main : unsafe Int -> Int -> Int -> model -> vals .
main mt t0 tickMs model =
  ltt = 0;
  while True do
    (evs, ltt) = dueTick [] t0 ltt tickMs;
    if evs == [] then break;
    _ = napTick mt t0 tickWait mt t0 (tickMs * 10);
    _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
    _ = renderWorker parent render env vl self mt t0 ltt tickMs model;
  end;
  model.
```

