    // Perform only raw, reentrant operations
    // e.g., read registers, update mscratch, call pure functions
    // Do not use allocation, managed refs, strings, or CSR writes
    unit
}
```

A checked resumable interrupt handler must not perform any allocation, managed construction, projection, string or printing operations, indirect calls, or CSR writes. Furthermore, the handler cannot exceed the eight-register argument ABI. The compiler enforces these checks by rejecting any call graph reachable from the interrupt entry point that violates these constraints to ensure reentrancy and safety.

```fprisc
machineInterrupt cause pc value {
    // Valid handler: only uses raw registers and raw writes
    let r1 = raw 1;
    let r2 = raw 2;
    // raw write to a known safe address (unsafe if address is unknown)
    raw_store ptr r1; 
    // ...
    mret
}
```

