  writePath "out.txt" "Data after commit";
};
# This block will not execute if the surrounding transaction is abandoned.
```

Use `Proc.afterCommit` to queue a structured process specification that executes after the filesystem commit. This approach ensures recoverability from the redo journal with at-least-once execution semantics, meaning the command must tolerate repetition. For example, to create a gzip tar archive, use the `archive.sol` script which utilizes `tar -czf`; if rerun, it simply replaces the existing named archive.

