  name: "make-archive",
  cmd: "tar -czf",
  args: ["output.tar.gz", "-C", ".", "."]
);

> Proc.afterCommit (spec);
```

`Proc.afterCommit` is used for repeatable external mutations that must tolerate repetition due to at-least-once recovery; it queues a structured process specification and cannot run in an abandoned transaction. In contrast, `Proc.runNow` is reserved for genuinely real-time effects that cannot wait for a commit and deliberately bypasses the rollback model.

Example usage for `Proc.afterCommit`:
```sol
