The fprc compiler computes the WCET by analyzing the Control Flow Graph (CFG) of emitted assembly to determine the maximum number of IR instructions between consecutive safepoint events, such as function entry or calls. Since loops are implemented as tail calls, the resulting structure is a DAG where back-edges are absent; encountering a back-edge would trigger a loud UNBOUNDED error. While a single function entry consumes one fuel unit, the work between entries (the function body) can be arbitrarily long, particularly if it contains a straight-line vector kernel or a large literal fold. To ensure timing safety, kernels must enforce a per-invocation lane cap where the total cost (N lanes multiplied by the cost per lane) does not exceed the quantum's time target defined in the hardware version (hw_v).

```fprc
// Example of a WCET comment added by fprc during compilation
