```

The `Proc.runNow` process executes immediately, before the queued `Proc.afterCommit` effects are processed. This occurs because queued effects are only executed at commit time, whereas `Proc.runNow` refuses to run if any effect is still pending in the transaction. Consequently, the output "ranNow" appears in the log before "queued".

