When an append error occurs, the write operation may have written some data to the storage device before failing, resulting in incomplete records that remain physically present on the disk. This situation is not automatically corrected by the system; it is not treated as a rolled-back transaction, and simply retrying the operation does not guarantee a safe or consistent state. Consequently, the application must handle these partial writes explicitly rather than assuming a clean slate after a failure.

```sol
