// The system state remains inconsistent, and further retries may corrupt data.
```

An append error can leave partial bytes on disk, and it is not a rolled-back transaction; therefore, callers must not assume that blind retries are safe. The system has no fsync policy or atomic multi-field commit to guarantee consistency.

```sol
