In the context of `Os.watchClose`, "yield and retry" describes an asynchronous teardown process where the caller pauses execution (yields) and attempts the operation again until the function returns True, which signals that the watch slot has been successfully released. This ensures the caller waits for the system to finish freeing descriptor buffers, waking descriptors, and allowing detached workers to exit before the handle can be considered free.

