The `msum` function returns `(0, 0, 0)` for an empty list. When this result is passed to the `Box` measure, the calculated inner width and height become `0`, and the final size becomes `(2*p, 2*p)`, effectively ignoring the padding logic intended for non-empty layouts. This can cause layout collapse or incorrect rendering if the box is expected to have content.

```fprisc
measure (Box a kids) =
  p = padOf a; g = gapOf a;
  (mw, mh, n) = msum (isRow a) kids;
  -- If kids is Nil, msum returns (0,0,0)
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  inner = case isRow a of
    True -> (mw + gaps, mh)
  | False -> (mw, mh + gaps);
  (iw, ih) = inner;
  sized a (iw + 2 * p, ih + 2 * p).
```

