The `bootWire` function initializes the QOS system by spawning the core actors (system, logging, and application) and registering them with the registry. It first creates the actors, then constructs a list of entity paths for both system logs and file system entities, combines them with application entities, and spawns the `vfsActor` to manage the unified view. Finally, it registers these components under specific service paths and calls the recursive `boot` function to continue the initialization sequence.

```sol
bootWire me st apps =
  sys = spawn sysActor;
  logA = spawn logActor;
  appsA = spawn (appsActor apps);
  ents0 = ("/services/log", 0, logA)
       :: ("/logs/normal", 1, logA)
       :: ("/logs/warns", 1, logA)
       :: ("/logs/errors", 1, logA) :: Nil;
  ents1 = bootFileEnts st;
  vfs = spawn (vfsActor (cat ents0 (cat ents1 (appEnts apps appsA))));
  reg = ("/services/vfs", vfs)
     :: ("/services/log", logA)
     :: ("/services/storage", st) :: Nil;
  _ = call me sys (Reg reg);
  Qsys sys st vfs logA appsA.
```

