The `mergeRuns` function recursively processes a list of integers to identify consecutive runs where the difference between adjacent elements does not exceed 5. It groups these runs into pairs representing their start and end indices. The implementation uses a helper function `mrGo` to traverse the list and `mrStep` to check the difference condition, yielding the first pair once the difference exceeds the threshold or the list is exhausted.

```sol
mergeRuns = fun xs = case xs of Nil -> Nil | x :: rest -> mrGo x x rest;

mrGo = fun s e xs = case xs of Nil -> (s, e) :: Nil | c :: cs -> mrStep s e c cs;

mrStep = fun s e c cs = case (c - e) <= 5 of True -> mrGo s c cs | False -> (s, e) :: mrGo c c cs;
```

