The `epoch` function implements a single iteration of gradient descent training for a polynomial regression model. It calculates gradients for the coefficients (a, b, c) by folding the vector of data points through three helper functions (`gA`, `gB`, `gC`) that accumulate the partial derivatives of the squared error residual with respect to each coefficient. The function then updates these coefficients by subtracting the learning rate scaled by the average gradient, returning the new coefficients and the final accumulated gradient sum.

```sol
epoch n lr a b c v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (gA a b c) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (gB a b c) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (gC a b c) 0 v2;
  (a - lr * (s1 / n), b - lr * (s2 / n), c - lr * (s3 / n), v3).
```

