The `qlog.fpr` file defines the functional logic for the Qlog module, which manages the write-ahead log used for durable storage in the QOS operating system. It implements core operations for writing data to the log buffer, compacting free space by reclaiming deleted entries, and constructing an index of live log chunks to optimize read performance. The module utilizes unsafe direct I/O (`blkWrite`) to append pages and `compact` to merge fragmented records, ensuring that subsequent reads traverse the index rather than performing random disk seeks.

```fpr
# Example of writing to the log buffer
writeBuf dev p pages = case pages of Nil -> p | pg :: r -> writeBuf2 dev p r pg;

# Example of compacting the log to reclaim space
compact dev head =
  ris = scanRIs dev head;
  ld = lastDels ris;
  kept = kGo ris ld (kaGo ris ld Nil) Nil;
  cpDo dev (metaOr dev head) (bufPages dev kept Nil) (mkRoot (lvGo dev kept Nil)).
```

The `writeBuf` function handles an empty list of pages by returning the page count `p`, and for a non-empty list, it calls `writeBuf2` to perform a bulk write on the first page and then recursively processes the remaining pages with an incremented page count.

```sol
fun writeBuf(dev: unsafe dv, p: Int, pages: List String): Int {
    case pages of
        Nil -> p
        pg :: r -> writeBuf2(dev, p, r, pg)
    end
}

fun writeBuf2(dev: unsafe dv, p: Int, r: List String, pg: String): Int {
    _ = blkWrite(dev, p, pg)
    writeBuf(dev, p + 1, r)
}
```

