Sys.sleepUs is a PARKED sleep where the actor blocks on its hart's sleeper list with an mtime deadline, allowing the hart-loop to wake other sleepers and arm the CLINT for the nearest deadline. Unlike a standard nanosleep which would block the hart thread itself, Sys.sleepUs leaves the hart thread (and all memory allocations associated with it) running. This distinction prevents the memory actor from being woken thousands of times a second just to wait out a sleep, as the hart remains active to service other actors.

```sol
