The launcher reads the application manifest from `/apps/<id>.qa` and grants only the permissions the user approves. If any required permission is denied, the application does not run; the launcher prints the specific error message "Cannot Run Application without all required compulsory Permissions" and the denial persists only for the current launch attempt. The application then receives only the granted capabilities as an opaque `caps` value, and its services enforce these permissions on every call to prevent silent failures.

