The `serveFront` function acts as a dispatcher that routes incoming operations to the appropriate shard based on a configuration key. When it receives an `FPut` operation, it first calculates the target shard index by dividing the configuration key of the data item by the configuration span. If a shard already exists at that index, it retrieves the existing shard; otherwise, it spawns a new one. The function then asks the selected shard to perform a `SPut` operation, counts the resulting items, updates the shard count map, and finally sends a confirmation message containing the total count of all shards back to the caller.

```fprisc
idx = (cfg.key x) / cfg.span;
(sh, shards2) = (case M.get idx shards of
    O.Some s -> (s, shards)
  | O.None -> s = spawnShard cfg idx; (s, M.insert idx s shards));
r = A.askSure self sh (SPut x);
n = (case r of SCountIs c -> c | _ -> 0);
counts2 = M.insert idx n counts;
_ = A.sendSure self from (FDone (total counts2));
