This design separates immutable file data from volatile state to ensure data integrity and efficient space reclamation. Data is append-only and bounded to prevent corruption, while swap acts as a circular buffer to allow overwriting of old entries when full. The mutable HEAD pointer in metadata allows the system to track the latest log entry's position, enabling the compaction process to merge chunks, mark pages for deletion, and reclaim space idempotently without altering the underlying file data.

