The `frameWorker` function implements the main game loop for the FP-RISC application. It continuously receives a `Frame` message containing the current state (coordinates, keys, buttons, and camera angles) from the parent process, extracts the necessary input data, and polls for new user input using `pollInput`. It then calculates the player's new position based on the pressed keys via the `move` function, renders the updated scene by calling `renderFrame`, and sends the new `Frame` message back to the parent to close the loop.

```sol
frameWorker parent self =
  message = receiveFrom self parent;
  Frame x z keys buttons yaw pitch = message;
  Input nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch =
    pollInput (Input keys buttons yaw pitch) 64;
  (nextX, nextZ) = move x z nextKeys;
  _ = renderFrame nextX nextZ nextYaw nextPitch;
  reply = Frame nextX nextZ nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch;
  _ = send parent reply;
  _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
  frameWorker parent self.
```

