The page-in trigger is initiated by the wake path when a sender performs a CAS(BLOCKED->READY) on a paged actor, shipping the event to the owner hart. Upon noticing the PAGED status in its loop's dequeue, the hart re-reads the actor's chunk before switching it in.

```sol
// Conceptual representation of the wake path logic
func page_in_trigger(sender: Sender, actor: Actor) -> Void {
  // Sender CAS triggers the wake
  if CAS(actor.status, BLOCKED, READY) == BLOCKED {
    // Ships to owner hart
    send_wake(actor.owner_hart, actor)
  }
}

// Hart loop dequeue logic
func hart_dequeue() -> Actor {
  let msg = dequeue()
  if msg.status == PAGED {
    // Re-read the chunk before switching in
    let fresh_chunk = read_actor_chunk(msg.id)
    switch_in_actor(fresh_chunk)
  }
}
```

