DATA is the bounded, append-only region where records are added without overwriting existing entries, while SWAP is a circular region reserved for overwriteable actor paging data that wraps around after reaching its end. For instance, an append operation past the DATA limit returns an error, whereas SWAP allows continuous storage by cycling through its pages.

```sol
// Example illustrating the difference in append behavior
dataEnd = QLOG.getDataEnd()
if QLOG.append(dataEnd, payload) == Err {
  // Fails because DATA is append-only and full
}

// SWAP allows continuous writes by wrapping
swapCursor = QLOG.getSwapCursor()
QLOG.appendSwap(swapCursor, payload) // Automatically wraps to oldest page
```

