The `loop` function returns `Unit` (void) because it enters an infinite recursive call to itself without an explicit return statement. When `irq` is 0 and `owners` is not empty, `receiveNow` failing triggers `OS.poll` to wake up waiters, followed by a sleep. On the next iteration, if `receiveNow` still fails, the function simply re-enters the loop with an exponentially increasing wait time (capped at 5000 microseconds) until `receiveNow` eventually succeeds or the `owners` map becomes empty.

