```

The file `fprisc/sol/examples/plotdemo.sol` serves as a self-contained SVG/SMIL plotting backend that generates interactive visualizations of physics simulations using only pure arithmetic and Euler-Cromer integrators. It defines three distinct simulation functions—`spring` for damped oscillations, `gd` for gradient descent on a paraboloid, and an implicit two-body orbit model—each producing time-series data or trajectory points that are rendered as static charts or animated sequences via the `lib/plot` library. The code demonstrates that complex graphical output, including animated morphs and hoverable markers, can be achieved without trigonometric functions by relying solely on rational bump functions and iterative numerical integration.

```sol
