The `apply` method parses incoming JSON data representing system statistics and dynamically updates the internal state of the `View` object. If the JSON contains a static snapshot under the key `"s"`, it replaces the stored static and dynamic lists while incrementing a full-data counter. If the JSON contains only dynamic updates under the key `"d"`, it overwrites specific integer-indexed entries in the dynamic dictionary and increments a delta counter. This approach allows the `View` to maintain both a complete history of snapshots and a current state of real-time fluctuations.

```python
