The `train` function leverages the LOOP-INVARIANT property of input rows by extracting them once into a separate matrix variable (e.g., `xaug`) before the training loop begins. This avoids the computational overhead of re-walking the matrix structure during every epoch. Developers can further optimize memory management by freeing unused intermediate data structures, such as `M.free xaug2`, after the training process completes.

