while (Os.watchClose(handle) == False) {
    yield();
}
// Proceed with Poller.stop to handle client cancellation and IRQ unbinding
Poller.stop(poller);
```

When `Os.watchClose` returns False, the watcher slot is not yet free; the caller must yield and retry until it returns True to release the slot and allow the detached worker to exit. Abandoned handles are not automatically collected, so a released handle must never be reused, similar to a closed Unix descriptor.

```sol
loop {
    if Os.watchClose(handle) {
        // Slot released, handle can be discarded
        break
    }
    // Yield here to allow teardown to complete
    yield()
}
```

