If an actor is already admitted (in the run queue) and a stale wake-up message causes it to be re-added to the backlog, the system can create a deadlock where the actor points to itself, causing the hart to spin infinitely in the dequeue loop. This occurs because the guard preventing re-queuing of admitted actors fails to detect the stale push.

