_ = drop r;
_ = case who == me of True -> 0 | False -> error "fanin: reply addressed to another client";
```

In the FP-RISC runtime, when multiple senders transmit to a shared hub beyond the dedicated per-sender channels, the overflow ring must preserve the original recipient address. Each client must use `receiveFrom` to target the specific hub and verify that the `who` field in the received `Reply` matches its own identity. If the reply is addressed to a different client, the system must raise an error to maintain correctness.

```fprisc
client hub boss me = clLoop hub boss me 0.
clLoop hub boss me k | k >= 1500 = _ = send boss (Done me); k.
clLoop hub boss me k =
  _ = send hub (Ask me k);
  r = receiveFrom me hub;
  Reply who k2 = r;
  _ = drop r;
  _ = case who == me of True -> 0 | False -> error "fanin: reply addressed to another client";
  _ = case k2 == k of True -> 0 | False -> error "fanin: reply out of order";
  _ = case k % 97 == 0 of True -> yield me | False -> 0;
