To detect a torn write, you first set the `Torn` metadata flag on the disk using `QL.sbW` with the `mTorn` accessor on the current disk head. You then call `QL.ensure` to trigger the commit process, which will roll back the transaction if the flag is set. You can verify the rollback by checking if the resulting head position is the same as before the ensure call; if it is, the operation was rolled back.
```sol
_ = QL.sbW dsk (mTorn (QL.metaOr dsk h7));
hT = QL.ensure dsk;
tornOk = case hT == h7 of
           True -> mCommit (QL.metaOr dsk h7) == 1
         | False -> False;
```

