The formula fails because dividing by zero occurs when `y2` equals `y1`, which is a valid case handled by `padB` to ensure non-zero spans. The correction replaces the division with a conditional check: if the span is zero, the result defaults to the baseline `pB`; otherwise, it calculates the linear interpolation using the standard slope formula.

```sol
sy bx v = (x1, x2, y1, y2) = bx;
  case y2 - y1 == 0 of
    True -> pB;
    False -> pB - (v - y1) * (pB - pT) / (y2 - y1);
