```

The current implementation incorrectly uses the initial map `m` for the `receive` and `step` operations but fails to update the local variable `m` with the new state `m2` before the recursive call. This causes the loop to repeatedly process the same stale state, ignoring all subsequent writes. The fix is to assign `m2` back to `m` before recursing.

Corrected code:
```fprisc
serveLog self path m =
  msg = receive self;
  (rt, q) = msg;
  (m2, r) = step path m q;
  _ = (if rt == 0 then (case r of Failed why -> _ = Sys.stderr "kvlog: {path}: a posted write failed: {why}\n"; Unit | _ -> Unit)
       else _ = send rt r; Unit);
  _ = drop msg;
