q = QS.boot me;
Qsys sys st vfs log apps = q;
```

Upon booting, the `QS.boot` function spawns the registry, storage, log, file system, and virtual file system, then reads the `apps/index` file. It attaches every application file named in the manifest (identified by the manifest's identity) located in the `apps/` directory, skipping any files where attachment fails. The system reports the set of attached application IDs, which are derived from the disk manifests rather than any hardcoded lists within the image; adding a new `.qa` file to the disk and rebooting will cause it to appear with zero shell changes.

```fpr
main =
