To calculate the slack for Grow children, use the `grownSlack` function, which takes the container axis (`a`), the container size (`m`), the children list (`kids`), and the padding (`p`). The function computes the available space, subtracts the space used by the children and their gaps, and divides the remainder by the count of Grow children.

```fpr
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

question:
