The `runQuery` function initializes a heap vector `hp` and a trace vector `tr`, then uses `allocVars` to allocate variables for the goal positions before converting the goal list into memory addresses via `instArgs`. After solving the goals with `solveG`, the function retrieves the updated memory state and explicitly frees the allocated heap and trace vectors using `Vec.free` to prevent leaks before returning the reversed solution list and remaining fuel.

```sol
hp = Vec.new Unit;
tr = Vec.new Unit;
m0 = (hp, 1, 0, tr, 1, 0);
m1 = allocVars nqv m0;
...
(m3, fuelLeft, sols) = solveG db syms m2 gaddrs fuel qpairs [];
...
