If an actor waits while holding a core, it blocks the hart's execution; the new `Sys.sleepUs` mechanism prevents this by parking the sleep on the hart's sleeper list so the actor never holds a core, whereas the old `nanosleep` approach caused every actor sharing that hart to wait out the sleep.

```fprisc
// Old approach: actor holding core blocks hart
actor wait_old() {
    lock L;
    L.acquire();
    nanosleep(1000); // Blocks hart
    L.release();
}

// New approach: actor yields hart immediately
actor wait_new() {
    lock L;
    L.acquire();
    Sys.sleepUs(1000); // Parks sleep, hart continues
    L.release();
}
```

