Deferred processes utilize an at-least-once delivery model, meaning they may be re-executed if a crash occurs between the process's external effect and the durable done marker recorded in the journal. In contrast, exactly-once delivery guarantees a process runs precisely once, even after a crash. To safely handle the at-least-once model, wrappers must use idempotent operations or guards like compare-and-swap.

