When annotating a module, the AST hash changes, causing a mismatch between the pinned hash on disk and the new hash in the source. The system automatically repins the module by replacing the old hash with the new one in all affected `.fpr` files. This process repeats until no further mismatches occur or the iteration cap is reached.
```python
