poller p = create_poller();
wait(p, event); // First waiter
stop(p);        // Poller shutdown
wait(p, event); // Duplicate waiter while in shutdown state
// The above sequence causes the poller to malfunction upon reuse
```

The `poller_stop` function handles poller shutdown by managing repeated reuse scenarios, filtering out duplicate waiters, and performing fallback cancellation if necessary. In Sol, this is implemented by checking the poller state before stopping and ensuring no new waiters are queued during the shutdown sequence.

```sol
function poller_stop() {
    if (poller_active()) {
        cancel_all_waiters();
        poller_shutdown();
    }
}
```

