The file `fprisc/tests/pingpong.fpr` serves as a functional test for the FP-RISC operating system's message passing and concurrency mechanisms, specifically verifying round-trip communication between a main thread and spawned processes. It demonstrates the creation of a `replier` process, a `poller` that waits for messages on a specific core, and a `spammer` that sends messages to the replier on another core, while the main thread receives and drops the responses to confirm successful delivery. The test concludes by printing a success message once a specified number of round trips are completed.

```fprisc
main =
  me = myself 0;
  rep = spawn replier;
  pol = spawnOn 1 (poller rep me);
  spm = spawnOn (Sys.harts Unit - 1) (spammer rep);
  r = receiveFrom me pol;
  Reply k = r;
  _ = drop r;
  "pingpong: ok after {k} round trips".
```

