```

If the `ping` function receives a reply other than `TOkI n`, it executes the `error` branch and returns the string literal "timer ping: protocol reply mismatch". This occurs when the `receiveFrom` call yields a result `o` that fails the case match, indicating a protocol violation in the CLINT bridge communication.

```fprisc
ping svc =
  me = myself 0;
  _ = send svc (me, TPing);
  r = receiveFrom me svc;
  case r of
    TOkI n -> n
  | o -> error "timer ping: protocol reply mismatch".
```

The `ping` function serves as a liveness probe that verifies whether the hardware CLINT bridge is operational. It achieves this by sending a `TPing` message to itself via the service and then checking the response; if the reply matches the expected `TOkI` format, it returns the associated integer value, otherwise it raises an error.

```fpr
ping svc =
  me = myself 0;
  _ = send svc (me, TPing);
  r = receiveFrom me svc;
  case r of
    TOkI n -> n
  | o -> error "timer ping: protocol reply mismatch".
```

The `ping` function acts as a liveness probe that returns `1` if the hardware CLINT bridge is active and `0` otherwise. It achieves this by first identifying the current service instance, sending a `TPing` message to that service, and then receiving the response. If the received reply matches the expected protocol state (`TOkI`), the function extracts and returns the associated integer value; any mismatch triggers an error.

```sol
ping svc =
  me = myself 0;
  _ = send svc (me, TPing);
  r = receiveFrom me svc;
  case r of
    TOkI n -> n
  | o -> error "timer ping: protocol reply mismatch".
```

The file `fprisc/tests/procdefer.sol` demonstrates the usage of the `Proc.afterCommit` function to execute a process only after a transaction is successfully committed. It specifically illustrates how to defer a shell command that increments a counter file, ensuring the operation occurs exactly once after validation succeeds rather than on every script attempt, which is controlled by setting the `SOL_FORCE_RETRY=1` environment variable to discard the initial plan.

> u = Proc.afterCommit (ProcessSpec ["/bin/sh", "-c", "printf x >> /tmp/sol-proc-defer.count"] "" [] "" 2000);
