Waiting never blocks a hart; instead, socket primitives are non-blocking and return `"again"`. If a `std/stream` operation fails to complete immediately, it places the associated ACTOR to sleep with a backing-off delay (starting at 0.1 ms and increasing up to 4 ms) before retrying. This mechanism ensures that a hart remains responsive and does not stall indefinitely, even when waiting for I/O.

```sol
// Example of a non-blocking socket operation that returns "again"
// and triggers the actor to sleep and retry.
socket_read() returns "again" -> actor_sleep(0.1ms) -> retry
```

The file `fprisc/tests/vecedge.fpr` serves as a test case for verifying the behavior of vector operations on an initially empty vector. It specifically validates that `Vec.map`, `Vec.fold`, and `Vec.filter` correctly handle a never-pushed vector by ensuring that mapping an empty vector yields an empty result, folding an empty vector with an accumulator of zero returns that zero, and filtering an empty vector produces a vector of length zero. The test confirms this by asserting that the sum of the folded result and the length of the filtered result equals zero.

```fprisc
m1 = Vec.map f1 (Vec.new Unit);
(ms, m2) = Vec.fold (fn a x -> a + x) 0 m1;
m3 = Vec.filter (fn x -> x > 0) m2;
(mn, m4) = Vec.len m3;
u18 = verdict "empty-map-fold-filter" (ms + mn == 0);
```

To verify this, create an empty vector using `Vec.new`, apply `Vec.map`, `Vec.fold`, and `Vec.filter` sequentially, and check that the resulting length is zero and the fold sum is zero. The following Sol code demonstrates this verification:

```sol
m1 = Vec.map f1 (Vec.new Unit);
(ms, m2) = Vec.fold (fn a x -> a + x) 0 m1;
m3 = Vec.filter (fn x -> x > 0) m2;
mn = Vec.len m3;
u18 = verdict "empty-map-fold-filter" (ms + mn == 0);
```

The `Vec.len` function returns the number of elements currently contained within a vector. In the test case, it is used to calculate the final length of the empty vector `m3` after filtering, which is expected to be zero. This value is then compared against the sum of intermediate results to verify that operations on an empty vector yield zero.

```fprisc
(mn, m4) = Vec.len m3;
u18 = verdict "empty-map-fold-filter" (ms + mn == 0);
```

