Including a span field in every constructor provides the best precision but incurs high overhead by touching every pattern match in every pass. The current approach uses statement granularity via wrappers to reach most of the value for a fraction of the churn, while allowing the span to widen later if it earns it.

```fprisc
wrapper {
  span: (file, line)
}
```

