  // Wrapper logic applies here without needing a span field in the constructor
  print "Positive";
}
```

A span field was omitted from every constructor to avoid the performance cost of touching every pattern match simultaneously; instead, statement granularity is achieved via a wrapper that covers most value for a fraction of the churn, with potential widening later. The LSP tie-in utilizes the `Name -> (file, line)` anchor map combined with check-only runs to provide diagnostics, which is designed to be the first day of an LSP diagnostics provider implementation.

```sol
