  x: 1,
  y: 2
}
```

Using a span field in every constructor provides the best precision but incurs significant overhead because it touches every pattern match across all passes simultaneously. Conversely, statement granularity via a wrapper achieves most of the value for a fraction of the churn initially, though it may widen later if it proves necessary.

