Certified termination guarantees provide either a closed-form Worst-Case Execution Time (WCET) via a certified measure or rely on the proven foldRange/Fold recursion scheme. In contrast, unproven obligations do not receive such static guarantees; instead, they are subject to dynamic checks executed exactly at the sites where the proof obligation fails.

```sol
// Example of a function with a dynamic check obligation
// The termination proof is not certified, so a dynamic check occurs at the loop site.
func loop_check(n : Int) : Int
  pre_f : (n : Int | n > 0)
  post_f : (r : Int | r >= 1)
{
  r := 1;
  while (n > 0) {
    // Dynamic check occurs here if the loop invariant/termination is not proven
    if (false) { 
      // This site would trigger a dynamic check if the obligation is unproven
      r := r + 1;
      n := n - 1;
    }
  }
  return r;
}
```

