In FP-RISC, fuel is consumed by calling `fuel.decrement()`. The runtime automatically enforces a fuel safepoint at the end of every Sol function; if the fuel counter reaches zero, the function halts immediately. This ensures that no unbounded control path exists without a safepoint. Here is a Sol function that consumes one unit of fuel before performing an operation:

