The `/actorchunks` partition is a reserved area on the log used to store chunks of an actor's stack and heap when the runtime is under memory pressure. When an actor yields or becomes blocked, its memory is copied out to this partition to allow the system to reclaim the original memory, with the design ensuring the runtime work has a clear target for this paging operation.

```fpr
// Example: A simplified representation of moving an actor's memory to a chunk
actor moveToDiskChunks(actorId) {
    // Identify the actor to be moved
    let actor = getActor(actorId);

    // Copy stack and heap to the reserved partition
    let chunk = copyMemory(actor.stack, actor.heap, "/actorchunks");

    // Reclaim original memory
    freeMemory(actor.stack, actor.heap);

    // Update the actor to point to the new chunk
    setActorMemory(actorId, chunk);
}
```

When an actor yields or is blocked under memory pressure, its stack and heap are copied out as a single chunk to a reserved partition of the log mounted at `/actorchunks`, after which the memory is reclaimed. This mechanism relies on the `URActors` managing files via the VFS with a non-blocking forward discipline; specifically, the original `replyTo` travels with the message while the storage front never blocks, ensuring the operation completes without halting the system.

```fprisc
actor myActor {
  let buffer = createBuffer(1024);
  yield; // Triggers potential chunking to /actorchunks
  // Storage front processes asynchronously without blocking
}
```

