Unlike standard arrays where growth often involves copying the entire dataset, `Vec` uses a single contiguous span per column that grows by reallocating by doubling via `fpr_realloc`. This design ensures that push operations are amortized O(1) and that the cost of copying during growth is attributed to the specific push that triggered it, maintaining WCET compositional guarantees. Indexing is performed simply as base plus index, allowing consumers like specialized loops or GPU uploads to stride one span without directory hops or per-block re-entry.

```sol
