The standard deviation is computed by first calculating the sum of the input values to derive the mean (mu), then folding the squared deviations from this mean to get the sum of squares (sq). The variance is obtained by dividing the sum of squares by the count (n), and the standard deviation (sd) is the square root of this variance.

```sol
(s0, raw1) = Vec.fold plus 0 raw;
mu = s0 / n;
(sq, raw2) = Vec.fold (sqDev mu) 0 raw1;
sd = Num.sqrt (sq / n);
```

