Enabling this configuration prevents the performance penalty associated with Transparent Huge Pages (THP) during memory allocation. When THP is set to `always`, every page reset in a pool causes the OS to fault in 2 MiB of zeroed pages, increasing build costs by 27%. Setting it to `madvise` aligns the behavior with standard Linux defaults, eliminating this specific overhead.

