reset my_pool; // Triggers 27% cost if THP is always enabled
```

Transparent Huge Pages significantly impact memory allocation, causing a 27% cost increase during pool resets where pages are faulted in again and zeroed at 2 MiB per fault. However, THP has no measurable difference on cross-hart wake and short sleep operations, where pingpong performance remains slower on Linux compared to macOS or FreeBSD regardless of THP settings.

```sol
