The `advance` function updates the animation state by adding a duration `dt` to the current time `t`. If the animation is not done and the new time `t2` is greater than or equal to half the duration of the current kind (for kinds 1, 2, or 3), it triggers a midpoint rule by resolving the attack or spending resources, then continues the animation with the updated time. If the animation is done or the new time exceeds the full duration (with kind 4 having zero duration), the animation finishes.

```sol
advance m dt =
  An kind s fz fc tz tc t done = m.anim;
  t2 = t + dt;
  m1 = case done == 0 and t2 >= durOf kind / 2 of
    True -> { (midpoint m kind s fz fc tz tc) | anim = An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 1, snap = m.snap + m.auto * bi (kind < 4) }
  | False -> { m | anim = An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 done };
  case t2 >= (case kind == 4 of True -> 0 | False -> durOf kind) of
    True -> finishAn m1 kind s fz fc tz tc
  | False -> m1.
```

