The previous harness cleanup relied on a `finally` block that failed to execute if the harness itself was killed by a sweep timeout or user interruption, leaving server ports in use. The updated implementation places the server in its own process group, ensuring cleanup occurs on SIGTERM, SIGINT, SIGHUP, and exit, while also sweeping a pidfile on startup to handle cases where standard signals are missed.

