The file `fprisc/examples/service.fpr` defines a functional service implementation in FP-RISC that listens on a local TCP port and handles HTTP requests. It logs every request with its method, path, status code, and body length, escalating to a warning level if the response status is 400 or higher. The service spawns an actor to manage routing logic and terminates gracefully when stopped, printing a readiness message and a final summary of active keys and acceptance status.

