  s = secsOf (svcClock caps);
  mm = s / 60;
  ss = s - mm * 60;
  strcat (strcat (pad2 mm) ":") (pad2 ss).
```

The `clockStr` function formats the current time into a "mm:ss" string by first retrieving the elapsed time in ticks from the CLINT mtime using `svcClock`, converting that value to seconds, and then calculating minutes and remaining seconds. It utilizes a helper function `pad2` to ensure both minute and second values are zero-padded to two digits before concatenating them with a colon.

```fprisc
