}
```

The file `qos/programs/voxel-interactive.fpr` defines an interactive application for a voxel-based 3D world, implemented in the FP-RISC language. Its primary function is to initialize a world structure, bake lighting information, and launch a continuous rendering loop that processes user input to navigate the voxel environment. The program sets up a framebuffer at full capacity, registers a device for interaction, and enters a `driver` loop that increments a frame counter and executes rendering logic for each iteration until terminated.

