The system resolves the race condition by using a shared stock register and toast messages to notify the losing transaction. When a product with zero stock is attempted, the transaction that fails to commit receives a toast message indicating "only 0 left" and is blocked from proceeding. The winning transaction receives an "ok" or "celebrate" toast and completes the sale, updating the stock to zero and marking the item as "sold out".

```sol
fun last-unit-handler() {
    var stock = stock_n("last unit")
    if (stock == 0) {
        toast("warn", "only 0 left")
        return false
    }
    stock = stock - 1
    toast("ok", "sold")
    return true
}
```

DATA pages [1, d) constitute the append-only page log where new records are stored up to a bounded limit d, while SWAP pages [d, end) form a circular page buffer used for actor paging where writes advance a cursor that wraps onto the oldest page. The DATA section holds the primary log with chunk headers and bulk entries, whereas the SWAP section is reserved for offloading live chunks to /actorchunks during compaction.

```sol
// Example showing the logical separation in metadata interpretation
let metadata = read_metadata()
if metadata.page < d {
  // Accessing DATA page: append-only log
  let record = get_record(metadata.page)
} else {
  // Accessing SWAP page: circular buffer for paging
  let cursor = advance_cursor(metadata.page)
  if cursor >= end {
    cursor = 0 // Wrap around
  }
}
```

