The file `fprisc/std/live.fpr` defines the `live` module, which implements a watch-and-rebuild system for automatically reloading programs when source files change. It utilizes the `stamps` function to monitor file modification times and sizes, and the `watcher` function to trigger a rebuild via the `P.run` function whenever a change is detected. If the rebuild succeeds, the system sends a `Reload` signal; if it fails, it logs the error and continues serving the old program.

```fprisc
watcher reg cfg seen self =
  _ = Sys.sleepUs 300000;
  now = stamps cfg.watch;
  (if now == seen then watcher reg cfg seen self
   else
     _ = Sys.stderr "live: a source changed; rebuilding\n";
     (case P.run cfg.rebuild of
         Ok r -> (if r.status == 0 then _ = A.sendSure self reg (0, Reload); Unit
                  else _ = Sys.stderr "live: the rebuild FAILED; still serving the old program\n{r.out}{r.err}\n"; watcher reg cfg now self)
       | Err why -> _ = Sys.stderr "live: cannot run the rebuild: {why}\n"; watcher reg cfg now self)).
```

