A supercombinator is a generated function that includes a specific fuel exhaustion check at its entry point. Upon execution, it decrements the hart's fuel counter (`0(tp)`), and if the result is non-positive, it immediately calls the `fpr_fuel_exhausted` function. This design ensures that after lambda lifting, all loops become tail calls to top-level supercombinators, meaning every loop iteration passes through this entry check, including allocation-free busy spins.

```fpr
// Pseudo-example of a supercombinator entry check
fun supercomb(x) {
  if (0(tp) <= 0) {
    call fpr_fuel_exhausted
  } else {
    // Function body executes
    return x
  }
}
```

The system will exhaust fuel incorrectly because the accounting model decrements fuel only once per kernel invocation, not per element processed. A `Vec.map` over n elements should cost exactly one fuel unit, but invoking the kernel repeatedly per element causes an underestimation of resource consumption, leading to premature exhaustion and an immediate call to `fpr_fuel_exhausted`. This triggers a single path off the hart: the fuel counter is preempted, refilled to FUEL_QUANTUM, and the hart yields via the standard descheduling mechanism.

```fpr
// Incorrect: Invoking kernel per element (n invocations for n elements)
// This will exhaust fuel prematurely despite doing O(n) work.
let x = Vec.map vec_add [1..n] kernel

// Correct: Invoking kernel once for the whole vector
// This costs exactly one fuel unit regardless of n.
let y = Vec.map vec_add [1..n] kernel
```

To configure the UART, you must first ensure the caller is the device owner, then set the divisor latch to enable 8N1 mode, write the calculated divisor to the lower and upper latches, and finally reset the divisor latch to restore 8N1 settings while disabling interrupts.

```sol
configUart me st from d =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  case owner == from of
    False -> reply me from (UErr "not the owner") st
  | True -> {
      _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 131;  -- Enable DLAB
      _ = write (reg8 dev 0) (band d 255);
      _ = write (reg8 dev 1) (BITSHIFTR d 8);
      _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 3;     -- Disable DLAB, 8N1
      reply me from UOk st
    }
```

