The `amoswap.d.aqrl` instruction performs an atomic exchange on naturally aligned eight-byte locations in ordinary RAM, combining an acquire read and a release write. You must ensure the target address is aligned to 8 bytes; otherwise, the operation is undefined.

```sol
// Example: Atomic exchange on a naturally aligned 8-byte location
