Phase 2 implements a contiguous vector on reallocation by performing an in-place grow via buddy-absorb, an in-place shrink, or a copy fallback, rather than relying on a fixed-size helper. This approach coalesces memory blocks intact after randomized rounds, ensuring the full qosp-reachable golden set remains byte-identical. In contrast to the previous method which likely involved separate allocation and copying, this mechanism attempts to reuse existing memory space first, minimizing data movement.

```sol
// Conceptual example of the in-place grow via buddy-absorb mechanism
// This is illustrative of the logic described in the plan, not a direct copy of the landing commit.
void* fpr_realloc_contiguous(void* ptr, size_t new_size) {
    // Attempt in-place grow via buddy-absorb
    if (can_grow_in_place(ptr, new_size)) {
        absorb_buddy_block(ptr, new_size);
        return ptr;
    }
    // Fallback to copy if contiguous growth is not possible
    return copy_fallback(ptr, new_size);
}
