```

The `buddy_realloc` mechanism replaces the previous pool-based initialization with a unified in-place reallocation strategy that handles growth via buddy-absorb, shrinkage via in-place reduction, and fallback to copying when necessary, while preserving coalescing integrity after extensive randomization. In contrast, `fpr_pool_init` was a foundational fix specifically addressing the Sys.arena uninitialized-bigfree bug by routing all five pool creation sites through a single initialization function, ensuring proper arena setup rather than managing dynamic block resizing.

```fprisc
// Example of the new in-place shrink/grow logic concept
void* buddy_absorb(void* block, size_t new_size) {
    // Attempt to coalesce with adjacent blocks to grow in-place
    if (can_coalesce(block, new_size)) {
        return absorb(block, new_size);
    }
    // Fallback to copy if coalescing fails
    return copy_fallback(block, new_size);
}
```

The error is an uninitialized bigfree bug within the system arena. This occurs because `fpr_pool_init` is the required centralization point for all five pool creation sites; bypassing it leaves the pool's internal state, specifically the bigfree mechanism, in an undefined or uninitialized state.

```fprisc
