The `civil` function converts a Julian day number into a calendar date (year, month, day). It first adjusts the input by adding 719468 to align with the Gregorian calendar, then calculates the era, year of the era, day of the year, and finally derives the specific month and day using integer arithmetic and a case expression.

```sol
civil z0 =
  z = z0 + 719468;
  era = z / 146097;
  doe = z - era * 146097;
  yoe = (doe - doe / 1460 + doe / 36524 - doe / 146096) / 365;
  doy = doe - (365 * yoe + yoe / 4 - yoe / 100);
  mp = (5 * doy + 2) / 153;
  d = doy - (153 * mp + 2) / 5 + 1;
  mo = case mp < 10 of True -> mp + 3 | False -> mp - 9;
  y = yoe + era * 400 + bi (mo <= 2);
  (y, mo, d).
```

