```

The file `fprisc/std/ws.fpr` defines the functional logic for WebSocket frame parsing and masking within the FP-RISC language. It implements a protocol where the first two bytes determine the close code or frame flags, subsequent bytes specify the payload length (either 7 bits or a 14-bit big-endian integer), and the final section handles the unmasking of the payload using an XOR operation with a 4-byte key. This module enables the system to correctly interpret incoming WebSocket messages by extracting the frame type, opcode, and unmasked data while rejecting frames with reserved bits set.

```fprisc
// Example: Parsing a masked frame with a 2-byte payload
readFrame r = case ST.readExactly 2 r of (res, r2) ->
  (case res of
      Err why -> (Err why, r2)
    | Ok h ->
        b0 = charAt h 1;
        b1 = charAt h 2;
        (if band b0 112 != 0 then (Err "reserved bits set", r2)
         else lengthThen (band b0 128 != 0) (band b0 15) (band b1 128 != 0) (band b1 127) r2))
```

