The `GFX=1` flag enables the compilation of the raw graphics core (specifically `runtime/posix/gfx.c`) into the host image, allowing applications to access low-level graphics operations like scene-value walking and FBO readback directly. When this flag is set, the host fills the nullable `gfx` entries in the `qos_hal_t` table with implementations for functions such as `gfx_render`, whereas a host built without it leaves these entries NULL and reports the missing capability to the application.

```fpr
// Example showing the difference in capability detection
if (gfx_render != null) {
    // Host with GFX=1: Can render directly
    gfx_render(scene_value, output_value);
} else {
    // Host without GFX=1: Must use stubs or alternative path
    error("Missing GFX capability");
}
