When `GFX=1`, the `gfx_render` function receives the application's scene VALUE and the host walks it read-only through the shared address space layout. All value construction for drawing results and inputs occurs on the application side using its own allocator, ensuring no memory allocation crosses the boundary between the raw host core and the application.

```sol
; Example Sol function demonstrating read-only scene access
