```fpr
(gfx_render scene_value host_ptr) -> (draws dynBytes) {
    // Host walks scene_value read-only via shared fpr.h layout
    // App constructs draws and dynBytes using its own allocator
}
```

The function `leadSlack` calculates the extra space available along the leading axis of a row or column of child entities when they do not grow to fill the container. It first sums the widths (or heights) of all children and the gaps between them to determine `used` space, then subtracts this from the total `avail` space (container size minus padding). If any children are configured to grow (`countGrow > 0`), it returns 0; otherwise, it returns half of the remaining space.

```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

The `leadSlack` function determines the extra space allocated to the leading edge of a row of widgets when none of them are set to grow. It calculates the available width (or height for columns) minus the total width (or height) used by the widgets and their gaps, then divides the remaining difference by two. If any widget is set to grow, the slack is zero.

```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

The `leadSlack` function calculates the horizontal or vertical space reserved at the leading edge of a container to accommodate potential growth from its children, ensuring the container can expand if needed. It first computes the total width or height of the children plus their gaps, then determines the available space within the container's bounds (accounting for padding). If any child is marked to grow, the function returns zero slack; otherwise, it returns half of the remaining unused space, using integer division to split the leftover space evenly along the axis.

```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

