Attempting to free a shared allocation triggers a panic with the message "Builtin: free of shared allocation". This check occurs immediately after verifying the address is not null and before proceeding to mark the block as unused and merge it. The code explicitly prevents this by returning an error if the read count (`Block.rc b`) is not equal to 1 (exclusive).

```fprisc
freeLive b =
  _ = case Word.eq (Block.rc b) (w 1) of True -> Unit | False -> error "Builtin: free of shared allocation";
  _ = Block.setUsed b (w 0);
  _ = merge b;
  mergePrev (Block.prev b).
```

The `free` function locates a block via `find` and calls `freeLive` if the address is not null. Inside `freeLive`, the system first checks if the block's reference count (`Block.rc`) is 1; if it is not, an error is raised indicating the allocation is shared. If the count is 1, the block's usage flag is set to 0, and the block is merged with its next and previous neighbors to consolidate memory.

```sol
free v = case Addr.eq v (Addr.null Unit) of
    True -> Unit
  | False -> freeLive (find v)
;
freeLive b =
  _ = case Word.eq (Block.rc b) (w 1) of True -> Unit | False -> error "Builtin: free of shared allocation";
  _ = Block.setUsed b (w 0);
  _ = merge b;
  mergePrev (Block.prev b)
;
mergePrev p = case Block.isNull p of
    True -> Unit
  | False -> mergeIfFree p
;
mergeIfFree p = case used p of True -> Unit | False -> merge p
```

The file `fprisc/std/mvu.fpr` defines the core rendering loop for the MVU (Model-View-Update) architecture within the FP-RISC operating system. It implements `renderWorker`, which manages the asynchronous request lifecycle by receiving events, calling the application's `vals` function to compute the new view state, invoking the service call mechanism, and enforcing frame boundaries via `Sys.poolReset 0`. The file also provides timing utilities like `waitTick` and `dueTick` to handle event pacing and frame synchronization without blocking cores, ensuring deterministic execution on the QOS platform.

```sol
renderWorker : unsafe Int -> Int -> env -> (Int -> env -> (Int, Int) -> model -> vals) -> Int -> c .
renderWorker parent render env vl self =
  m = receiveFrom self parent;
  Rq st model vw vh sc fr = m;
  vs = vl self env (vw, vh) model;
  r = svcCall self render (Render st vs sc fr);
  _ = send parent r;
  _ = drop r;
  _ = drop m;
  _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
  renderWorker parent render env vl self.
```

