The system enforces a 24-character limit on user names, ensuring that multi-byte UTF-8 characters are not split. Valid UTF-8 escapes are decoded to their corresponding characters, while control bytes are dropped. Surrogate pairs representing emojis are rejected and displayed as "??", and empty strings are refused without allowing login.

```sol
fn validate_name(name: String) -> Result {
    // Decode UTF-8 escapes for BMP, drop control bytes, cap at 24 chars
    let cleaned = name.map(|c| {
        if c.is_control() { None }
        else if c.is_surrogate_pair() { None }
        else if c.is_utf8_escape() { decode_utf8_escape(c) }
        else { Some(c) }
    }).filter_map(|opt| opt).collect();

    if cleaned.len() > 24 {
        return Err("Name too long");
    }

    if cleaned.is_empty() {
        return Err("Name cannot be empty");
    }

    Ok(cleaned)
}
```

