If the task notification park is disabled because condition variables are measured as faster on the board, `task_notify` will bypass the traditional park/wake mechanism. The merge explicitly preserves this park unless the condition variables prove superior; therefore, if they are not used, the standard task notification path remains active. Attempting to use a mechanism that relies on the park when it is absent would cause the task to hang indefinitely waiting for a signal that will never arrive, as the runtime lacks the necessary synchronization primitive.

```sol
