  print "wrote {n + 1}".
}
```

When multiple transactions run concurrently on a shared counter, the transaction that writes the final value may overwrite a previous write if it does not detect the race condition. To prevent this, the loser of the race must retry the operation. This is implemented by reading the current value, incrementing it, and writing the new value back, ensuring the counter reflects the highest value written so far.

```sol
n = parseInt (readPath @/tmp/sol-txn-race.txt);
u = sleepMs 300;
