```

When a deferred command fails, the transaction half-commits, but the system ensures atomicity by not claiming full success in the receipt. The journal is cleared to prevent applying effects from a failed transaction, and the summary explicitly reports that the operation was "NOT atomic" due to the failure of the deferred command.

