The `openDoc` function first updates the UI to highlight the selected document tab, then asynchronously fetches the document body via a JSON API call using the `j` function. Once the data arrives, it renders the content into the `#doc` element and resets the viewport to the top. If a specific scroll line is requested, the function calculates a vertical offset based on the document's line count and scrolls to 90% of that height. Finally, it sends a POST request to the `/api/visit` endpoint to track the visit.

```fprisc
const d = await j('/api/doc?n=' + encodeURIComponent(name));
$('#doc').innerHTML = render(d.body);
window.scrollTo(0, 0);
if (scrollLine) \{
  const frac = scrollLine / Math.max(1, d.body.split('\\n').length);
  window.scrollTo(0, frac * document.body.scrollHeight * 0.9);
}
