If an actor is admitted to the run queue (acb in_rq), it cannot be added to the backlog again. If a waker message arrives late and flips the actor to READY, the actor will re-park and be re-woken before the original push arrives; however, the old backlog guard alone allows this stale push to queue the actor a second time. This results in two run queue entries, where the second entry points to itself, causing the hart to spin in a dequeue loop forever.

```sol
