```sol
// Example illustrating the state check
if (acb.in_rq) {
    // Actor is admitted and in the run queue; do not add to backlog
    // The guard alone prevents re-queuing stale pushes
}
```

This rule prevents infinite loops caused by stale wake messages. If a waker's message arrives late after an actor has already been marked READY and is in the run queue, the actor might re-park and be re-woken before the original push arrives. Without this guard, the stale push could queue a second entry pointing to itself, causing the hart to spin in the dequeue loop forever. The guard ensures that only one run queue entry exists for any admitted actor.

```sol
// Conceptual logic for the admission check
if (acb.in_rq) {
    // Do not add to backlog; actor is already admitted
    return; 
}
```

