`send` deep-copies a message into a new ownerless slab, ensuring no shared references or dangling pointers exist. `sendLinear` transfers ownership directly via a move operation, changing the reference count without copying the data, which enables zero-copy relay chains. `sendArc` shares the object by incrementing the holder count for each receiver, freezing the object under contract to prevent linear bulk moves or copies.

