The code incorrectly assumes the buffer contains data before retrieving it, which will cause a runtime error when the peer disconnects and sends an empty string. The fix requires checking if the accumulated request string is empty before attempting to route it, effectively treating an empty read as a disconnection. The corrected logic should be:

```fprisc
srvBytes mt cfg app sv cid "" =
  Sv model sess nsid ltt bufs = sv;
  srvLoop mt cfg app (Sv model sess nsid ltt (bufDel bufs cid));

srvBytes mt cfg app sv cid bytes =
  Sv model sess nsid ltt bufs = sv;
  req = strcat (bufGet bufs cid) bytes;
  if (req == "") then
    srvLoop mt cfg app (Sv model sess nsid ltt (bufDel bufs cid))
