The `walk` function first calculates the new coordinates based on the direction, then checks if an enemy exists at those coordinates. If an enemy is present, it triggers an attack by calling `endTurn (hitEnemy m1 i nx ny)`. If no enemy is present, it checks if the tile is blocked; if blocked, the move ends with a message, otherwise the entity's position is updated and the turn ends.

```fpr
walk m d =
  (dx, dy) = dxOf d;
  nx = m.px + dx;
  ny = m.py + dy;
  m1 = { m | dir = d };
  case enemyAt m1.ens nx ny of
    En i ex ey hp :: _ -> endTurn (hitEnemy m1 i nx ny)
  | Nil -> (case blocked m1 nx ny of
        True -> endTurn (say m1 "blocked")
      | False -> endTurn (arrive { m1 | px = nx, py = ny })).
```

