    return commit(line, state) // Updates model and queues for disk
```

The system relies on a single append-only log where every change to the shop is represented as a line. The only function that reads this log is `apply`, which validates the line and commits it to the model. Because the current state is constructed by folding `apply` over the entire log, restarting the process automatically rebuilds the exact same state that was active at the time of the last commit, eliminating any possibility of a second interpretation of a sale.

```fprisc
// Example of the apply function reading a log line
apply(line) {
    if (validate(line)) {
        model = apply(model, line)
        queue(line)
