When a `FPut` operation arrives, the server calculates the shard index by dividing the key by the configuration span. It retrieves or spawns the corresponding shard, performs the put operation via an asynchronous ask, and then updates the shard counts map with the new count before sending a done message.

```sol
idx = (cfg.key x) / cfg.span;
(sh, shards2) = (case M.get idx shards of
    O.Some s -> (s, shards)
  | O.None -> s = spawnShard cfg idx; (s, M.insert idx s shards));
r = A.askSure self sh (SPut x);
n = (case r of SCountIs c -> c | _ -> 0);
