When a developer opens a UART port, the system first checks if the device is already claimed by another owner; if so, it returns a "uart is claimed" error. If the device is free, the system initializes it by writing the value 3 to register 3 (setting the FIFO enable bit) and then writing 0 to register 1 (disabling interrupts) to prepare for the 8N1 configuration. This sequence ensures the FIFO is reset and interrupts are off until the `UArm` flag is set.

```fpr
_ = write (reg8 d2 3) 3;
_ = write (reg8 d2 1) 0;
