The commit protocol is genuinely crash-atomic because `writeAtomic` utilizes a redo journal with PID-stamped lock reclaim to ensure writes are either fully committed or safely aborted without disk corruption. If a panic occurs mid-script, the disk remains untouched, and deferred shell commands rely on `.done` markers to execute at-least-once rather than every crash, ensuring data integrity even if the transaction is not atomic overall when any of the five Now* realtime escapes fire.

```sol
