To verify in-place allocation for fused scalar maps, compare the heap usage before and after the operation. If the difference is less than the size of a single vector element (e.g., 4096 bytes for 4000 elements), the operation reused existing memory rather than allocating new space. This is demonstrated by checking that the heap difference is less than the vector size:

```fprisc
b1 = fillI (Vec.new Unit) 1 4000;
b2 = Vec.map scaleUp b1;
b3 = Vec.map shiftDn b2;
(s2, b4) = sumI b3;
_ = Vec.free b4;
u2 = verdict "fused-scalar-pipeline" (s2 == refI 1 4000);
