The `frameWorker` function implements the core game loop by first receiving a new frame message from the parent process, extracting the current state variables (position, keys, buttons, and camera angles), and then polling for the next 64 milliseconds of input. It calculates the next player position using the `move` function based on the polled keys, renders the updated scene via `renderFrame`, and sends the resulting frame back to the parent. The loop then resets the system pool and recursively calls itself to continue the cycle.

```fprisc
frameWorker parent self =
  message = receiveFrom self parent;
  Frame x z keys buttons yaw pitch = message;
  Input nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch =
    pollInput (Input keys buttons yaw pitch) 64;
  (nextX, nextZ) = move x z nextKeys;
  _ = renderFrame nextX nextZ nextYaw nextPitch;
  reply = Frame nextX nextZ nextKeys nextButtons nextYaw nextPitch;
  _ = send parent reply;
  _ = drop reply;
  _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
  frameWorker parent self.
```

