} catch (error: "slot occupied") {
    # Overlapping load refused
}
```

The flat image is pre-processed to contain loadable bytes at their final offsets with gaps already zero-filled, which eliminates the need for the loader to perform an ELF program-header walk. Consequently, the loader simply copies the image to the base address and zeroes the memory size fields (`imagesz` and `memsz`).
