You can extract the SHA hash by parsing the binary file to locate the LOAD section entry and reading the corresponding line that starts with "sha". The process involves verifying the file starts with the "QAR2\n" signature, partitioning the header to find the LOAD offset and size, extracting the raw bytes for that section, and parsing the decoded text for the specific hash line.

```python
with open(qa_path, "rb") as f:
    b = f.read()
if b[:5] != b"QAR2\n":
    raise SystemExit("not a QAR2 archive")
head, _, _ = b.partition(b"\n\n")
off = len(head) + 2
for line in head.decode().split("\n")[1:]:
    name, o, n = line.split()
    if name == "LOAD":
        load = b[off + int(o) : off + int(o) + int(n)].decode()
        for ln in load.split("\n"):
            if ln.startswith("sha "):
                return ln.split()[1]
```

