To switch the DC pin from command mode to data mode, you must set it to a high value (1) after completing the SPI transaction. In the provided driver, this is done by calling `pinW dc 1` immediately following the `cmd` or `dat` function, which handles the low-level SPI communication.

```fprisc
# Example: Send a command then switch to data mode
cmd pinW pinR pins miso bytes =
  Pins sck mosi cs dc = pins;
  _ = pinW dc 0;
  _ = S.csLow pinW cs;
  _ = S.xfer (S.Bus pinW pinR sck mosi miso) bytes;
  _ = S.csHigh pinW cs;
  _ = pinW dc 1;  # Switch to data mode
```

The driver uses a dedicated DC (Data/Command) pin to toggle the mode. The `cmd` function sets the DC pin to 0 before transmitting commands, while the `dat` function sets it to 1 for data transfers. This is implemented by asserting the DC pin low before calling the SPI bus transfer for commands and high for data, ensuring the SSD1306 controller interprets the subsequent bytes correctly.

```fprisc
cmd pinW pinR pins miso bytes =
  Pins sck mosi cs dc = pins;
  _ = pinW dc 0;
  _ = S.csLow pinW cs;
  _ = S.xfer (S.Bus pinW pinR sck mosi miso) bytes;
  _ = S.csHigh pinW cs;
  pinW dc 1.

dat pinW pinR pins miso bytes =
  Pins sck mosi cs dc = pins;
  _ = S.csLow pinW cs;
  _ = S.xfer (S.Bus pinW pinR sck mosi miso) bytes;
  S.csHigh pinW cs.
```

The code violates the hardware protocol because the `cmd` function incorrectly attempts to toggle the chip select (`cs`) line while the data direction (`dc`) line is still set to command mode (0). According to the `Pins` constructor definition, the `dc` pin is a separate control signal from `cs`; the `cmd` function must explicitly switch `dc` to 1 (data mode) before or after the chip select transition to ensure the SPI controller interprets the byte stream correctly. The correct sequence requires setting `dc` to 1 before the chip select is asserted low, as shown in the corrected `cmd` implementation:

```fpr
cmd pinW pinR pins miso bytes =
  Pins sck mosi cs dc = pins;
  _ = pinW dc 1;
  _ = S.csLow pinW cs;
  _ = S.xfer (S.Bus pinW pinR sck mosi miso) bytes;
  _ = S.csHigh pinW cs;
  pinW dc 1.
```

