The UV coordinate is derived by calculating the fractional position of the ray's intersection point on the voxel's six faces. These fractional coordinates are then blended based on the normal vector of the specific face being shaded. For instance, the U coordinate for the X-face (where the normal is 0, 0, 1) uses the Z-fraction, while the V coordinate for the Y-face uses the X-fraction. The resulting UV pair is used as an index into the atlas texture maps:

```fprisc
fxv = fracOf (hitPoint t1 dxv ox);
fyv = fracOf (hitPoint t2 dyv oy);
fzv = fracOf (hitPoint t3 dzv oz);
uu = Vec.sar 12 (Vec.blend (Vec.eqS 0 ax1) fzv fx1);
vv = Vec.sar 12 (Vec.blend (Vec.eqS 1 ax2) fx2 (Vec.axpb (0 - 1) (fx - 1) fyv));
(ti1, tir) = Vec.dup (Vec.minS (atlasN - 1) (Vec.maxS 0 Vec.zipAdd uu vv));
(tr1, ar2) = Vec.gather ti1 ar;
```

