The `dPins` function is a dispatcher that interprets a URL and a desired value type to perform operations on a specific pin. To read from a pin, the URL must contain a numeric segment at index 7 (representing the pin number) and a segment at index 8 that is not equal to "mode". When these conditions are met, `dPins` parses the pin number and calls `Pin.read` with that number, returning the result wrapped in an `IInt`.

```sol
dPins url want v =
  ns = segAfter url 7;
  n = parseNum ns;
  case strEq (segAfter url (7 + strlen ns + 1)) "mode" of
    True -> dPinMode n v
  | False -> dPinRW n want v;
```

