When the main transaction commits, the system must check the actor registry for any live spawned threads. If such actors exist, the script must either join them with a bounded timeout using the join idiom or explicitly commit and print a warning stating that the number of running actors and their effects are not part of the current commit. This prevents the silent loss of effects that occurs when committing while actors are still executing.

```sol
// Example Sol script demonstrating the join idiom and warning
runTxLoop {
  spawn actor {
    sleep 200 ms
    writePaths ["/tmp/test.txt"]
  }
  commit
  // If the spawned actor is still live, the system will warn:
  // "N actor(s) still running — their effects are NOT part of this commit"
}
```

If a main process commits a transaction while a spawned actor is still running, the actor's effects written after the commit point vanish silently, potentially causing files to disappear without a warning. To fix this, the system must check the actor registry at commit time; if any actors are still live, the main process should either join them with a named timeout or commit and explicitly print a loud warning stating that the number of still-running actors and their effects are not part of this commit.

```sol
-- Example of the join idiom to ensure actors finish before commit
actor main() {
  spawn actor worker() {
    sleep 200 ms
    writePaths ["data.txt", "hello"]
  }
  // ... other work ...
  join worker -- timeout 1 s -- name "worker"
  commit
}
```

When the main function commits, you must explicitly check the actor registry to ensure no spawned actors remain live. If live actors exist, you should either join them with a named timeout or commit the transaction while printing a warning that their effects will not be part of this commit. Relying on silent failure is incorrect; a robust implementation warns the user and logs the count of orphaned actors to prevent data loss or inconsistent state.

```sol
if (isLiveActorRegistry()) {
    joinActors(timeout: 5000)
} else if (hasLiveActors()) {
    commitTransaction()
    printWarning("N actor(s) still running — their effects are NOT part of this commit")
}
```

