The `leadSlack` function calculates the unused space along the primary axis after accounting for padding and gaps between children, dividing the remainder by two if no children are allowed to grow. It first sums the widths or heights of all children plus their gaps to determine `used` space, then compares it against the available space (`avail`) defined by the container's dimension minus double the padding. If the list of children allows growth (`countGrow > 0`), the result is zero; otherwise, it returns half the difference between available and used space.

```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

The `leadSlack` function determines the space available for growth by calculating the difference between the container's internal dimension (minus padding) and the sum of children's widths (or heights) plus their gaps. If any children are set to grow, the slack is zero; otherwise, the remaining space is divided by two.

```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

