The `fly` function computes the speed `v` using `Numeric.sqrt` on the sum of squared velocity components, then derives acceleration components `ax` and `ay` by applying the drag coefficient `cD` multiplied by the product of speed and velocity direction. This semi-implicit Euler integration updates position and velocity using these calculated accelerations over the time step `dt` until the vertical position `y` becomes negative.

```sol
fly x y vx vy | y < 0 = x.
fly x y vx vy =
  v  = Numeric.sqrt (vx * vx + vy * vy);
  ax = 0 - cD * (v * vx);
  ay = 0 - g - cD * (v * vy);
  fly (x + vx * dt) (y + vy * dt) (vx + ax * dt) (vy + ay * dt).
```

