The `std/store` actor maintains a keyed collection distributed across SHARD actors, where each shard holds a specific partition in memory and appends changes to its own file. Compaction occurs incrementally when superseded lines outnumber live ones within a single shard. The available commands are `add`, `edit`, and `delete`, which write to the store and return `Stored`, `Saved`, or `Deleted` respectively.

```fprisc
