To utilize the full memory block, set the `acb_t.stack_sz` variable to match the size of the allocated buddy block, effectively doubling the available stack space compared to the previous half-block usage. Stack overflow is detected when an actor attempts to grow past its allocated limit, triggering a panic handled by the HAL. On POSIX systems, this is caught via a fault on an alternate signal stack, resulting in an exit code of 1. Developers can register a custom fault handler by providing `fpr_current_stack` to the HAL table, allowing the host to identify the specific actor that caused the overflow.

