  }
}
```

The recommended order is to perform property-based testing first, as it is the most efficient method for checking invariants on random op sequences and runs in seconds per module. Bounded model checking should be performed second on specific modules like parsers and the buddy allocator, though it may blow up quickly. Fuzzing complements property-based testing for crash-freedom on adversarial bytes. Deductive proofs of C and formal methods like Isabelle or Coq are reserved for later stages or specific high-level concerns like the language semantics, not for low-level C implementation details.

