FP-RISC allows sequential variable assignments where each variable is computed based on the result of the immediately preceding variable within the same block. The language evaluates these statements from top to bottom, ensuring that subsequent variables utilize the updated values of their predecessors. For example, the following sequence calculates a running sum by incrementing each new variable by the value of the previous one:
```
v188 = v187 + 188;
v189 = v188 + 189;
v190 = v189 + 190;
