s.write buf; 
```

Socket primitives are non-blocking and immediately return an "again" status without blocking the hart, whereas `std/stream` puts the actor to sleep for a brief duration (backing off from 0.1 ms to 4 ms) before retrying. This distinction ensures that the hart remains responsive while allowing the stream to handle asynchronous I/O efficiently.

```sol
