Certified termination is achieved either through a closed-form Worst-Case Execution Time (WCET) proof or by using the proven foldRange/Fold recursion scheme. In contrast, unproven obligations are not statically verified for termination but instead undergo dynamic checks specifically at the sites where those obligations fail to prove termination.

```sol
// Example: A function relying on dynamic checks for an unproven obligation
