The total worst-case execution time (WCET) bound will be underestimated because the formula for T(segment) explicitly includes a term for scheduler-level latency defined as FUEL_QUANTUM multiplied by the worst instructions per fuel unit for each runnable peer. Omitting this term fails to account for the time spent waiting for other actors to finish executing their fuel units, leading to an inaccurate and non-conservative bound.

```fprc
// Incorrect calculation: summing only instruction costs and communication bounds
// Missing: scheduler-level latency (FUEL_QUANTUM * worst_instructions_per_fuel_unit * runnable_peers)
// This results in a WCET bound that is strictly less than the actual execution time.
```

