badS = case bad of Ok i -> "ACCEPTED?!" | Err e -> "refused";
```

The system returns an error instead of accepting the load. In the provided test case, attempting to load "sysbad" results in a value that is not "Ok", which is then handled by a case expression to display the string "refused". This demonstrates that invalid or missing files trigger an error condition rather than a successful load.

