The `items` function in `json.fpr` recursively parses a JSON array by iterating through characters, handling commas to separate items and stopping when a closing bracket `]` (ASCII 93) is encountered. It accumulates values in a list and reverses it upon completion. Below is the Sol implementation of this logic:

```sol
fn parseJsonArray(s: unsafe String) -> List Value {
    var acc: List Value = Nil
    var i: Int = 0
    while (charAtOr s i != 93) {
        if (charAtOr s i == 93) {
            break
        }
        if (charAtOr s i == 44) {
            i = skip s (i + 1)
            continue
        }
        let (v, i) = value s i
        acc = v :: acc
        i = skip s i
    }
    return rev acc Nil
}
```

