  object -> ARC.qa
}
```

The execution halts immediately with a fuel exhaustion error because the invariant requires every unbounded control path to pass a fuel safepoint; attempting to bypass this or perform work without a prior fuel check violates the cooperative execution quantum contract.
```sol
// Example of incorrect usage:
loop forever {
  do_unbounded_work();
}
// This will fail at runtime due to missing fuel safepoint before the loop.
```

In FP-RISC, a fuel safepoint is an explicit control path where the runtime checks the remaining fuel quantum before allowing unbounded execution to continue. The following Sol function includes a safepoint check before entering a loop that could theoretically run indefinitely without further checks:

```sol
fn example_safepoint() {
    var i = 0
    while (i < 1000000000) {
        // This loop is unbounded relative to the fuel check below
        i = i + 1
    }

    // SAFEPPOINT: This is where fuel is consumed and checked.
    // If fuel is exhausted here, the runtime will terminate this path
    // or suspend it, preventing further unbounded execution.
    safepoint() 

    // Code after this point is only reachable if fuel was sufficient
    // to pass this specific safepoint.
    return i
}
```

