A Sol function can extract the application title list and virtual file system by destructuring the `env` tuple using the `envTitles` and `envVfs` accessors. These functions pattern match on the first two elements (log and mt) to isolate the remaining tuple, which contains the titles and vfs. The resulting values are then accessible as `ts` and `vfs` respectively.

