To compute the mean and standard deviation, first sum the vector elements to get the total, then divide by the vector length to obtain the mean. Next, fold the vector with a squared deviation function using the captured mean, take the square root of the result divided by the length, and return both values.

```sol
func meanAndStdDev (v: Vec.int): (float, float) {
  n = Num.length v;
  (s0, _) = Vec.fold plus 0 v;
  mu = s0 / n;
  (sq, _) = Vec.fold (sqDev mu) 0 v;
  sd = Num.sqrt (sq / n);
  return (mu, sd);
}
```

