QOS Portable is a hosting runtime designed to run a single FP-RISC program on a host OS, whereas QOS Native is a full operating system with real hardware abstractions and per-hart schedulers. Attempting to run a QOS Portable application as QOS Native would fail because the Portable runtime relies on host OS services like libc, sockets, and files, which are not present in the freestanding environment of QOS Native. Conversely, running a QOS Native application in QOS Portable is impossible because the Portable runtime expects a single QOS-x86_64 ELF program packaged as a `.qa` archive, not a native binary requiring direct hardware access.

