The `advance` function calculates a new time `t2` and checks if the current animation kind has reached its midpoint to apply the `midpoint` rule, which may modify the animation state and snap values. If the animation duration is reached, the `finishAn` function is invoked to complete the animation, typically resetting the animation state to `noAn`.

```fpr
advance m dt =
  An kind s fz fc tz tc t done = m.anim;
  t2 = t + dt;
  m1 = case done == 0 and t2 >= durOf kind / 2 of
    True -> { (midpoint m kind s fz fc tz tc) | anim = An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 1, snap = m.snap + m.auto * bi (kind < 4) }
  | False -> { m | anim = An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 done };
  case t2 >= (case kind == 4 of True -> 0 | False -> durOf kind) of
    True -> finishAn m1 kind s fz fc tz tc
  | False -> m1.
```

