The "void twice" operation specifically targets the last-unit race condition where two registers ring the final item; exactly one commit succeeds while the other is rejected, ensuring the inventory delta reflects only one sale. A standard receipt generation follows the same commit logic for valid transactions but does not inherently handle the specific race condition of two simultaneous claims on the last unit. In FP-RISC, this logic is expressed by allowing the second attempt to fail gracefully:

```sol
def void-twice(item: sku) -> bool:
  if last-unit(item):
    if commit(item):
      return true
    else:
      return false
  else:
    return true
```

