The file `qos/programs/mods/dungeonrules.fpr` defines the core game loop and camera mechanics for a dungeon game running within the QOS operating system. It establishes a tick-based system where state updates occur every 40 milliseconds, ensuring that player input is processed one key at a time per tick to create smooth movement frames. The module also implements a critically-damped camera that smoothly follows the player by moving one-sixth of the remaining distance to the target position each tick, with coordinates clamped to the board boundaries to prevent the view from extending beyond the level.

```sol
tickMs = 40.
tick m =
  m1 = { m | ms = m.ms + tickMs };
  take (follow m1);

follow m =
  tx = clampI (m.px * cell) (camMx * cell) ((m.w - 1 - camMx) * cell);
  tz = clampI (m.py * cell) (camMzN * cell) ((m.h - 1 - camMzS) * cell);
  { m | camx = m.camx + (tx - m.camx) / 6, camz = m.camz + (tz - m.camz) / 6 };
```

The camera moves by calculating the difference between the target position and the current position, then adding one-sixth of that difference to the current coordinates. This process is repeated until the camera is clamped within the board's margins.

```sol
def camEase m =
  tx = clampI (m.px * cell) (camMx * cell) ((m.w - 1 - camMx) * cell);
  tz = clampI (m.py * cell) (camMzN * cell) ((m.h - 1 - camMzS) * cell);
  { m | camx = m.camx + (tx - m.camx) / 6, camz = m.camz + (tz - m.camz) / 6 };
```

Upon receiving a successful `Ok` result from `WS.accept`, the actor spawns a dynamic writer actor using `A.spawnWith` and retrieves a unique session ID via `A.askSure` to pin the register's slab. If the session ID is non-zero, it immediately initiates a reading process by calling `reading` with the session ID and the active connection, ensuring the session can read from the poller and write to the connection simultaneously.

```fprisc
session reg poller app conn req = case WS.accept req of
    Err why -> _ = ST.write (H.renderResponse (H.text 400 "{why}\n")) conn; Unit
  | Ok head ->
      _ = ST.write head conn;
      me = myself 0;
      writer = A.spawnWith (A.Dynamic 64) (fn self -> writerStart (protocolOf req.query) reg app conn self);
      r = A.askSure me reg (Join writer);
      sid = (case r of Welcome n _ -> n | _ -> 0);
      _ = drop r;
      (if sid == 0 then Unit else reading reg app.codec writer sid (ST.readerOn poller conn) conn A.tidySmall).
```

