               else Store.search (matches q) (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store);
  pages = (if n == 0 then 1 else (n + pageSize - 1) / pageSize);
  ...
```

The function first retrieves the relevant entries using either `Store.page` or `Store.search` based on the query string. It then calculates the total number of pages required to display all results by dividing the count by the page size, rounding up. If the requested page index exceeds the calculated total, the function recursively reloads the store with the last valid page index before returning the final data structure.

```sol
pages = (if n == 0 then 1 else (n + pageSize - 1) / pageSize);
(if v.page >= pages and v.page > 0 then load store {v | page = pages - 1}
