If `OS.watchOpen` returns an error, the function logs the reason to standard error and initiates polling on a timer instead by spawning a `waker` actor and entering a `loop` with an empty map.

```fpr
begin me = case OS.watchOpen Unit of
    Err why ->
      _ = Sys.stderr "poller: no watcher ({why}); polling on a timer instead\n";
      loop me 0 0 (M.empty Ord.int) A.tidy0 100
  | Ok irq ->
      w = spawn (fn self -> waker me irq self);
      m = receiveFrom me w;
      _ = drop m;
      loop me irq w (M.empty Ord.int) A.tidy0 100.
```

