The `shard` function receives a message from the system, extracts the sender and answer channel, calls `serveShard` to process the shard's state and return an answer, and then forwards that answer back to the sender using `A.sendSure`. After sending, it drops the message and recursively calls itself with the next shard index to continue processing.

```sol
shard self cfg st0 t0 = case A.tidy self (st0, t0) of (st, t) ->
  m = receive self;
  (from, q) = m;
  (next, ans) = serveShard cfg q st;
  _ = A.sendSure self from ans;
  _ = drop m;
  shard self cfg next t.
```

