The frameWorker updates the latency ring by writing the spawn-to-reply time from the previous frame into a specific slot of a vector handle `lv`, calculated as `(n mod latN) + 1`. It then averages these values by folding the vector with a sum function and dividing the result by the number of slots `n` and a scaling factor of 1000 to convert ticks to tenths of milliseconds.

