The `grownSlack` function calculates the remaining space along an axis after accounting for padding and gaps between children. It determines the total used width or height by summing the measured sizes of children and the gaps between them (one gap per child pair). The leftover space is then divided equally among all children marked with the `grows` attribute, using the `idiv` function which returns zero if the divisor is zero or the dividend is negative.

```fprisc
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

The `tcStep` function in `logic.sol` attempts to execute a single instruction by first extracting its head and body, allocating new variables, and instantiating the instruction to generate a memory address. It then unifies this address with the current global state; if unification fails, the function returns the original state unchanged. If unification succeeds, it executes the instruction body, decrements the fuel, undoes variable allocation, and recursively processes the remaining clauses with the updated state.

```sol
tcStep db syms m c rest g gs fuel qvars sols =
  (hd, body, nv) = c;
  (hm, tm) = marks m;
  (hp0, vbase0, hl0, tr0, tt0, tl0) = m;
  m1 = allocVars nv m;
  (m2, haddr) = inst hd vbase0 m1;
  (m3, ok) = unify haddr g m2;
  (m4, fuel2, sols2) = tcBody db syms m3 ok body vbase0 gs (fuel - 1) qvars sols;
  m5 = undoTo hm tm m4;
  tryClauses db syms m5 rest g gs fuel2 qvars sols2.
```

The `splice` function calculates the edit distance by first finding the length of the common prefix and the length of the common suffix (after reversing the remaining parts of the strings). The number of characters to remove is the length of the string portion after the common prefix minus the length of the common suffix, and the number of characters to insert is the length of the string portion after the common prefix minus the common suffix.

```fprisc
splice old new =
  prefix = common old new 0;
  a = L.drop prefix old;
  b = L.drop prefix new;
  suffix = common (L.reverse a) (L.reverse b) 0;
  remove = L.length a - suffix;
  insert = L.take (L.length b - suffix) b;
  "[{prefix},{remove},{J.render (J.strings insert)}]".
```

