The `con` register pair facilitates console output by mapping the LSR (Line Status Register) and THR (Transmit Holding Register) via MMIO, allowing the implementation of `putc` for single characters and `puts` for strings. The `puts` function utilizes `putsFrom` to iterate through the string's characters, stopping if the index exceeds the string length, while `putcV` intelligently directs data to the write buffer only when the character index is odd. To ensure a complete line, the `nl` function appends a carriage return (13) followed by a line feed (10) after the string content.

```sol
putsFrom con s i n = case i > n of
    True -> Unit
  | False -> putc con (charAt s i) >> putsFrom con s (i + 1) n;
