module MyApp;

foreign {
  sndPlay: (Addr -> Unit);
}

-- The build will fail if sndPlay is not implemented in a linked driver
```

In the FP-RISC QOS environment, a write to a diskless service returns an `IErr` value if the target data is absent, which is treated as valid data rather than a fault. To detect this, the program must pattern match the result of the `Svc.write` call against `IErr`; if the result is `IErr`, the write was successful in signaling absence.

```sol
main =
  me = myself 0;
  u = device "uart";
  con = (reg8 u 5, reg8 u 0);
  granted = ("/services/storage", "write") :: Nil;
  caps = SVCM.Caps con me (reg32 49144) granted "test" (False, 0);
  _ = expect "diskless miss"
        (case Svc.write caps "/services/storage/kv" (IStr "x") of
           IErr _ -> True | _ -> False);
```

