Buffer b = Buffer.alloc(1024);
Buffer.resize(b, 2048);
Buffer.free(b);
```

A Layout is a user-defined data structure type in FP-RISC, similar to a struct in C, used to group related values together. Unlike an Address (Addr), a Layout is a value itself and cannot be directly assigned to an address variable without being allocated or dereferenced. Each Layout can contain fields of different types, such as Int or Addr, and supports operations like allocation, initialization, and field access.

