The file `fprisc/hal/fpr_g.c` serves as the runtime implementation that resolves unresolved global symbols in FP-RISC programs by providing the necessary C function pointers. It defines the `fpr_g_<name>` symbols required to bridge the language's static callable descriptors (`FPR_FN`) with the host system's external world, effectively allowing FP-RISC code to interact with the operating system or hardware abstraction layer.

