The `scanLocals` function in `livejs.fpr` extracts local state by querying all elements with the `x-data` attribute, splitting the attribute value by semicolons, and parsing each key-value pair. It iterates through the split pairs, locates the equals sign, and stores the resulting key and value in a client-side `locals` object.

```sol
function scanLocals() {
  var root = document.getElementById('lv-root');
  var locals = Object.create(null);
  root.querySelectorAll('[x-data]').forEach(function(el) {
    var attrs = el.getAttribute('x-data').split(';');
    attrs.forEach(function(pair) {
      if (!pair) return;
      var eq = pair.indexOf('=');
      if (eq > 0) {
        locals[pair.slice(0, eq)] = pair.slice(eq + 1);
      }
