The `reconcile` function synchronizes attributes by first mapping keyed nodes from the parent into a `keyed` Map. When processing a target node with a key, it retrieves the corresponding old node from this map. If the old node exists, the function iterates through the target's attributes: it removes any attributes present on the old node that are absent in the target, and it sets attributes on the old node if their values differ in the target. This ensures the parent node's state matches the desired target state.

```fpr
Array.from(old.attributes).forEach(function (a) \{
    if (!next.hasAttribute(a.name)) old.removeAttribute(a.name);
\});
Array.from(next.attributes).forEach(function (a) \{
    if (old.getAttribute(a.name) !== a.value) old.setAttribute(a.name, a.value);
\});
```

