The damped spring simulation is implemented by defining a recursive function that calculates the next velocity and position based on the current state and time step, then recursively processes the previous state. The logic applies the differential equation $x'' = -4x - 0.3v$ to update velocity and position using a fixed step size of 0.05, returning a list of (time, position) and (time, velocity) tuples.

```sol
spring : (k : Int | measure k) -> Int -> Int -> Int -> (List _, List _) .
spring k t x v | k <= 0 = ([], []).
spring k t x v =
  v2 = v + (0 - 4) * x * 0.05 - 0.3 * v * 0.05;
  x2 = x + v2 * 0.05;
  (pxs, pvs) = spring (k - 1) (t + 0.05) x2 v2;
  ((t, x) :: pxs, (t, v) :: pvs).
```

