The `drainN` function recursively receives messages from the source channel until k items are processed or the source is exhausted. It maintains a `last` value to enforce ordering, updating it only if the current message is greater than `last`. The function returns a tuple containing the count of items drained and the new ordered state.

```sol
drainN me main 0 last ordered = (last, ordered);
drainN me main k last ordered =
  v = receiveFrom me main;
  drainN me main (k - 1) v (ordered and v > last);
```

