The FP-RISC runtime automatically uses the new 128 KiB stack block size for actors when the system is initialized; no manual configuration or code changes are required by the user. This optimization reduces the initial stack allocation for an actor from 512 KiB to 128 KiB, allowing more actors to fit within the same memory pool. For example, a session with two actors now consumes significantly less memory than the previous measurement, aligning with the documented floor of a 128 KiB stack block per actor.

