The function `attachOne` retrieves the app's manifest, logs the attachment, and returns the app record if the operation succeeds. If the manifest is unreadable or the attachment fails, it logs an error and returns an empty list, effectively skipping that app.

```sol
attachOne : unsafe Int -> Int -> List String -> String -> String -> List App .
attachOne me st r id =
  b = rpc me st 1 "apps/{id}.qa" "";
  case b of
    Err e ->
      _ = Sys.logAt 1 "system: apps/{id}.qa unreadable ({e}), skipped";
      attachIds me st r
  | Ok bytes ->
      ti = Mod.plugs 0;
      (aid, anm) = qaManifest bytes;
      a = Plug.attach bytes;
      case a of
        Err e ->
          _ = Sys.logAt 1 "system: attach {id} failed ({e}), skipped";
          attachIds me st r
      | Ok u ->
          _ = Sys.logAt 0 "system: app {aid} ({anm}) -> table #{ti}";
          App aid anm ti :: attachIds me st r
```

