The `moveBy` function calculates new velocity components by projecting forward and right movements onto the current yaw orientation, scaling them by the move velocity, and applying them to the existing velocity vector. To replicate this, define a function that computes sine and cosine of the yaw, calculates the new velocity deltas, and returns a new model state with updated velocities.

```sol
moveBySol : unsafe Mdl -> Int -> Int -> Mdl .
moveBySol (Mdl (Bd px py pz vx vy vz g) yaw pit sel act) f r =
  sw = sinA yaw; cw = cosA yaw;
  nvx = (f * sw + r * cw) * moveV / fx;
  nvz = (f * cw - r * sw) * moveV / fx;
  Mdl (Bd px py pz (vx + nvx) vy (vz + nvz) g) yaw pit sel "move".
```

