A library unit compiles a file as a linkable object where every defined name is qualified by its module hash to prevent clashes with linked programs, requires no `main` function, and emits constructor stubs as `.weak` symbols so the program's copies win at link time. A program unit serves as the executable root, whereas a library unit is designed to be imported by a program using the `BUILTIN_EXTRA=` flag.

```fprisc
