The file `std/mvu.fpr` provides the MVU driver as a library that implements a persistent render worker architecture for FP-RISC applications. It utilizes soft death semantics where the system pool resets at every frame boundary to manage memory without traditional actors, and it caches statics only when the model key changes to trigger renderer recompilation. This design eliminates per-frame actor ledger overhead by having a single worker actor receive render requests from the caller, which then forwards the reply before dropping its reference.

```sol
