let worker = spawn {
  recvFrom {
    case r of
      RvRequest -> {
        let reply = textRender(model);
        sendTo caller reply;
        drop worker;
      }
    end
  }
}
```

The MVU driver utilizes `Sys.poolReset` at every frame boundary to enforce soft death, ensuring that actor memory is cleared and self-healed for the next frame without spawning new actors. This mechanism provides frame-per-actor memory semantics while eliminating the need for persistent actor lifecycles. In Sol, this is implemented by calling the system reset function within the frame loop:

