The test involves allocating a 64-bit mask with the 63rd bit set, then verifying that `bitSet` creates it, `bitTest` detects it, `bitClear` removes it, `shr` and `shl` shift the bit to/from position 63, `and` and `or` with their inverses result in zero and all ones respectively, and `not` inverts the mask.

```fprisc
bits =
  top = Word.bitSet (Word.fromInt 0) 63;
  _ = check (Word.bitTest top 63);
  _ = check (Word.bitClear top 63 == Word.fromInt 0);
  _ = check (Word.shr top 63 == Word.fromInt 1);
  _ = check (Word.shl (Word.fromInt 1) 63 == top);
  _ = check (Word.and top (Word.not top) == Word.fromInt 0);
  _ = check (Word.or top (Word.not top) == Word.mask 64 0);
```

