The file `runtime/vec.c` defines the column vector structure `col_t` as a single contiguous memory span consisting of a capacity and a base address, eliminating per-block walks and SIMD tier complexity by running on one span. Growth operations are handled by `fpr_realloc`, which uses a copy-based approach through pool tiers where the freed predecessor is recycled exactly, while bigfree remains as the pool's exact-fit recycler for large payloads. This layout simplifies allocation paths and ensures that codegen and GPU marshalling loops operate on raw spans without needing per-block cursor management.

```c
