typedef struct {
    size_t cap; // Total capacity of the contiguous span
    void* base; // Base address of the contiguous span (word offset 1)
} col_t;
```

In-place growth will not occur. The runtime will fall back to a copy-based allocation through the pool tiers, which involves copying the existing data and allocating a new span. This deviation from the plan is recorded because in-place growth is only efficient when bulk storage sits behind Memory.qa.

