In FP-RISC, the `step` function represents the core transition of the system state, mapping an event to a new model and a list of commands. Unlike mutable state in other languages, the model is immutable, and the next state is derived purely from the current model and the event. The function signature is `step : Ev -> Model -> (Model, Cmds)`.

```sol
step : Ev -> Model -> (Model, Cmds) {
    case event of
        Move(dir) ->
            newModel = updatePosition(model, dir)
            cmds = collectCommands(model, dir)
            return (newModel, cmds)

        Interact(tile) ->
            newModel = updateInteraction(model, tile)
            cmds = collectCommands(model, tile)
            return (newModel, cmds)

        _ ->
            return (model, emptyCmds)
    }
}
```

