The `ddaStep` function calculates the next cell index by multiplying the step direction components (dx, dy, dz) by the axis selectors (sx, sy, sz) derived from the current maximum coordinates and the entry point, then summing these products with the current index. Simultaneously, it updates the maximum traversal coordinates (tmx, tmy, tmz) by adding the step direction vectors (tdx, tdy, tdz) scaled by the axis selectors to the previous maximum values, ensuring the algorithm correctly tracks the bounding box for the ray's path through the voxel grid.

```sol
idx2 = Vec.zipAdd (Vec.zipAdd (Vec.zipAdd idx (Vec.zipMul sx1 dsx1))
                        (Vec.zipMul sy1 dsy1))
                (Vec.zipMul sz1 dsz1);

tmx3 = Vec.zipAdd tmxU (Vec.zipMul sx2 tdx1);
tmy3 = Vec.zipAdd tmyU (Vec.zipMul sy2 tdy1);
