If a panic occurs after writes have been buffered and a command has been queued, the transaction commits nothing, effectively discarding all pending writes and queued commands. To prevent this, ensure that no code executes between the buffering of writes and the finalization of the transaction that could trigger a panic, such as calling `parseInt` on an invalid string or performing an invalid operation.

