```sol
-- Example demonstrating the non-atomic receipt message
tx {
  shq {
    write_file "data.txt" "content"
    fail "intentional error"
  }
}
-- The receipt will state: NOT atomic: a deferred command failed
```

When a deferred command fails, the transaction does not claim full atomicity. The system fails the shq half-commits, applies the receipt to claim partial atomicity, and explicitly reports the failure in the summary with the message "NOT atomic: a deferred command failed". This ensures that the receipt accurately reflects that not all validated file effects were successfully applied, preventing the illusion of a complete transaction.

```sol
-- Example Sol code illustrating the non-atomic receipt
tx {
  deferred {
    write "file.txt" "content"
  }
}
-- If the deferred write fails, the receipt will state:
-- "NOT atomic: a deferred command failed"
```

