The `epoch` function performs a single training iteration by computing gradients for weights and bias over a dataset and updating them using the specified learning rate. It executes three sequential vector folds: the first calculates the gradient for weight $w_1$, the second for $w_2$, and the third for the bias $b$. After computing these sums ($s1, s2, s3$), it updates the parameters by subtracting the learning rate multiplied by the average of each sum (divided by $n$).

```sol
epoch n lr w1 w2 b v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (gW1 w1 w2 b) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (gW2 w1 w2 b) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (gB w1 w2 b) 0 v2;
  (w1 - lr * (s1 / n), w2 - lr * (s2 / n), b - lr * (s3 / n), v3).
```

