When the font size (`fsOf a`) is greater than zero, `textSize` calculates width and height using proportional formulas based on the font's advance and line metrics; if the calculated width exceeds the character cap (`ellipOf a`), the width is clamped to the cap value. If the font size is zero or negative, it uses fixed-width calculations based on the character's script size (`scOf a`).
```fprisc
textSize a n t =
  e = fsOf a;
  (w, h) = case e > 0 of
    True -> (propW t e, propH e)
  | False -> (textW n (scOf a), textH (scOf a));
  cap = ellipOf a;
  case cap > 0 and w > cap of True -> (cap, h) | False -> (w, h).
```

