The code uses `el.textContent` to update the visible text content of elements, while `el.style.display` controls the visibility (showing or hiding) of elements based on a condition. If `v` is undefined when accessing `locals[spec[0]]`, the expression `v && v !== '0' && v !== 'false'` evaluates to `false`, correctly hiding the element. However, if the intent is to treat an empty string as a valid state or if the logic requires explicit handling of missing keys, the code should ensure `v` defaults to an empty string before comparison to avoid relying solely on the truthiness of an undefined value, which might not match all intended display states.

