h0 = heapUsed Unit;
a2 = Vec.filter keepEven a1;
h1 = heapUsed Unit;
-- h1 - h0 < 4096 proves in-place compaction
```

The function `fillI` returns a vector containing the integers from 1 up to the specified limit, constructed in-place without heap allocation. When called with a limit of 1000, it produces the sequence [1, 2, ..., 1000]. Summing these values using `Vec.fold` returns 250,500, calculated as the sum of the first 1000 positive integers.

