In hosted AArch64 builds, the operating system keeps the hardware thread (hart) in the x28 register, which is read via a volatile assembly instruction in the runtime. To prevent the compiler from saving x28 on the callee-saved register stack during function calls, all C files are compiled with the `-ffixed-x27` flag. This ensures that x28 remains available for the scheduler to track hart migration without being clobbered by the function epilogue.

```sol
