The flag `-ffixed-x27` instructs the compiler to treat the x27 register as a fixed register that cannot be saved or restored during function calls. This is necessary because AArch64 normally saves callee-saved registers in pairs, including the x27-x28 pair, but QOS applications always read the hart identifier through the volatile assembly variable `__thread` which maps to x28. Since the actor body migrates between hardware threads while the hart remains in x28, saving x28 would cause the epilogue to return to the wrong thread. By compiling with `-ffixed-x27`, the compiler avoids saving x28 entirely, ensuring that the hart value remains available in x28 for the scheduler to locate the correct thread upon resumption.

```sol
