Atomics require naturally aligned eight-byte locations in ordinary RAM. The exchange operation uses the `amoswap.d.aqrl` instruction, while compare-exchange utilizes an LR/SC retry loop that applies an acquire on the read and a release on a successful write (with failure performing an acquire read).

