The commit protocol ensures crash-atomicity by utilizing a redo journal with PID-stamped lock reclaim and a complete-or-absent journal written specifically at the commit point. This design allows the system to verify the state of a transaction upon restart, ensuring that either all writes are successfully applied or none are, without leaving the disk in an inconsistent state. For instance, a script using `writeAtomic` will either fully commit its changes or abort silently, leaving the filesystem untouched if a panic occurs mid-script.

```sol
// Example of a crash-atomic write operation
writeAtomic {
  file: "data.log",
  content: "committed record"
}
```

The `QL.compact` function reclaims space in a disk image by removing tombstones (deleted records) that are no longer referenced, effectively shrinking the file size. It achieves idempotency because if the disk is already compacted or if there are no tombstones to remove, running the function again results in the same metadata and size; for example, in the provided test, `h7` (the result of the second compact) is identical to `h6` (the first compact), confirming that `cIdem` evaluates to true.

```fprisc
h6 = QL.compact dsk h5;
h7 = QL.compact dsk h6;
cIdem = h7 == h6;
```

The QOS compiler optimizes nested vector maps by fusing multiple sequential map operations into a single, more efficient kernel execution, eliminating intermediate allocations and reducing overhead. This optimization is verified by checking that the result of fused operations matches the expected mathematical outcome and that heap usage remains minimal, indicating in-place execution without temporary buffers. For instance, the `Vec.map` operations on a vector `a1` are fused such that `Vec.map scaleUp` followed by `Vec.map shiftDn` produces the same sum as a non-fused pipeline, while simultaneously ensuring the heap footprint difference is less than 4096 units:

```fprisc
a1 = fillI (Vec.new Unit) 1 4000;
h0 = heapUsed Unit;
a2 = Vec.map shiftDn (Vec.map scaleUp a1);
h1 = heapUsed Unit;
(s1, a3) = sumI a2;
_ = Vec.free a3;
u0 = verdict "fused-scalar-nested" (s1 == refI 1 4000);
u1 = verdict "fused-scalar-inplace" (h1 - h0 < 4096);
```

