No, standalone modules cannot reliably resolve the full prelude, so `List.rev` is unavailable at the module level. You must implement a reversal using an accumulator or use the root program's prelude. For example, in a root program you can use `List.rev`, but in a separate module like `programs/mods/coreutil.fpr`, you must define your own helper:
