tr = Vec.new Unit;
m0 = (hp, 1, 0, tr, 1, 0);
```

The `splice` function first calculates the length of the common prefix between the two strings using the `common` function. It then removes this prefix from both strings. Next, it reverses the remaining parts of both strings and calculates the length of their new common prefix to determine the overlap (suffix). The number of characters to remove is the length of the first string's remainder minus this suffix length, while the number of characters to insert is the difference between the second string's remainder length and the suffix length.

```fprisc
splice old new =
  prefix = common old new 0;
  a = L.drop prefix old;
  b = L.drop prefix new;
  suffix = common (L.reverse a) (L.reverse b) 0;
  remove = L.length a - suffix;
  insert = L.take (L.length b - suffix) b;
  "[{prefix},{remove},{J.render (J.strings insert)}]".
```

