The manager actor is spawned by ARC.qa for each promoted object to handle Increment (INC) and Decrement (DEC) messages, ensuring structural atomicity through mailbox linearization. When a DEC message reduces the count to zero, the system deallocates the object and causes the manager actor to exit.

```fprisc
// Conceptual example of the manager actor receiving messages
actor Manager =
  receive INC {
    count := count + 1
    send to Holder { count }
  }
  receive DEC {
    count := count - 1
    if count == 0 {
      dealloc object
      exit
    }
    send to Holder { count }
  }
```

