A flat image consists of loadable bytes laid out at their final offsets with gaps already zero-filled, allowing the loader to copy the image directly to a base address without walking ELF program headers. In contrast, a slot is a fixed virtual-address range reserved for a single loaded process or plugin image; the QOS loader will refuse to load a second overlapping plugin image into such a slot.

