The scheduling discipline ensures that only actors with an earlier stamp can be admitted ahead of a given actor. Therefore, even though `x` was moved to the `ready` list, `y` (being un-aged) will be selected for admission first.

```sol
// Example showing the incorrect assumption
actor x = new Actor();
park x; // x has old stamp

actor y = new Actor();
y.receive(msg); // y becomes READY with fresh stamp

// Incorrect: expecting x to run next because it was manually moved
ready add x; 

// Correct behavior: y runs first due to age priority
run x; // This will not happen immediately; y will be admitted first
```

