```sol
siStamp : unsafe Int -> Int -> Int -> a .
siStamp left from me =
  clint = device "clint";
  mt = reg32 clint 49144;
  _ = send from (4, read mt, 1);
  stampInput (left - 1) me.
```

The `siStamp` function is called recursively by `stampInput` when the remaining press count (`left`) is greater than zero. It accesses the CLINT device at address 49144, reads the current time, sends a message containing the key code (4), the read time, and a flag (1) to the sender, and then decrements the press counter before calling `stampInput` again.

```sol
siStamp left from me =
  clint = device "clint";
  mt = reg32 clint 49144;
  _ = send from (4, read mt, 1);
  stampInput (left - 1) me.
```

The stampInput service measures latency by treating the instant a key is pressed (key-down) as the instant the service replies. The system reads a CLINT register to capture the timestamp immediately before sending the reply and again immediately after receiving the reply; the difference between these two timestamps represents the service-to-update latency.

```sol
siStamp left from me =
  clint = device "clint";
