The `std/store` system compacts one small shard at a time by rewriting only the file containing superseded lines when they outnumber live ones. To ensure state survives a tidy, any data built inside an actor must reside within the tidied value itself; a bug was found where a shard kept its file path outside its state, causing the path to dangle after the first reset.

```fprisc
// Example of a shard value that survives tidying (path inside the value)
