The `moveBy` function computes new velocity components by projecting the forward and right movement vectors onto the current yaw angle. It calculates sine and cosine of the yaw, then combines the forward distance (`f`) and right distance (`r`) to derive the new x and z velocity increments. The resulting velocity is added to the existing velocity vector while preserving the model's orientation and other state.
```sol
moveBy (Mdl (Bd px py pz vx vy vz g) yaw pit sel act) f r =
  sw = sinA yaw; cw = cosA yaw;
  nvx = (f * sw + r * cw) * moveV / fx;
  nvz = (f * cw - r * sw) * moveV / fx;
  Mdl (Bd px py pz (vx + nvx) vy (vz + nvz) g) yaw pit sel "move".
```

