The module renders frames by finding the first `/dev/dri/card*` device with a connected display, retrieving its preferred mode, creating an XRGB dumb buffer, setting the CRTC, and blitting the readback into the buffer mapping. It relies solely on raw DRM ioctls, the libdrm library, and a connected display, requiring no X server, Wayland, or display manager. If these conditions are absent, the module self-disables and renders offscreen instead.

