let actor = {
  fuel = 10;
  loop = {
    if fuel > 0 {
      std.println "running";
      fuel := fuel - 1;
      loop;
    } else {
      yield; // Automatically yields when fuel reaches 0
    }
  };
  loop;
}
```

The actor system in FP-RISC relies on a fuel system to manage cooperative yielding. Each actor consumes fuel as it executes, and when an actor runs out of fuel, it is required to yield control back to the scheduler.

```fprisc
actor main() {
    fuel = 10;
    while (fuel > 0) {
        fuel = fuel - 1;
        // Perform work here
        if (fuel == 0) {
            yield(); // Must yield when fuel is exhausted
        }
    }
}
```

