This pattern violates the "DROP LAWS" of the MVU driver, which mandate that drops must be drained every poll reply to prevent memory accumulation. Keeping a reference to the reply causes the worker to forward the render reply and then drop its own ref, but the retained reference prevents the advance drop of the previous frame's reply, leading to a ~50-second idle fuse where multiple live ARC entries accumulate per frame. The code must be corrected by ensuring the reply is dropped immediately after forwarding, allowing the system to maintain only one live ARC entry per frame.

```sol
