The `boundary` keyword is used to define a frame boundary, which is essential for manual memory management in FP-RISC. It ensures that temporary objects created within a loop are cleaned up correctly at the end of the loop iteration, preventing memory leaks where objects persist indefinitely. Without `boundary`, a long-lived loop could accumulate all temporary objects it ever made.
