h2 = heapUsed Unit;
b2 = Vec.filter keepBig b1;
h3 = heapUsed Unit;
(n2, b2b) = Vec.len b2;
(s3, b3) = sumP b2b;
_ = Vec.free b3;
u6 = verdict "record-in-place" (h3 - h2 < 65536);
```

Yes, the `Vec.filter` operation automatically compacts the resulting vector, ensuring that rows stay aligned without gaps. This is verified by comparing the heap usage before and after the filter; if the vector were not compacted, the heap usage would increase significantly due to the allocated space for the gap, whereas the test confirms the usage difference is minimal (less than 65536 units).

