The `histB` function recursively processes a list of integers to increment their corresponding bin counts in a histogram vector. For each element, it retrieves the bin index and the value from their respective vectors, calculates a position based on the bin index and value, retrieves the old count, increments it, and updates the histogram vector using `Vec.set` before recursing on the remaining list.

```fprisc
histB h cs ys (i :: r) k =
  (b, cs2) = Vec.get (i + 1) cs;
  (y, ys2) = Vec.get (i + 1) ys;
  pos = b * k + y + 1;
  (old, h2) = Vec.get pos h;
  histB (Vec.set pos (old + 1) h2) cs2 ys2 r k.
```

The function `histB` recursively processes a list of values `ys` to update a histogram `h` based on a counter `k` and a list of cumulative sums `cs`. For each value `i` in the list, it retrieves the bin index `b` and the value `y` from the cumulative sum vector `cs` at position `i+1`. It calculates a new position `pos` as `b * k + y + 1` and increments the count at that position in the histogram `h`. The function returns the updated histogram, the remaining cumulative sum vector, and the rest of the list.

```fprisc
histB h cs ys (i :: r) k =
  (b, cs2) = Vec.get (i + 1) cs;
  (y, ys2) = Vec.get (i + 1) ys;
  pos = b * k + y + 1;
  (old, h2) = Vec.get pos h;
  histB (Vec.set pos (old + 1) h2) cs2 ys2 r k.
```

