QOS pool slabs start small and double in size with each new slab, whereas actors in an FP-RISC session initially took a full `FPR_SLAB_SZ` (256 KiB) regardless of their needs. This initial large allocation meant that a thousand small session actors consumed 508 MiB of arena memory before performing any work, contrasting with the incremental growth model of the slabs.

```sol
