// Actors always take the full block immediately
```

Memory allocation in FPR pools utilizes a buddy system where slabs start small and double in size. Every actor that allocates memory initially takes a whole `FPR_SLAB_SZ` block (256 KiB), which is now the first buddy block, with subsequent slabs doubling until reaching a maximum of 196 MiB. Additionally, an actor's first stack is allocated as a single 128 KiB block instead of the previous 512 KiB block.

```sol
