The `ddaLoop` function terminates the traversal when the step counter `k` reaches zero or less, at which point it invokes `ddaDone` to release all allocated resources (registers and vectors) and return the updated view matrix `w` and height `rh`. The loop internally decrements a counter derived from the initial `k` and the current step count `cnt` to determine the next iteration, ensuring that once no lanes are active, the tile processing is considered finished.

```fpr
ddaLoop w dda k | k <= 0 = ddaDone w dda;
ddaLoop w dda k =
  (w2, dda2, cnt) = ddaStep w dda;
  ddaLoop w2 dda2 (kNext k cnt).

kNext k 0 = 0.
kNext k cnt = k - 1.

ddaDone w (Dda rs rk rd rf rh te) =
  _ = freeRs rs; _ = freeRk rk; _ = freeRd rd; _ = freeRf rf;
  _ = Vec.free te;
  (w, rh).
```

