The `Layout` type acts as a nominal pointer over raw memory that computes offsets but incurs no runtime cost, as the generated code is no larger than the equivalent version using raw offsets. Additionally, any accessor code derived from a `Layout` is stripped out during the linking process, meaning no accessor survives into the final linked image.

```sol
