val x = @layout.load(i32)
```

A malformed `Layout` is refused by name, meaning the compiler will reject it during the type-checking phase. The documentation states that `Layout` is a nominal pointer type over raw memory, and because it is a type of its own, any code attempting to use an invalid layout definition will fail to compile before execution.

