In the context of the `versions_db` function, "last binding wins" means that if multiple lines in the `.fpr/versions.db` file define the same hash, only the entry from the last matching line will be stored in the dictionary. The `versions_db` function iterates through the file line by line, splitting each line into parts. If a line has at least three parts, it uses the third part (the hash) as a key in the `db` dictionary, assigning the name and version from the first and second parts to that key. Because Python dictionaries update existing keys with new values, subsequent occurrences of the same hash overwrite previous entries, ensuring the final result reflects the most recently defined version for that hash.

