Transparent Huge Pages incur a significant performance penalty on allocation when configured to `always` in Buildroot, causing a 27% cost increase due to the process of resetting and refaulting 2 MiB pages during pool resets. To mitigate this, the kernel configuration should set `CONFIG_TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_MADVISE=y`, which aligns THP behavior with the standard `madvise` default used in Ubuntu, eliminating the extra allocation overhead.

