The `logged` handler determines the log level by checking if the HTTP response status code is greater than or equal to 400. If the status indicates a failure (4xx or 5xx), it logs a warning with the message "request failed" and the request details. Otherwise, it logs an info message with the message "request".

```sol
logged log handler req =
  resp = handler req;
  fields = ("method", req.method) :: ("path", req.path) :: ("status", str resp.status) :: ("bytes", str (strlen resp.body)) :: Nil;
  _ = (case resp.status >= 400 of True -> Log.warn log "request failed" fields | False -> Log.info log "request" fields);
  resp.
```

