}
```

The `--system=esp-idf` profile compiles to RV32 assembly but does not generate any ESP-IDF specific code, relying instead on FP-RISC refusals to interact with the OS. A major architectural constraint is that each FP-RISC hart is pinned to a core as a FreeRTOS task at priority 1, meaning any standard ESP-IDF task (such as those handling lwIP or SDIO) can preempt the actor. Additionally, if a CPU-bound actor runs indefinitely on its core, it prevents the FreeRTOS idle task from running on that core, which disables the system watchdog checks and makes detecting a real hang impossible.

```sol
-- Example of an actor pinned to a core in an ESP-IDF context
actor main =
  let loop = forever {
    yield; -- Yields to allow ESP-IDF tasks to preempt
  }
  in run loop;
```

