In QOS, every unit runs on its own phase determined by a hash of its slot, which functions as a triangle wave clock that sweeps briskly between ends with holds. This clock drives specific idle animations, such as soldiers shifting weight, drawing rifles, scanning tank turrets, and bobbing trucks. Because all motion is a function of the clock, a replayed game moves the same way as the original.

