To convert a received message into a list of EMsg events, use the `portAsk` function, which sends a drain signal, receives the messages, and converts them using `portConv`. If the port is not subscribed (indicated by a port number of 0), `portAsk` returns an empty list immediately.

```fprisc
portAsk me pa =
  _ = send pa (PDrain me);
  ms = receiveFrom me pa;
  evs = portConv ms Nil;
  _ = drop ms;
  evs.

portConv ms acc = case ms of
  Nil -> revK Nil acc
  | tv :: r -> portConv1 r acc tv.

portConv1 r acc tv =
  (tag, arg) = tv;
  portConv r (EMsg (strCopy tag) (strCopy arg) :: acc).
```

Calling `portAsk` with `pa = 0` results in an infinite loop because the guard `pa == 0` evaluates to `True`, causing the function to return `Nil` without ever executing the `receiveFrom` or `send` operations. The code explicitly guards against this case to prevent the system from attempting to interact with a non-existent or invalid port, which would otherwise block the loop indefinitely.

```fprisc
portAsk : unsafe Int -> Int -> List Ev .
portAsk me pa =
  if pa == 0 then
    Nil
  else
    _ = send pa (PDrain me);
    ms = receiveFrom me pa;
    evs = portConv ms Nil;
    _ = drop ms;
    evs.
```

