The deadlock detector treats an actor waiting for an interrupt as non-deadlocked, similar to how it treats a sleeper, via the `g_irq_waiting` exemption. This is necessary because idle servers previously appeared "moving" only due to poller ticks; without this exemption, the detector would incorrectly kill idle servers after two seconds.

```sol
