    actor.await_irq(); 
} else {
    // Standard blocking behavior
    actor.await_condition();
}
```

The `std/poller` module manages non-blocking polling for event readiness by offloading descriptor management to a dedicated host thread that blocks on `poll(2)` and signals readiness via hardware interrupts. When an interrupt arrives, the runtime's `irq_drain` delivers it to an actor bound with `Sys.irqBind`, which notifies the poller and re-arms it. This design prevents the deadlock detector from misidentifying actors waiting for interrupts as deadlocked, thereby allowing idle servers to remain active without being prematurely terminated.

