The `load` function retrieves rows from the store either by calculating the start index for a specific page or by searching if a query string is provided. It calculates the total number of pages based on the result count and page size, ensuring at least one page is displayed. If the requested page exceeds the total available pages, it automatically loads the last page instead.
```fprisc
load store v =
  q = String.toLower v.q;
  (rows, n) = (if strlen q == 0 then Store.page (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store
               else Store.search (matches q) (v.page * pageSize) pageSize store);
  pages = (if n == 0 then 1 else (n + pageSize - 1) / pageSize);
  (if v.page >= pages and v.page > 0 then load store {v | page = pages - 1}
   else {rows = rows, count = n, total = (if strlen q == 0 then n else Store.count store), pages = pages, page = v.page}).
```

The `load` function calculates the total number of pages by dividing the count of matching entries by the page size, rounding up to ensure a complete page is allocated. If the current page index provided in the request is greater than or equal to this calculated total, the function automatically redirects the request to the last valid page (total - 1) to prevent rendering a page beyond the data's end.

```fprisc
