expect "disk untouched" (readNow "/tmp/test.txt") "";
```

The deletion is immediately visible to the user, and subsequent attempts to read the deleted file fail. The system treats the removal as a composition of effects that overwrites the pending write state. For example, after writing "b" to a file, if you delete it, the `ls` command will no longer list the file, and any attempt to read it will return an error or false success status rather than the content "b".

