  print (show (Http.get "{base}/test"));
  Tcp.stop l;
  print "Server stopped".
```

The file at `/etc/.sol-lock` serves as a write-lock for the parent directory, which is acquired whenever a path is touched during a transaction commit, including reads. For a non-root user, attempting to read `/etc/hostname` forces the system to lock `/etc`, causing the read to fail with an `EACCES` error indistinguishable from lock contention. Consequently, the user enters a 5-second spin loop and terminates with a "could not lock" message, whereas a root user would succeed because the container does not see the permission error.

```sol
# Example of the lock acquisition failure
try {
    read "/etc/hostname"
} catch EACCES {
    # Spins 5s and dies with "could not lock"
    exit "could not lock"
}
```

