The system initializes the UART by first resetting the FIFO and disabling interrupts via specific register writes to the device control register. It then configures the baud rate divisor latch by setting the DLAB (Divisor Latch Access Bit) to enable 16-bit mode, writing the low and high bytes of the divisor, and finally disabling DLAB to restore the 8-bit 8N1 configuration.

```sol
doInitUart me st from =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  d2 = device "uart";
  _ = write (reg8 d2 3) 3;
  _ = write (reg8 d2 1) 0;
  _ = write (reg8 d2 3) 131;
  _ = write (reg8 d2 0) (band 115200 255);
  _ = write (reg8 d2 1) (BITSHIFTR 115200 8);
  _ = write (reg8 d2 3) 3;
  reply me from UOk st.
```

