The `writeAtomic` function ensures crash-atomicity by utilizing a redo journal that is PID-stamped and written at the commit point, guaranteeing that either the entire transaction is committed or none of it is. It handles lock reclaim by performing dead-owner lock reclaim through atomic rename operations, ensuring that if a process terminates unexpectedly, its locks are properly released without data corruption.

```sol
writeAtomic (pid, data) {
  // PID-stamped entry appended to redo journal
  journal.append (pid, data)

  // Atomic rename performs dead-owner lock reclaim
  if (owner.isDead) {
    atomic.rename (oldPath, newPath)
  }

  // fsync ensures complete-or-absent journal persistence
  fsync (journal)
}
```

