_ = QL.sbW dsk (mTorn (QL.metaOr dsk h7));
hT = QL.ensure dsk;
tornOk = case hT == h7 of
           True -> mCommit (QL.metaOr dsk h7) == 1
         | False -> False;
```

The `QL.compact` function processes tombstoned data and removes their associated tombstones from the disk state. When invoked a second time on a state where all tombstones have already been removed, the operation returns a state identical to the previous one, indicating idempotency. This is verified by comparing the resulting handle with the input handle; if they are equal, the compaction has stabilized.

```sol
h5 = QL.appendRec dsk h4 "QDEL" "qd2/tmp{boot}" "";
h6 = QL.compact dsk h5;
h7 = QL.compact dsk h6;
cIdem = h7 == h6;
```

When a write operation is torn, the system detects that the commit flag is 0 instead of 1. The system automatically rolls back the operation to restore consistency. This behavior is demonstrated by setting the `Torn` flag on the disk metadata and then calling `QL.ensure`, which verifies the rollback by checking if the commit flag remains 0.

```fprisc
_ = QL.sbW dsk (mTorn (QL.metaOr dsk h7));
hT = QL.ensure dsk;
tornOk = case hT == h7 of
           True -> mCommit (QL.metaOr dsk h7) == 1
         | False -> False;
```

To find the bounds of a list of points, you first extract the x and y coordinates using `fst2` and `snd2`, then use `bMin` and `bMax` to find the extremes, and finally apply `padB` to handle degenerate spans where the minimum and maximum are identical. The `ptsBounds` function combines these steps.

```sol
ptsBounds pts =
  xs = map (fn p -> fst2 p) pts;
  ys = map (fn p -> snd2 p) pts;
  (lo1, hi1) = padB (bMin xs) (bMax xs);
  (lo2, hi2) = padB (bMin ys) (bMax ys);
  (lo1, hi1, lo2, hi2).
```

