To implement this pattern, define a state type to track the counter and use a recursive function that checks the counter value against a threshold. If the threshold is met, send a reply to the boss and return the counter; otherwise, send an ask to the replier, receive the reply, yield control, and increment the counter. When the counter reaches a specific boundary, reset the state to self and call `Sys.poolReset` to simulate a frame boundary.

```sol
St = Type (St rep boss k).
pollLoop me st =
  St rep boss k = st;
  case k >= 20000 of
    True -> _ = send boss (Reply k); k
  | False -> pollTurn me st.
pollTurn me st =
  St rep boss k = st;
  _ = send rep (Ask me);
  r = receiveFrom me rep;
  Reply n = r;
  _ = drop r;
  _ = yield me;
  st2 = St rep boss (k + 1);
  pollLoop me st2.
```

