```sol
boundary me st =
  _ = send me st;
  _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
  m = receiveFrom me me;
  st2 = keep m;
  _ = drop m;
  st2.
```

Phase 2 introduces a contiguous Vec on `realloc` to replace the previous strategy of copying data into a new location. Instead of allocating a new block and copying the old contents, the new mechanism attempts to perform an in-place grow via buddy-absorb, falling back to a copy only if necessary. This reduces overhead by avoiding unnecessary data duplication when the new size is contiguous with existing memory.

```c
// Conceptual example of the new contiguous Vec behavior on realloc
// Attempting in-place grow via buddy-absorb before copying
if (can_grow_in_place(current_vec, new_size)) {
    absorb_buddy(current_vec, new_size);
    // No copy needed
} else {
    copy_fallback(current_vec, new_size);
}
```

