The file `fprisc/std/store.fpr` defines the `serveShard` function, which implements a high-performance, append-only key-value store service operating on a single shard. It manages a collection of entries within a map while tracking line counts for potential compaction, supporting operations such as inserting and removing key-value pairs, retrieving specific keys, counting total entries, and paginating results. The implementation leverages the Fprisc `M` map type for efficient lookups and uses a `J` (JSON) codec to serialize data before appending to a text file, ensuring durability through atomic file operations.

```fprisc
serveShard cfg q st = case st of 
    Sh entries lines path -> 
      case q of
        SPut x -> 
          k = cfg.key x;
          _ = append path (J.render (J.object (("k", J.Integer k) :: ("v", one cfg x) :: Nil)));
          entries2 = M.insert k (keep x) entries;
          lines2 = compactIf cfg path entries2 (lines + 1);
          (Sh entries2 lines2 path, SCountIs (M.size entries2))
        -- ... other operations ...
```

