The `heapInit` function performs two checks on the heap bounds. First, it verifies that the start address is not greater than the end address; if `hi <= lo`, it returns the error "Builtin: heap too small". Second, it checks if the calculated word count between the aligned start and end is less than 96; if `(Word.sub hi lo) < 96`, it returns the error "Builtin: heap too small". This ensures the heap can hold at least 96 words (768 bytes) before initialization fails.

```fprisc
heapInit start end =
  lo = alignUp (Addr.toWord start);
  hi = Word.and (Addr.toWord end) (Word.not (w 15));
  _ = case i hi <= i lo of True -> error "Builtin: heap too small" | False -> Unit;
  _ = case i (Word.sub hi lo) < 96 of True -> error "Builtin: heap too small" | False -> Unit;
  ...
```

