To verify integrity, a program must first append a record to the disk, then use `QL.verifyLog` to confirm its initial validity. After corrupting the payload page via `blkWrite`, a second verification should fail, indicating data inconsistency. Finally, writing the correct data back and running `QL.verifyLog` again should succeed, confirming the record has been healed.

```fprisc
main =
  dsk = device "blk";
  n = blkPages dsk;
  case n == 0 of
    True -> "no disk"
  | False ->
      h0 = QL.ensure dsk;
      h1 = QL.appendRec dsk h0 "QREC" "test" "data";
      ok1 = isOk (QL.verifyLog dsk h1);
      _ = blkWrite dsk (h1 + 1) "corrupted";
      ok2 = isErr (QL.verifyLog dsk h1);
      _ = blkWrite dsk (h1 + 1) "data";
      ok3 = isOk (QL.verifyLog dsk h1);
      "verify passed: " ++ show ok3
```

