```sol
if (netRead.len == 0) {
  // The socket tier reported EOF/FIN/reset
  sendToSelf(EGone)
}
```

The file `std/map.fpr` defines a persistent, ordered map data structure implemented as an AVL tree, ensuring O(log n) insertion and removal while guaranteeing deterministic iteration in ascending key order. It requires a single comparison function provided at construction time to define key ordering, eliminating the need for type classes or hashing. Because the tree shape depends on insertion order, direct equality comparison (`==`) between maps with identical entries but different insertion sequences may fail; users should instead use `Map.equal` for key/value equality or `Map.equalBy` for custom value comparison.

```fpr
Map = use "std/map";
