The `fpr_builtin_alloc_adt` method records exact field counts and uses a compiler-installed immutable descriptor to distinguish managed fields, whereas arbitrary external functions are not admitted into the ARC mode without an explicit ownership contract. While the allocation method supports raw fields containing any bits including live heap addresses, the ARC mode strictly rejects external functions lacking this contract to maintain safety.

```sol
// Compiler-created object using fpr_builtin_alloc_adt
let obj = fpr_builtin_alloc_adt(32, [F32, F32, F32])

// Arbitrary external function call is rejected without ownership contract
