Standard integer division in FP-RISC truncates toward zero, which causes negative results to be rounded up toward zero (e.g., -3 / 2 = -1). The `fdiv` function corrects this by performing true mathematical floor division, rounding negative results down to the next integer (e.g., -3 / 2 = -2). This is necessary when precise floor division is required for potentially negative numerators. The implementation handles this via the rule `fdiv n d | n < 0 = 0 - ((0 - n + d - 1) / d)`.

```fprisc
fdiv n d | n < 0 = 0 - ((0 - n + d - 1) / d);
fdiv n d = n / d;
```

