```sol
bakeCells w lm c | c >= wCells = (w, lm);
bakeCells w lm c =
  (b, w2) = wGet w c;
  (w3, lm2) = bakeCellFaces w2 lm c 0 b;
  bakeCells w3 lm2 (c + 1).
```

A zone is defined as a list of three slots, where each slot is either `Empty` or `Occ` containing a card. To create a zone with one card in the first slot and two empty slots, initialize the zone as `[Empty, Empty, Empty]` and use the `setAt` function to place the card at index 1 (the second slot, as indexing starts at 1 in this logic). The resulting zone will be `[Empty, Occ card, Empty]`.

```sol
zone = [Empty, Empty, Empty];
setAt 1 (Occ "Roach Soldier") zone;
```

The GL context is initialized lazily on the first request within the single `serve` actor, ensuring the context belongs strictly to the thread that will draw. Since the GL context is thread-bound, this actor acts as the sole caller and the mailbox serialization point, requiring the geometry to be handed over from this specific actor. This design prevents context migration issues and ensures that `std.MVU` draws correctly through the actor answering the Rv protocol.

```sol
gl = spawn (GL.serve 960 600);
cfg = { env = 0, mt = mt, tick = 160000, input = gl, render = gl };
MV.game me cfg (App init update subs view)
```

