```sol
hal_heap_before_reserve() {
    // Reserve host heap first to avoid conflict with app address space
    // This ensures apps get their reserved span without host heap interference
}
```

The application does not link the arena's end address into its binary; instead, it reads the reserved span directly from the boot record at runtime. This mechanism allows the app to access the full reserved address space, which can be up to 1 TiB, regardless of the build-time image size limit. To implement this, the application must query the boot record for the allocated span during initialization:

```fprisc
proc init_arena {
    let span := read_boot_record("arena_span");
    let base := read_boot_record("arena_base");
    let limit := base + span;
    // Use span and limit for heap management
}
