To compute the normalized UV coordinates, you first determine the intersection points of the ray with the voxel's height and depth planes, then extract the fractional coordinates along the face's normal vectors. The X coordinate is derived from the Z-plane intersection, while the Y coordinate depends on the face normal: for the top face, it uses the inverted Z-flipped coordinate, and for side faces, it uses the inverted Y-flipped coordinate.

```fpr
fxv = fracOf (hitPoint t1 dxv ox);
fyv = fracOf (hitPoint t2 dyv oy);
fzv = fracOf (hitPoint t3 dzv oz);
# u: the X face reads z, everything else reads x
uu = Vec.sar 12 (Vec.blend (Vec.eqS 0 ax1) fzv fx1);
# v: the Y face reads x-flipped-none (z), the side faces read y flipped
vv = Vec.sar 12 (Vec.blend (Vec.eqS 1 ax2) fx2 (Vec.axpb (0 - 1) (fx - 1) fyv));
```

