To measure service round-trip latency, a script reads a CLINT register (e.g., 49144) to establish a timestamp, sends a message to the service, receives the reply, reads the register again, and calculates the difference. The provided `pollRt` function demonstrates this pattern by iterating `k` times, accumulating the time delta (`statAdd`) for each round-trip.

```sol
pollRt me inp mt k st =
  t0 = read mt;
  _ = send inp (me, Poll 0);
  r = receiveFrom me inp;
  t1 = read mt;
  _ = drop r;
  pollRt me inp mt (k - 1) (statAdd st (t1 - t0)).
```

