The system verifies required permissions by calling `askAllRem` with `True` to check if all entries in the application's required permission list (`manReq`) are granted. If any required permission is missing, the `case` statement evaluates to `False`, triggering an error message stating the application cannot run without all compulsory permissions. If all are granted, the system proceeds to handle optional permissions and execute the application.

```sol
# Example: Launching an app with a missing permission
launchMan io qa m =
  con = ioCon io;
  aid = manId m;
  req = manReq m;
  stored = permsStored io aid;
  _ = putLn con (strcat "Launching " aid);
  _ = putLn con "Required permissions:";
  reqG = askAllRem io stored True req;
  case allTrue reqG of
    False -> putLn con "Cannot Run Application without all required compulsory Permissions"
  | True -> launchGranted io qa m stored reqG.
```

The `launchGranted` function orchestrates the final steps of launching an application after verifying both required and optional permissions. It logs the launch status, processes optional permission requests, persists the permission state, calculates the resulting capability set (`caps`), and finally dispatches the application by calling `runEntry`.

```sol
launchGranted io qa m stored reqG =
  con = ioCon io;
  opt = manOpt m;
  _ = case opt of Nil -> Unit | _ :: _ -> putLn con "Optional permissions:";
  optG = askAllRem io stored False opt;
  _ = persistPerms io (manId m) stored (manReq m) reqG opt optG;
  granted = append (keepGranted (manReq m) reqG) (keepGranted opt optG);
  caps = mkCaps con (ioMe io) (ioClk io) granted (manId m) (ioSt io);
  runEntry con qa m caps.
```

