The `page` function requests a specific range of shards from the front coordinator using `A.askSure`. The coordinator responds with a list of shard identifiers and the keys to fetch from each. The function then iterates over these shards, requesting the specific data rows from each via `A.askSure`, and finally concatenates all returned rows into a single list.

```fprisc
page skip take store = case store of Store front _ ->
  me = myself 0;
  r = A.askSure me front (FPlan skip take);
  (n, parts) = (case r of FPlanIs c ps -> (c, keep ps) | _ -> (0, Nil));
  _ = drop r;
  (L.concatMap (fn part -> (case part of (sh, s, t) -> rowsFrom me sh (SPage s t))) parts, n).
```

The `search` function retrieves elements by first querying the front for the list of shards. It then sends a filter request to each shard simultaneously, collects the resulting rows, and applies pagination logic (skipping and taking elements) before returning the final list and total count.

```fprisc
search pred skip take store = case store of Store front _ ->
  me = myself 0;
  r = A.askSure me front FShards;
  shards = (case r of FShardsAre xs -> keep xs | _ -> Nil);
  _ = drop r;
  _ = L.each (fn sh -> A.sendSure me sh (me, SFilter pred)) shards;
  found = L.concatMap (fn sh -> m = receiveFrom me sh; xs = (case m of SRows ys -> keep ys | _ -> Nil); _ = drop m; xs) shards;
  (L.take take (L.drop skip found), L.length found).
```

