  me = myself 0;
  r = A.askSure me front (FPlan skip take);
  (n, parts) = (case r of FPlanIs c ps -> (c, keep ps) | _ -> (0, Nil));
  _ = drop r;
  (L.concatMap (fn part -> (case part of (sh, s, t) -> rowsFrom me sh (SPage s t))) parts, n).
```

The initial implementation of the buddy allocator iterated through a 1 GiB plugin window one 64 KiB unit at a time, writing a free-list node into each unit, which caused excessive memory usage and application crashes. The corrected version, found in `runtime/buddy.c`, avoids writing inside the range entirely by taking the aligned blocks as a whole, thereby reducing the resident set size and preventing OOM kills.

```sol
// Corrected behavior: allocate the range as whole aligned blocks
// without writing individual free-list nodes into every 64 KiB unit.
buddy_reserve_range(range) {
    // Allocate the entire range as a single block
    // No per-unit node writes performed
}
```

If the buddy allocator is used incorrectly by writing into the whole plugin window, the application will be OOM-killed before it draws anything. This happens because the allocator was previously fencing off the 1 GiB window one 64 KiB unit at a time, writing a free-list node into each unit, which caused every `qosp` process to become 256 MiB resident on 16 KiB pages (on macOS) or consume the whole GiB on the image, triggering an out-of-memory condition. The correct approach is to take the range as whole aligned blocks and write nothing inside it.

```sol
// Correct usage: allocate the range as a whole aligned block without writing inside it
// Incorrect usage: iterating and writing free-list nodes into every 64 KiB unit
// buddy_reserve_range(free_list, 1GiB) // Correct
// For every i in 0..16384: buddy_reserve_range(free_list, 64KiB) // Incorrect
```

The developer should modify the buddy allocator implementation to reserve the entire plugin window as whole-aligned blocks rather than fencing off the range one 64 KiB unit at a time. Writing a free-list node into every unit causes unnecessary memory pressure, as seen when 16,384 writes filled 256 MiB of resident memory on macOS, leading to an OOM kill. By writing nothing inside the reserved range, the application reduces its memory footprint significantly.

```sol
buddy_reserve_range(arena, start, size) {
    // Reserve the entire range as whole-aligned blocks without internal writes
    // to avoid filling memory with free-list nodes unnecessarily.
    buddy_reserve_range(arena, start, size)
}
```

