```

The `sendLinear` mechanism transfers a message slab between actors with zero copies and no Arc growth, ensuring that only one frame root remains live at any moment. Unlike `send`, which deep-copies messages and risks violating copy-on-retain laws if frames are dropped prematurely, `sendLinear` acts as a move operation where the receiving actor takes ownership directly. To implement this correctly, an actor must use `receive` to get the frame, mutate it if necessary, and then `sendLinear` it to the next actor without retaining any reference, thereby preventing Arc growth.

```sol
