In POSIX environments, the lowest page of an actor's stack is made inaccessible to trigger a fault, which is caught by an alternate signal stack to panic the actor with exit code 1. This mechanism incurs a cost of two `mprotect` calls per actor lifetime, consuming approximately 0.9 microseconds, which is less than the 2.6 microseconds spent on a spawn-reply-die cycle.

```fprisc
