The typed tier refuses to doubleize exact-Int arithmetic because the margin-ok arm of `hB` yields an exact-Int (`0 - p.y`), while the violation arm yields an inexact 0. This mismatch prevents the compiler from treating the function as a typed dual. To fix this, store the label as an inexact value at `mkRow` so that all three folds remain native.

```sol
mkRow s =
  s1 = Rand.next s;
  s2 = Rand.next4 s1;
  s3 = Rand.next4 s2;
  cls = Rand.uniform s3 2;
  cx = case cls == 0 of True -> 0 - 1 | False -> 1;
  cy = case cls == 0 of True -> 0 - 1 | False -> 1;
  {x1 = cx + Rand.gauss4 s1 / 2, x2 = cy + Rand.gauss4 s2 / 2,
    y = case cls == 0 of True -> Numeric.inexact (0 - 1) | False -> Numeric.inexact 1}.
```

