The file `fprisc/sol/lib/logic.sol` defines the core logic for the Sol scripting profile within the QOS operating system, specifically implementing the trail-based backtracking mechanism and unification engine required for functional logic programming. It provides the `bind` function to record bindings on a trail for potential backtracking, along with `undoTo` and `unwind` operations to restore the system state to a previous mark. Additionally, it includes `deref` for accessing cell values and `unify` to perform variable unification, which is essential for solving logic problems and executing recursive definitions in Sol.

```sol
bind a t v m = trailPush a (setCell a t v m);
unify a b m =
  (m1, a2, ta, va) = deref a m;
  (m2, b2, tb, vb) = deref b m1;
  case a2 == b2 of
    True -> (m2, True)
  | False -> unify2 a2 ta va b2 tb vb m2.
```

