The system loads the new versioned module bytes into a plugin sub-slot of the running image and registers it in the module table, allowing the new version to sit alongside the old one without write-execute (W^X) or global offset table (GOT) complications. Resolution is handled by walking the module table to find the newest attachment, which wins, while in-flight calls into the old image continue running to completion. This is achieved by using a resolve operation as a table walk followed by a PAP apply for the call, as shown in the `Mod.find` logic:

```fpr
Mod.find = func(name) {
    // Returns the newest attachment for 'name'
    // In-flight calls to the old version continue to completion
    return Mod.table.lookup(name).newest;
}
```

