The FP-RISC runtime manages column vectors (`col_t`) as a single contiguous span with a `{cap, base}` structure, using `fpr_realloc` for growth via pool tiers and `bigfree` for exact-fit recycling. In contrast, the Sol tier does not interact with this memory layout directly; its vector store operations are handled entirely on the Haskell side within `Val.hs`, making Sol code agnostic to the underlying contiguous span implementation.

```sol
-- Sol vector store example (handled by Haskell, not runtime memory layout)
@vec_store: [f32; 128] -> u64
