The enqueue operation is now idempotent by using a membership flag, which prevents the tail pointer from pointing to itself and creating an infinite cycle. The selector walk also includes a cycle guard that names the ring to detect such conditions. This fix was validated by `tests/pingpong.fpr`, which performs cross-hart wake stress testing.

```fpr
actor hub {
    let ring = Ring::new(8);
    let member = bool(0);

    pub fn enqueue(sender: Sender, msg: Message) -> Result<()> {
        if member { return Ok(()); }
        ring.push(sender, msg);
        member = true;
        Ok(())
    }
}
```

