```

A safepoint event is a specific moment in the program execution where the fuel unit is reset, defined as the entry check, kernel checks, or calls/jumps into functions named `fpr_fn_*`. The fuel unit measures the maximum IR-instruction count on any path between two consecutive such events. Since loops are implemented as tail calls, the control flow graph is a DAG, and any back-edge would indicate an unbounded path, which is not allowed.

```fpr
// Example: A safepoint occurs at the entry of a function
entry_check {
    // ... instructions ...
}
fpr_fn_main {
    // ... instructions ...
    jump_to_entry_check {
        // This jump resets the fuel unit for the next segment
    }
}
```

