The FP-RISC runtime disables hardware stack guards and relies on software checks because the P4 processor lacks an MMU and its PMP/watchpoints are not wired up. In `hal.c`, the `hal_stack_guard` function is defined as a no-op. Consequently, FP-RISC code manually checks its own stack window and grows it as needed, whereas standard C code that overruns an actor stack will silently corrupt the memory block immediately below it.

```fp-risc
// hal.c: stack guard is a no-op
