Passing the same object to both `blend` and the next `Rs` causes a use-after-free error because `blend` frees the block and the allocator immediately hands the freed memory back out to the next iteration. This violates memory safety rules in QOS.

```fprisc
# Dangerous pattern: passing the same object to blend and next Rs
(bl, w2) = Vec.gather (Vec.minS (wCells - 1) (Vec.maxS 0 ix1)) w;
(h1, hr) = Vec.dup (Vec.zipMul (Vec.ges 1 bl1) al1);
