The `par2` function in FP-RISC demonstrates parallel execution by spawning a worker, sending it a message with the current thread ID and arguments, and then combining the received result with the output of a sequential function. It handles success by returning the tuple of the received result and the sequential output, or errors if the worker fails.

```fprisc
par2 h f a g b =
  me = myself 0;
  w = spawnOn h parWorker;
  _ = send w (me, f, a);
  rb = g b;
  case receiveRes me of
    Ok ra -> (ra, rb)
  | Err _ -> error "par2: the worker failed".
```

