The function transforms 3D vertices by scaling the x and z axes while inverting the y-axis, effectively rotating the geometry 180 degrees around the x-axis. If a floor offset is required, it calculates the minimum y-value across all triangles and shifts every vertex upward by that amount to create a flat base at zero.

```sol
