    hardware uart_0;
}
```

In this context, the ISA (Instruction Set Architecture) refers to the fundamental hardware architecture that the software runs on, which differs between hosts like the FPRISC processor and the ESP32. The decision to split ESP-IDF was partly driven by the need to handle these architectural differences, moving hardware-specific details out of the core machine layer into platform libraries so that a single POSIX system can support multiple distinct hardware hosts.

```sol
