```

In the FP-RISC architecture, the LOAD section is read during runtime via `runtime/qaimg.c`, which performs a hand-rolled scanner over the section's text to verify consistency and extract metadata like the `sha` line. This design ensures that the portable host, plugins, and native kernel all interact with FP-RISC components on their respective sides of the call, whereas the C loader only places the code.

