// Example of the key scanner logic conceptually used in runtime/qaimg.c
key = scan_load_section_text();
if (key != expected_sha_line) {
    return "consistency_refusal";
}
copy_to_memory(key);
```

In the FP-RISC runtime, the LOAD section is actively read and processed by `runtime/qaimg.c`, which performs a hand-rolled key scanner, consistency checks, and a copy operation across multiple call paths (portable host, plugin, and native kernel). In contrast, the C loader only places the LOAD section into memory without performing these runtime checks or processing steps.

```fprisc
// Example of the FP-RISC key scanner logic found in runtime/qaimg.c
key = scanner.scan(load_section_text);
if (key == -1) {
    return consistency_refusal;
