copy(load_section_text, destination_buffer);
```

The `fill` function iterates over a `pending` object to populate DOM elements that have a `data-input` attribute matching the object's keys. It assigns the stored values to the elements, triggers an `input` event to notify the server of the update, and then removes the entry from `pending` to prevent re-processing. This mechanism ensures that data arriving before the corresponding UI element is created is queued and applied immediately once the element appears in the document tree, managed by a `MutationObserver` watching the `lv-root` container.

```sol
function fill() {
  Object.keys(pending).forEach(function (n) {
    var els = document.querySelectorAll('[data-input="' + n + '"]');
    if (!els.length) return;
    els.forEach(function (el) { 
      el.value = pending[n]; 
      el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input')); 
    });
    delete pending[n];
  });
}
```

This line executes a callback function for each key in the `pending` object but returns `undefined`. The actual work of populating input fields and triggering the `input` event is performed inside the callback's body, specifically by assigning values to elements and calling `el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input'))`.

```sol
Object.keys(pending).forEach(function (n) {
  var els = document.querySelectorAll('[data-input="' + n + '"]');
  if (!els.length) return;
  els.forEach(function (el) { el.value = pending[n]; el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input')); });
  delete pending[n];
});
```

The `live:set` event is triggered by a single-port server (e.g., the one-port) to fill or clear inputs by name. The event detail must be a JSON object where keys correspond to the `data-input` attribute of the target elements. Upon receiving the event, the script parses the JSON, stores values in a `pending` object, and the `fill()` function subsequently updates all matching DOM elements and dispatches an 'input' event to trigger their rendering.

```sol
LJ.src 0 "
(function () {
  var pending = {};
  document.addEventListener('live:set', function (e) {
    var vals = JSON.parse(e.detail);
    Object.keys(vals).forEach(function (n) { pending[n] = vals[n]; });
    fill();
  });
})();
"
```

The script uses a `pending` object to store incoming values and a `MutationObserver` to detect when input elements appear in the DOM. When a `live:set` event fires, the values are stored in `pending` rather than being applied immediately. The `fill()` function is triggered by the observer whenever a new element is found; it then iterates through the `pending` object to assign values to matching elements and dispatch an `input` event, ensuring the UI updates only after the element exists.

```sol
(function () {
  var pending = {};
  function fill() {
    Object.keys(pending).forEach(function (n) {
      var els = document.querySelectorAll('[data-input="' + n + '"]');
      if (!els.length) return;
      els.forEach(function (el) { el.value = pending[n]; el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input')); });
      delete pending[n];
    });
  }
  document.addEventListener('live:set', function (e) {
    var vals = JSON.parse(e.detail);
    Object.keys(vals).forEach(function (n) { pending[n] = vals[n]; });
    fill();
  });
  new MutationObserver(fill).observe(document.getElementById('lv-root'), { childList: true, subtree: true });
})();
```

