if (mx >= box.x && mx <= box.x + box.w &&
    my >= box.y && my <= box.y + box.h) {
    // Hit detected
}
```

In the QOS UI, every box is represented as a rectangle within the 960x600 coordinate space, and mouse clicks are treated as points in this same space. Consequently, selecting an object like a card or button is performed as a rectangle test against the tree structure rather than using raycasting. This approach is defined by the layout logic where the walker reports relative mouse motion, and the picking mechanism relies on these spatial rectangle intersections.

