To read a file and print its contents, you must first open the file with `Os.open`, then enter a loop that calls `Os.ready` to wait for input, reads data using `Os.read`, and writes it to the standard output with `Os.stdout.write`. The loop terminates when `Os.read` returns zero, indicating end-of-file.

```sol
readAndPrint p = 
  fd = Os.open p "r";
  while True = 
    bytes = Os.read fd 1024;
    if bytes == 0 then break;
    Os.stdout.write bytes;
```

