In the V2-AUDIT.md disposition, `txIsDir` is explicitly joined to the read set to ensure directory transactions are properly included, whereas Sol tabling is currently off by default. This distinction ensures that directory operations are not silently corrupted or ignored by the default tabling mechanism, addressing a specific silent-corruption fix where wrong answers were previously given without notice.

```sol
// Example illustrating the read set inclusion for directory transactions
// txIsDir is true, so the transaction is joined to the read set
txIsDir = true;
readSet = readSet + tx;

// Sol tabling is off by default, so tabling does not apply here
