The handler checks if the response status code is 400 or higher; if so, it logs a warning message containing the request details, otherwise it logs an info message. The logged fields include the HTTP method, path, status code, and body length.

```sol
logged log handler req =
  resp = handler req;
  fields = ("method", req.method) :: ("path", req.path) :: ("status", str resp.status) :: ("bytes", str (strlen resp.body)) :: Nil;
  _ = (case resp.status >= 400 of True -> Log.warn log "request failed" fields | False -> Log.info log "request" fields);
  resp.
```

