A real-time contract is a guaranteed behavior defined by the system's timing constraints, whereas an accident represents an unintended deviation or failure within those constraints. In the context of the fixed tables, the system must adhere to the contract to ensure deterministic execution, while accidents indicate violations that require handling or prevention mechanisms.

```sol
-- Example illustrating a contract violation (accident)
-- Contract: Task A must complete before Task B starts.
-- Accident: Task A overruns, causing Task B to start late.

@contract {
  task A {
    duration <= 10ms;
  }
  task B {
    start_time >= A.end_time;
  }
}

-- This execution causes an accident:
