}
```

The `epoch` function performs one iteration of a gradient descent update step for a polynomial regression model. It initializes a new vector of points by folding the input data through three sequential accumulation functions (`gA`, `gB`, and `gC`), which calculate the gradients for the coefficients `a`, `b`, and `c` respectively. After computing these gradients, the function updates the coefficients by subtracting the learning rate scaled by the average gradient (total gradient divided by the number of points `n`), and returns the updated coefficients along with the final vector of points.

```sol
epoch n lr a b c v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (gA a b c) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (gB a b c) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (gC a b c) 0 v2;
  (a - lr * (s1 / n), b - lr * (s2 / n), c - lr * (s3 / n), v3).
```

The `epoch` function iteratively updates polynomial coefficients by folding gradient accumulation functions (`gA`, `gB`, `gC`) over a vector of points to compute sums of squared residuals and their derivatives. It then applies a learning rate to adjust the coefficients `a`, `b`, and `c` based on these accumulated gradients before returning the updated parameters and the final vector.

```sol
epoch n lr a b c v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (gA a b c) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (gB a b c) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (gC a b c) 0 v2;
  (a - lr * (s1 / n), b - lr * (s2 / n), c - lr * (s3 / n), v3).
```

