The expression `spawnAll hub boss 40 0` returns `0` (the identity unit). Its primary effect is to recursively spawn 40 distinct client processes, each running the `client hub boss` actor, onto different CPU harts within the QOS operating system.

The function works by first spawning a single instance of the client on a specific hart (calculated as `1 + 0 % (Sys.harts Unit - 1)`), then immediately recursing with the counter incremented to `1`. This process repeats until the counter `k` reaches `n` (40), at which point the recursion terminates and returns `0`.

```fprisc
spawnAll hub boss 40 0 =
  _ = spawnOn (1 + 0 % (Sys.harts Unit - 1)) (client hub boss);
  spawnAll hub boss 40 1;
  ...
  spawnAll hub boss 40 39;
  0
```

