The `serveFront` function processes a `FPut` request by first calculating the shard index using the configuration's key function and span. It checks the shard map: if the shard exists, it asks the shard to store the data; if not, it spawns a new shard. After the data is stored, it retrieves the current count from the shard, updates the global count map with this new total, and sends a `FDone` message containing the aggregated count to the caller.

```fprisc
serveFront self from q st = case st of Fs cfg shards counts -> (case q of
    FPut x ->
      idx = (cfg.key x) / cfg.span;
      (sh, shards2) = (case M.get idx shards of
          O.Some s -> (s, shards)
        | O.None -> s = spawnShard cfg idx; (s, M.insert idx s shards));
      r = A.askSure self sh (SPut x);
      n = (case r of SCountIs c -> c | _ -> 0);
      _ = drop r;
      counts2 = M.insert idx n counts;
      _ = A.sendSure self from (FDone (total counts2));
      Fs cfg shards2 counts2
```

To insert a value, the `FServe` function is called with a `FServeFront` command as the first argument, followed by the value `x` to be stored. The implementation handles the insertion by calculating the shard index, spawning a shard if necessary, asking the shard to perform a `SPut`, and then updating the counts map before sending a completion signal.

```fprisc
serveFront self from q st = case st of Fs cfg shards counts -> (case q of
    FPut x ->
      idx = (cfg.key x) / cfg.span;
      (sh, shards2) = (case M.get idx shards of
          O.Some s -> (s, shards)
        | O.None -> s = spawnShard cfg idx; (s, M.insert idx s shards));
      r = A.askSure self sh (SPut x);
      n = (case r of SCountIs c -> c | _ -> 0);
      _ = drop r;
      counts2 = M.insert idx n counts;
      _ = A.sendSure self from (FDone (total counts2));
      Fs cfg shards2 counts2
    ...
```

When `serveFront` receives a `FPut x` and the calculated index derived from the key and configuration does not exist in the shard map, it spawns a new shard using `spawnShard`. The newly created shard is immediately inserted into the shard map, and the data is then forwarded to this new shard via `A.askSure` for processing. After the operation completes, the count for that index is updated in the counts map before sending the final done message.

```fprisc
idx = (cfg.key x) / cfg.span;
(sh, shards2) = (case M.get idx shards of
    O.Some s -> (s, shards)
  | O.None -> s = spawnShard cfg idx; (s, M.insert idx s shards));
r = A.askSure self sh (SPut x);
```

