The provided `doParams` function in `uart.fpr` configures the UART by first setting the Divisor Lock Bit (DLAB) to 1, writing the lower 8 bits of the divisor to the device register, writing the upper 8 bits shifted left by 8 to the second register, and finally clearing DLAB to restore the 8N1 mode.

```sol
doConfigUART : unsafe Int -> St -> Int -> a .
doConfigUART me st from d =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  case owner == from of
    False -> reply me from (UErr "not the owner") st
  | True ->
      _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 131;
      _ = write (reg8 dev 0) (band d 255);
      _ = write (reg8 dev 1) (BITSHIFTR d 8);
      _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 3;
      reply me from UOk st.
```

When the caller is the owner, `doParams` returns a success status (`UOk`) and updates the state by writing the divisor latch configuration to the UART device registers before passing the modified state to the caller. The function first sets the DLAB (Divisor Latch Access Bit) to 1, writes the lower and upper byte of the divisor, then clears DLAB to restore the 8N1 baud rate, effectively configuring the baud rate for the UART.

```fpr
doParams2 : unsafe Int -> St -> Int -> Int -> a .
doParams2 me st from d =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 131;
  _ = write (reg8 dev 0) (band d 255);
  _ = write (reg8 dev 1) (BITSHIFTR d 8);
  _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 3;
  reply me from UOk st.
```

