The `grownSlack` function first sums the widths or heights of all children in the row or column to determine `used` space, accounting for gaps between `n` children. It calculates `avail` as the container's inner dimension minus the padding (`p`) on both sides. If any children are marked to grow (`countGrow` returns a value greater than 0), the remaining slack (`avail - used`) is divided equally among them using `idiv`; otherwise, the slack is 0.

```sol
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

