  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

The function `grownSlack` returns the integer amount of horizontal space to be distributed equally among all children marked with the `grow` attribute. It calculates this by determining the available width (container width minus twice the padding), subtracting the total width of children plus the gaps between them, and then dividing the remainder by the count of growing children.

