serveShard cfg q st = case st of
    Sh entries lines path -> case q of
      SPut x ->
        k = cfg.key x;
        _ = append path (J.render (J.object (("k", J.Integer k) :: ("v", one cfg x) :: Nil)));
        entries2 = M.insert k (keep x) entries;
        lines2 = compactIf cfg path entries2 (lines + 1);
        (Sh entries2 lines2 path, SCountIs (M.size entries2))
      ...
```

When the query is `SRemove k`, the function first checks if the key exists in the entries map. If it does, it appends a deletion record to the path, removes the key from the entries map, increments the line count, and returns the updated state with a new count. If the key is not found, the state remains unchanged but the count is still updated based on the current size.

```fprisc
| SRemove k ->
    (if M.member k entries then
       _ = append path (J.render (J.object (("k", J.Integer k) :: ("d", J.Boolean True) :: Nil)));
       entries2 = M.remove k entries;
       lines2 = compactIf cfg path entries2 (lines + 1);
       (Sh entries2 lines2 path, SCountIs (M.size entries2))
     else (st, SCountIs (M.size entries)))
```

