Idle harts now park on a condition variable until signaled by a doorbell or timer deadline, waking up every 200 microseconds for a maximum of 20 milliseconds to prevent hangs. This reduces idle power consumption from 5.0% to 0.4% per core. The mechanism relies on existing protocols in `actors.c` and uses `hal_ipi_send` for inter-processor interrupts and `hal_timer_arm` for deadlines.

