The `step` function processes a single event to update the application model, execute commands, and render the screen. It first invokes `app.update` to generate a new model and a list of commands. It then executes these commands via `perform`, which may spawn asynchronous tasks or recursive quits, initializes new subscriptions, and retrieves the visual representation of the new model using `app.view`. Finally, it paints the screen with these lines and returns the updated state or `O.None` if a quit command was issued.

```fprisc
step me app ev st = case st of St model screen cols rows pending ->
  (case app.update ev model of (model2, cmds) ->
      quit = perform me cmds;
      _ = startSubs me (app.subs model2) (app.subs model);
      lines = app.view (cols, rows) model2;
      _ = paint screen lines 1 rows Nil;
      (if quit then O.None else O.Some (St model2 lines cols rows pending))).
```

