```

Returning `False` allows the caller to yield and retry the shutdown sequence safely, ensuring the worker has finished using its buffers and wake descriptor before the handle is released. This prevents race conditions where a worker might still be executing an arm/take operation when the control block is reclaimed. The caller must ensure no further arm/take calls are issued before the function returns `True`.

```fprisc
let closeResult = Os.watchClose(handle)
