To comply with QOS verification rules, a parser must accept a pointer and a length argument, ensuring it never reads past the end of the provided buffer. Every numeric value parsed must be explicitly bounds-checked before usage. This pattern is implemented in `qaimg.c` as the template for such safety checks.

```c
void safe_parse(qos_image_t *img, uint32_t *out_value) {
    uint32_t end = img->end;
    uint32_t pos = img->pos;
    uint32_t len = img->len;

    // Bounds check before reading
    if (pos + len > end) {
        fpr_cpanic("Parser read past buffer end");
    }

    *out_value = img->data[pos];
    img->pos += 1;
}
```

