The function synchronizes attributes by first mapping existing keyed child nodes from the parent into a lookup table. When processing a desired child node, if a corresponding old node exists and they are compatible, the function iterates through the attributes of the old node. It removes any attributes present on the old node that are absent on the new node and updates attributes that have changed values.

```fprisc
if (old && compatible(old, next)) \{
    if (old !== cursor) parent.insertBefore(old, cursor);
    if (old.nodeType === 1) \{
        Array.from(old.attributes).forEach(function (a) \{
            if (!next.hasAttribute(a.name)) old.removeAttribute(a.name);
        });
        Array.from(next.attributes).forEach(function (a) \{
            if (old.getAttribute(a.name) !== a.value) old.setAttribute(a.name, a.value);
        });
    }
}
```

