The `clash` function calculates simultaneous damage between two units (`u` and `d`) using their attack and shield values, determining which unit(s) are eliminated and adjusting the environment variable accordingly. It first computes the health and usage status for both units after applying damage, counts the total kills, logs the event, and updates the mine and enemy sets for the surviving units. Finally, it increments the environment variable by the number of casualties if any occurred.

```sol
clash k u d g =
  u2 = {u | hp = u.hp - max0 (d.atk - u.sh), used = 1};
  d2 = {d | hp = d.hp - max0 (u.atk - d.sh)};
  kills = boolInt (u2.hp <= 0) + boolInt (d2.hp <= 0);
  g2 = addLog "{u.nm} clashes with {d.nm}" g;
  g3 = putMine k u2 g2;
  g4 = putTheirs k d2 g3;
  g5 = {g4 | env = capEnv (g4.env + kills)};
  case kills > 0 of True -> addLog "casualties: ENV +{kills}" g5 | False -> g5.
```

