```sol
clash k u d g =
  u2 = {u | hp = u.hp - max0 (d.atk - u.sh), used = 1};
  d2 = {d | hp = d.hp - max0 (u.atk - d.sh)};
  kills = boolInt (u2.hp <= 0) + boolInt (d2.hp <= 0);
  g2 = addLog "{u.nm} clashes with {d.nm}" g;
  g3 = putMine k u2 g2;
  g4 = putTheirs k d2 g3;
  g5 = {g4 | env = capEnv (g4.env + kills)};
  case kills > 0 of True -> addLog "casualties: ENV +{kills}" g5 | False -> g5.
```

When a launch proceeds, the full decision set (grants and denials) is appended to the log at `sys/perms/<aid>`. On subsequent launches, remembered decisions replay silently as `grant <url> (<mode>) ? [remembered y]`, except for required permissions remembered as DENIED, which are re-asked to prevent bricking the application. A QDEL storage tag on the file forgets one app's decisions, while `make wipe-disk` clears all history.

Sol:
```sol
// Example: Checking if a permission was remembered as DENIED for a required grant
let aid = "myapp";
let file = "sys/perms/" + aid;
let record = readLatest(file);
if (record != null) {
  // If the record exists, decisions are replayed.
  // If a required perm was DENIED in the past, the system re-prompts instead of replaying the denial.
