The `leadSlack` function calculates the amount of unused space to allocate as a leading gap when a layout's children cannot fully fill its available width or height. It first determines the total used space by summing the widths (for rows) or heights (for columns) of all children and adding the gaps between them. It then calculates the available space by subtracting the padding from the container's dimension. If any children are allowed to grow, the result is zero; otherwise, it returns half of the remaining unused space, rounded down.

```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

