The `moveBy` function calculates new velocity components by decomposing the forward and right movement vectors based on the current yaw angle using sine and cosine. It applies these trigonometric values to the forward (`f`) and right (`r`) inputs, normalizes the result by the forward step size (`fx`), and adds the resulting increments (`nvx`, `nvz`) to the existing velocity vector. The updated model retains the original yaw, pitch, and selection state while appending "move" to the action log.

```fprisc
moveBy (Mdl (Bd px py pz vx vy vz g) yaw pit sel act) f r =
