The Sol contract mandates a specified surface and set of execution guarantees to ensure consistent behavior across different environments. It explicitly defines rules for top-level sequencing, the meaning of `>` statements, default imports, and the treatment of linear resources and transaction boundaries. This separation ensures that observable resource failure and ownership behavior remain specifiable, even if internal memory management or interpreter dispatch techniques are implementation choices.

