The `buddy_alloc` function in FP-RISC allocates a block of size n from the arena. If allocation fails due to exhaustion, it returns `None`. To verify the result, one must check that the returned pointer `p` satisfies `base <= p` and `p + n <= base + MIN * NB`, and confirm the usable size meets the requirement using `buddy_block_usable_size`.

```sol
fn alloc_verify(n: int) -> (ptr: ptr, ok: bool) {
    p = buddy_alloc(n)
    if p is None {
        return (p, false)
    }
    ok = (base <= p) && (p + n <= base + MIN * NB) && (buddy_block_usable_size(p) >= n)
    return (p, ok)
}
```

