The `ring` primitive generates four quarter-circle arcs at the corners using the `arcEnt` function. These arcs are constructed by chaining entities (`addEnt`) to form a continuous path: two horizontal arcs at the top and bottom, and two vertical arcs on the left and right. Each arc is defined by its center coordinates, radius, and start/end angles relative to the viewport dimensions.

