The system uses a `ticker` function that sleeps for a duration calculated from the message interval, then queries the application via `A.askSure` to check if the tick is due. If the application returns `Wanted True`, the ticker recurses; otherwise, it terminates. This logic is applied within `startGo`, which spawns a new ticker process for every message-subscription pair not already active, maintaining a list of running tickers.

```fprisc
ticker reg ms key self =
  _ = Sys.sleepUs (ms * 1000);
  r = A.askSure self reg (TickDue ms key);
  again = (case r of Wanted True -> True | _ -> False);
  _ = drop r;
  (if again then ticker reg ms key self else Unit).
```

