The `tests/check_arc.py` suite validates the sharing and escape cycles within the FP-RISC runtime environment. It ensures zero live allocations occur during execution, verifies tail call optimization, and confirms the correct handling of ownership imports and graph destruction. A typical test involves running 10,000 sharing/escape cycles in a 16 KiB heap, followed by the destruction of a 12,000-node graph, all while running under memory sanitizers to detect invalid memory access.

```fprisc
