    let g = graph(6000);
    return g;
}
```

The `tests/check_builtin.py` suite validates standalone booting, scheduler-free linking, manual ABI compliance, invalid inputs, module resolution, and allocator checks under Address/Undefined Behavior Sanitizers. In contrast, the `tests/check_arc.py` suite specifically targets memory management and graph operations, validating 10,000 sharing/escape cycles within a 16 KiB limit, zero live allocations, tail calls, graph destruction of 6,000 to 12,000 nodes, and imported ownership under sanitizers.

```fprisc
// Example of a graph operation validated by check_arc.py
fn main() {
    let g = graph::new();
    for i in 0..10000 {
        g.add_edge(i, i+1);
