The tier split ensures that `std/` modules are limited to those that can carry formal bounds, whereas `lib/` is permitted to be large and contain modules that cannot prove such bounds. Consequently, any module requiring a proof of safety must reside in `std/`, while unprovable functionality is relegated to `lib/`.
```sol
