Because the runtime contains bugs where a wait loop that allocates on every poll and never reaches a tidy point causes the actor to keep every temporary it ever made until it takes a frame boundary. This leads to memory leaks and crashes, so any loop that can spin for a day must be allocation-free or utilize boundaries and an amortized tidy.
Answer:
```fprisc
// Bad: Allocates on every poll, risks memory leak until frame boundary
loop {
  msg = ask "channel" 1000;
  if msg == 0 then break;
  // ... process msg ...
}

// Good: Uses boundary and tidy to prevent accumulation
loop {
  boundary;
  msg = ask "channel" 1000;
  if msg == 0 then tidy; break;
  // ... process msg ...
}
```

