appendNow @/tmp/rt-live.log "progress: step 2\n";
```

The `appendNow` operation ensures that data is written to disk synchronously before the operation returns, eliminating the latency associated with asynchronous buffering. Consequently, when `readNow` is called immediately after one or more `appendNow` calls, it retrieves the exact bytes that were just written, resulting in a non-zero byte count reflecting the total length of the appended content.

```sol
