The system performs a three-stage integrity check: first, it verifies the image's SHA256 hash; second, it validates the Application Binary Interface (ABI); and third, it confirms the matched-set of required components. Upon passing these gates, the loader enforces W^X (Write XOR Execute) isolation. This process is handled by the loader's built-in gate mechanism, which explicitly refuses execution and names the specific reason for refusal if any check fails.

```sol
# Example gate invocation logic (conceptual)
verify_image integrity {
    if sha256(image) != expected_hash then
        refuse "SHA256 mismatch";
    end if;
    if abi(image) != expected_abi then
        refuse "ABI mismatch";
    end if;
    if matched_set(image) != required_set then
        refuse "Missing component in matched set";
    end if;
    enforce w^x(image);
}
```

