When an interrupt stops the poller, the `waking` function detects this by checking if the received message is `0`. If so, it unbinds the interrupt and sends a `WakerStopped` message to the poller's actor. If the interrupt remains active, it acknowledges the interrupt and re-sends a `Woke` message to continue polling.

```sol
waking poller irq self =
  m = receive self;
  done = m == 0;
  _ = drop m;
  if done then
    _ = unbind irq;
    _ = A.sendSure self poller WakerStopped;
    Unit
  else
    _ = Sys.irqAck irq;
    _ = A.sendSure self poller Woke;
    waking poller irq self.
```

