You can migrate entries by opening the legacy kvlog database, filtering for "model.entries" and its sub-keys, decoding them, and then writing them to the new store. If the store is already open, no migration is needed. If it is empty, the legacy entries are moved, the old log is compacted to remove duplicates, and the new store is returned.

```fprisc
migrate kvPath store = if Store.count store > 0 then 0
  else (case KvLog.open kvPath of
      Err _ -> 0
    | Ok db ->
        es = legacy db;
        _ = List.each (fn e -> Store.put e store) es;
        _ = (if List.isEmpty es then Unit
             else _ = List.each (fn k -> KvLog.put k Json.Null db) (List.filter (fn k -> k == "model.entries" or String.startsWith "model.entries/" k) (KvLog.keys db));
                  _ = KvLog.compact ("$event" :: Nil) db; Unit);
        List.length es).
```

