The store initializes by replaying all log records up to time zero, ensuring that any write occurring after the current time is ignored. When a request arrives, the `serveLog` function processes it by calling `step`; if the request originates from nobody (sender 0), it fails silently without a reply. If the key was not present in the replayed state or was written after the current time, it will not be found in the resulting map.

```sol
