```

When a write operation is posted to the KVLog store (identified by sender 0) and fails to be replayed, the `serveLog` function detects this via the `rt == 0` condition in the `step` function. It then prints a specific error message to standard error indicating the failure reason. The exact error string is: "kvlog: {path}: a posted write failed: {why}".

Example:
```fprisc
serveLog self path m =
  msg = receive self;
  (rt, q) = msg;
  (m2, r) = step path m q;
  _ = (if rt == 0 then (case r of
         Failed why -> _ = Sys.stderr "kvlog: {path}: a posted write failed: {why}\n";
         _ -> Unit
       );
       _ = send rt r;
       Unit);
  _ = drop msg;
  serveLog self path m2.
```

