In FP-RISC, ordinary computation performs zero reference counting; values are slab-allocated and owned by their actor. Reference counting is triggered exclusively when a value escapes via `fpr_arc_incref` at two specific promotion sites: `send` (making the message shared) and `spawn` (pinning the entry closure in the child). The owning slab is also pinned (`escaped++`), and the entire slab is freed only after the last escapee of an orphaned slab is consumed or the actor dies.

```fprisc
