To evaluate a binary string term, the system first dereferences the term to extract its type and value. If the type indicates a string (type 3), the value is divided by 1024 to determine the bit width (s) and modulo 1024 to determine the operation code (ar). The evaluation proceeds only if the width is between 2 and 6 (inclusive) and the operation code is 2; otherwise, it fails. If valid, it delegates to `evalBin` to perform the bitwise operation.
```sol
evalStr f m =
  (m1, tf, fv) = cellAt f m;
  s = fv / 1024;
  ar = fv % 1024;
  case and (and (s >= 2) (s <= 6)) (ar == 2) of
    False -> (m1, Nope)
  | True -> evalBin s f m1.
```

