Promotion moves an object into the ARC.qa pool via a deep-copy, after which a dedicated manager actor is spawned to handle increment and decrement messages. The object remains frozen and accessible via raw pointers until the count reaches zero, triggering automatic deallocation and manager exit. This design replaces complex lock interactions with a single atomic count in the manager's mailbox, ensuring that capacity exhaustion results in a refused promotion error rather than a system panic.

```fprisc
