You can determine the identity of the shell a plugin links against by parsing the QAR2 file's LOAD section. The process involves reading the file, locating the LOAD entry, and extracting the hash value that follows the "sha" keyword within that section. Here is the Python code to perform this operation:

```python
def load_sha_of(qa_path):
    with open(qa_path, "rb") as f:
        b = f.read()
    if b[:5] != b"QAR2\n":
        raise SystemExit(f"not a QAR2 archive")
    head, _, _ = b.partition(b"\n\n")
    off = len(head) + 2
    for line in head.decode().split("\n")[1:]:
        name, o, n = line.split()
        if name == "LOAD":
            load = b[off + int(o) : off + int(o) + int(n)].decode()
            for ln in load.split("\n"):
                if ln.startswith("sha "):
                    return ln.split()[1]
    raise SystemExit(f"no LOAD sha found")
```

