The program measures latency by invoking `stampInput` with an initial key count, which triggers `siStamp` to write a specific value to the CLINT timer register (address 49144) and immediately request the next press. By reading the timer register before and after the service call, the difference represents the service-to-update latency.

```sol
stampInput 400 me =
  m = receive me;
  (from, q) = m;
  siReply 400 from me.

siReply 400 from me = case 400 == 0 of
  True -> send from (0, 0, 0) >> stampInput 0 me
 | False -> siStamp 400 from me.

siStamp 400 from me =
  clint = device "clint";
  mt = reg32 clint 49144;
  _ = send from (4, read mt, 1);
  stampInput 399 from me.
```

