The `moveBy` function computes new velocity components by projecting the forward and right inputs onto the current yaw axis using sine and cosine values. Specifically, it calculates `sw` and `cw` as the sine and cosine of the yaw angle, then derives the new X (`nvx`) and Z (`nvz`) velocity updates by combining these trigonometric values with the forward (`f`) and right (`r`) movement amounts, scaled by the move velocity and normalized by `fx`. The resulting velocities are added to the existing velocity components within the model structure.

```fprisc
sw = sinA yaw; cw = cosA yaw;
