```

The register state `Rs` maintains a `told` set containing writers that have been notified of a model change but have not yet pulled the new model. This mechanism ensures that each writer receives the newest model only once per change, preventing duplicate pulls. If a writer attempts to pull before the register broadcasts the VERSION or before it is added to the `told` set, the writer will skip directly to the latest available model without receiving the specific notification, avoiding the potential queue buildup of millions of sends that would occur if every event triggered a broadcast to every session.

