The prefix sweep is an O(bins) operation used to score every threshold within a column's binning range. After a node performs an O(n) pass to scatter class counts into a flat histogram, the prefix sweep calculates cumulative sums across the bins to efficiently evaluate potential split gains for all thresholds simultaneously. This allows the algorithm to determine the best (column, bin) split if its gain exceeds the minimum gain threshold.

```sol
// Conceptual representation of the prefix sweep logic
// Input: A flat histogram vector where index i represents bin i
// Output: A score vector where each index contains the cumulative gain up to that bin
func prefix_sweep(histogram: Vec<F64>) -> Vec<F64> {
    result = Vec<F64>(length(histogram))
    acc = 0.0
    for i from 0 to length(histogram)-1:
        acc = acc + histogram[i]
        result[i] = acc
    return result
}
```

