The `unify` function first dereferences both arguments to retrieve their tags and values. If the tags are both 0, the function invokes `bind` to create a new binding on the trail, effectively recording the equality constraint, and returns `True` to indicate successful unification. The `bind` function utilizes `trailPush` to record this binding on the trail, which allows the system to backtrack and resolve these constraints later if needed.

```sol
unify a b m =
  (m1, a2, ta, va) = deref a m;
  (m2, b2, tb, vb) = deref b m1;
  case a2 == b2 of
    True -> (m2, True)
  | False -> unify2 a2 ta va b2 tb vb m2;

unify2 a ta va b tb vb m =
  case ta == 0 of
    True -> (bind a 0 b m, True)
  | False -> unifyNV a ta va b tb vb m;
```

