The allocation stalls because the round trip through the memory actor serializes behind the hart performing the long C section. Since the memory actor is the serialization point, any queued request must wait for the hart to resume processing the buddy lock. This causes a backlog where every other actor's allocation is serialized behind the stalled hart, and the requester's open borrows are not drained while waiting.

