To remove a specific session ID, use the `regForget` function, which internally calls `sDel` to filter the session list. This function takes the current state and the session ID to delete, returning a new state with that session removed. For example, if you have a session list `sess` and wish to remove session `sid`, you can execute `regForget st sid`, where `st` is the state containing `sess`.

```fprisc
regForget st sid =
  Rs cfg app model sess nev ns = st;
  Rs cfg app model (sDel sess sid) nev ns;

sDel sess sid = sDelGo sess sid Nil;
sDelGo Nil sid acc = acc;
sDelGo ((i, a) :: r) sid acc | i == sid = sDelGo r sid acc;
sDelGo (e :: r) sid acc = sDelGo r sid (e :: acc);
```

