        goto loop_entry // Back-edge triggers UNBOUNDED
    }
}
```

The mistake causes the server to reject valid WebSocket upgrade requests with a 400 Bad Request error because the header lookup is case-sensitive by design. The test explicitly shows that a request with a lowercase header name (`sec-websocket-key`) results in a 400 response, whereas the correct header name (`Sec-WebSocket-Key`) is required. To fix this, the header lookup logic in the Sol code must be changed to perform a case-sensitive comparison or ensure the incoming header name is normalized to uppercase before comparison.

```sol
