Because the P4 lacks an MMU and its PMP or debug watchpoints are not wired up, the `hal_stack_guard` function in `hal.c` acts as a no-op. Consequently, FP-RISC code checks its own stack window and grows it as needed, but C code that overruns an actor stack silently corrupts the memory block immediately below it.

```fprisc
// hal.c
hal_stack_guard() {
    // No-op when hardware guards are off
}
