  u1 = writePath @/tmp/sol-txn-ctr.txt "{n + 1}";
  u2 = shq "printf q >> /tmp/sol-shq.log";
  u3 = Proc.afterCommit (ProcessSpec ["/bin/sh", "-c", "printf p >> /tmp/sol-ac.log"] "" [] "" 2000);
  (c, o) = sh "printf i >> /tmp/sol-sh.log";
  print "attempt saw {n}".
```

The code below defines a transaction that increments a counter and uses an immediate shell command (`sh`) which executes on every retry attempt, alongside a deferred command (`Proc.afterCommit`) that executes exactly once upon successful commit.

