```fprisc
main =
  clint = device "clint";
  mt = reg32 clint 49144;
  svc = spawn UM.actor;
  h = U.open svc;
  u = U.arm h 4096;
  (n, u2) = U.write u "payload-0123456789\n";
  U.flush u2;
  (rx, u3) = waitRx u2 mt (read mt + 80000000);
  "tx={n}B flushed; rx={strlen rx}B".
```

The `U.write` function sends data to the UART device and returns a tuple containing the number of bytes written and the updated handle to the buffer. Specifically, the first assignment returns the byte count `n1` (which is 13) and the handle `u2` for the next write; the second assignment returns the byte count `n2` (which is 21) and the handle `u3`.

