```sol
(envLog, envMt, (titles, vfs)) = env;
titlesList = envTitles env;
vfsList = envVfs env;
```

This constant defines the maximum number of virtual keyboards that the operating system can open simultaneously. If a ninth keyboard is attempted to be opened, the system will fail to create it. This limit is enforced in the event driver file `hal/unix/evdev_raw.c`.

```sol
// Example: Attempting to open the 9th keyboard would be refused by the kernel
// because MAXKBD is defined as 8.
Host.openKeyboard(9) -> Error("Too many keyboards");
```

The entry ABI defines a static buffer of 64 KiB (`static char result[64 * 1024]`) to store the application's result string. Any result exceeding this size is truncated, and the application is required to manually hand back a pointer and a length to handle data larger than the buffer.

```sol
Host.run {
    static char result[64 * 1024];
    // If app result > 64 KiB, only first 64 KiB is stored here.
    // App must return: (pointer, length) for full data.
}
