The `targetOk` function validates a target by first calculating the opposing side and checking if the column difference is within one unit. It then applies specific logic based on the target's row: row 1 checks for occupancy at the target column, row 2 checks for occupancy at the target column while ensuring the lane is clear, and rows 3 and above check if the target column is free of occupancy at the lane level.

```sol
targetOk m s c tz tc =
  o = sideOf m (1 - s);
  case Int.abs (c - tc) <= 1 of
    False -> False
  | True -> targetOk2 o tz tc.
targetOk2 o 1 tc = occ o 1 tc;
targetOk2 o 2 tc = occ o 2 tc and not (occ o 1 tc);
targetOk2 o 3 tc = lane o (tc - 1) or lane o tc or lane o (tc + 1);
targetOk2 o z tc = False;
lane o c = not (occ o 1 c) and not (occ o 2 c);
```

