```

The `measure` function calculates the total width and height required to display a `Box` element, including its padding and gaps between children. It first determines the dimensions of each child, then sums their widths and gaps along the row axis (or heights and gaps along the column axis) using the `msum` helper, while taking the maximum dimension across the orthogonal axis. Finally, it adds twice the padding of the box to the resulting inner dimensions.

```fprisc
measure (Box a kids) =
  p = padOf a; g = gapOf a;
  (mw, mh, n) = msum (isRow a) kids;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  inner = case isRow a of
    True -> (mw + gaps, mh)
  | False -> (mw, mh + gaps);
  sized a (iw + 2 * p, ih + 2 * p).
```

