```fprisc
// Example of the hand-rolled scanner logic used in runtime/qaimg.c
key = scanner.scan(load_section_text);
if (consistency_checks.refuse(key)) {
    // Rejects the load if consistency rules are violated
    return error;
}
copy_data(load_section_text, key);
```

`runtime/qaimg.c` is a QOS utility that implements the complete load path for the LOAD section of an image. It executes a hand-rolled decimal key scanner over the LOAD section's text, performs five consistency checks, and executes the copy operation. This function is invoked by the portable host when loading an application or plugin, as well as by the native kernel when loading a process.

```fprisc
// Example logic within runtime/qaimg.c
load_section := key <decimal> scanner
if (consistency_checks(load_section) == 5) {
