To compute the mean and standard deviation, you first calculate the sum of the vector, divide by the length to get the mean, then fold the squared differences from the mean to get the variance, and finally take the square root. Here is the code:

```sol
def mean_sd (v: Vec<Int>) -> (Float, Float):
  n = Num.int (Vec.len v);
  if n == 0: return (0.0, 0.0);
  s0 = Vec.fold plus 0 v;
  mu = Num.float (s0 / n);
  sq = Vec.fold (sqDev mu) 0 v;
  sd = Num.sqrt (sq / n);
  return (mu, sd);

def sqDev (mu: Float) (x: Int) -> Float:
  return Num.float ((Num.float x - mu) ^ 2);
```

