The `countOf` function returns the number of shards in the shard pool. It obtains this count by using `A.askSure` to request the `SCount` state from the shard (`sh`) and extracting the integer value `c` from the resulting `SCountIs c` pattern; if the state is not `SCountIs`, it defaults to 0.

```fprisc
countOf me sh =
  r = A.askSure me sh SCount;
  n = (case r of SCountIs c -> c | _ -> 0);
  _ = drop r;
  n.
```

In FP-RISC, fan-out describes the amount of data an actor (such as the register) must process or copy when updating the model. A lower fan-out indicates better performance, as less data needs to be transferred. For example, the register actor copies the whole model during tidying, which can be optimized to reduce this overhead.

```sol
// Example of an actor with high fan-out copying the whole model
actor register {
  tidy() {
    copy whole model to updated state;
  }
}
```

The register is a single actor responsible for copying the entire model whenever it performs tidying operations, whereas Sol actors operate within the browser's v3 protocol which utilizes incremental rendering. In FP-RISC code, the register's full model copy is a bottleneck, while Sol templates only re-render changed assigns of a compiled template.

```fprisc
// Register copies the whole model during tidy
register.tidy = model => {
  model = tidy(model);
  return model; // Full copy
};

// Sol re-renders only changed assigns
@template = compile(template);
render(assigns.changes) { ... }
```

