The `Str` prelude defines `strTake` to extract the first `n` characters of a string by recursively concatenating characters until the count is reached. The implementation uses `strTakeGo` to iterate through the source string `s`, accumulating characters in `acc` until the index `i` exceeds the limit `n`.

```sol
fn strTakeGo s n i acc =
  if i > n then acc
  else strTakeGo s n (i + 1) (strcat acc (chr (charAt s i)));

fn strTake s n = strTakeGo s n 1 "";
```

The `advance` function simulates the progression of an animation clock by calculating the next time step and determining whether the current animation instance should trigger a midpoint event or finish. It takes the current animation state `m` and a time increment `dt`, computes the new time `t2`, and checks if `t2` has reached or exceeded half of the animation's duration to decide if a `midpoint` rule applies. If the animation is complete, it calls `finishAn`; otherwise, it updates the animation state with the new time.

```fpr
advance m dt =
  An kind s fz fc tz tc t done = m.anim;
  t2 = t + dt;
  m1 = case done == 0 and t2 >= durOf kind / 2 of
    True -> { (midpoint m kind s fz fc tz tc) | anim = An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 1, snap = m.snap + m.auto * bi (kind < 4) }
  | False -> { m | anim = An kind s fz fc tz tc t2 done };
  case t2 >= (case kind == 4 of True -> 0 | False -> durOf kind) of
    True -> finishAn m1 kind s fz fc tz tc
  | False -> m1.
```

The expression returns a modified state `m2` which is the result of spending one turn (`spend m s 1 fc`) and then applying a land blow attack (`landBlow m2 s fc tz tc a.atk`) on the slot of the side of `m` at that specific turn and frequency. The final value is this combined state `m2` with the attack details resolved into the slot's attributes.

```fpr
midpoint m 2 s fz fc tz tc =
  m2 = spend m s 1 fc;
  a = slotOf (sideOf m s) 1 fc;
  landBlow m2 s fc tz tc a.atk;
```

