```fprisc
function send(msg, arg) \{
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    fetch('/live/event', \{
      method: 'POST',
      body: JSON.stringify(\{ msg: msg, arg: String(arg) })
    }).then(function (r) \{ return r.json(); }).then(function (res) \{
      apply(res);
      stamp(msg, performance.now() - t0, res);
    }).catch(function () \{ /* server gone; locals keep working */ })
      .finally(function () \{ busy = false; });
  }
```

The `apply` function returns `undefined` in both cases. When `res.s` is truthy, it updates the `S` object with the shape and delta, calls `build()` to re-render the entire view, and then returns immediately. When `res.s` is falsy, it iterates over keys in `res.d`, updates the corresponding DOM elements' text content and classes to trigger a reflow, and then returns without modifying `S`.

```sol
function apply(res) {
    if (res.s) { S = { s: res.s, d: res.d }; build(); return; }
    for (var k in res.d) {
        S.d[k] = res.d[k];
        var el = root.querySelector('[data-slot="' + k + '"]');
        if (el) {
