The `logged` function acts as a middleware wrapper that intercepts every HTTP request, processes it through the core handler, and then logs the outcome based on the response status code. It constructs a list of fields containing the request method, path, status code, and body size. If the response status is 400 or higher, it triggers a `Log.warn` with the message "request failed"; otherwise, it triggers a `Log.info` with the message "request". The function returns the modified response unchanged.

```sol
logged log handler req =
  resp = handler req;
  fields = ("method", req.method) :: ("path", req.path) :: ("status", str resp.status) :: ("bytes", str (strlen resp.body)) :: Nil;
  _ = (case resp.status >= 400 of True -> Log.warn log "request failed" fields | False -> Log.info log "request" fields);
  resp.
```

The `epoch` function implements one iteration of gradient descent training for a polynomial model. It calculates the gradients for the coefficients (a, b, c) and the data points (v) by folding three specific gradient accumulation functions (`gA`, `gB`, `gC`) over the vector of data points. The function then updates the coefficients by subtracting the learning rate (`lr`) scaled by the average of the accumulated gradients and returns the updated coefficients along with the final set of data points.

```sol
epoch n lr a b c v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (gA a b c) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (gB a b c) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (gC a b c) 0 v2;
  (a - lr * (s1 / n), b - lr * (s2 / n), c - lr * (s3 / n), v3).
```

