The file `fprisc/std/live.fpr` defines the core logic for the `advance` function, which orchestrates a single step of the FP-RISC distributed execution model. It ensures that events are journaled first, followed by the application's update to the model and state persistence, and finally, the broadcast of the new version to all active sessions to guarantee consistency. The process concludes by either settling the state if the application has quit or starting new tickers for continued execution.

```fprisc
advance me ev st = case st of
    Rs cfg app model sessions nextSid db saved tickers version told ->
        _ = (if cfg.journal then journal app.codec db ev else Unit);
        (model2, cmds) = app.update ev model;
        saved2 = persist me app.fields db model2 saved;
        quit = perform me sessions cmds;
        told2 = broadcast me (M.values sessions) (version + 1) told;
        if quit then
            settle app.fields db model2 saved2
        else
            startTickers me (Rs cfg app model2 sessions nextSid db saved2 tickers (version + 1) told2);
```

The `advance` function first journals the event to the database if journaling is enabled, then updates the application model and persists the new state. It broadcasts the incremented version number to all active sessions to notify them of the change, and finally settles the database or terminates sessions depending on whether the update caused a quit.

```fprisc
advance me ev st = case st of Rs cfg app model sessions nextSid db saved tickers version told ->
  _ = (if cfg.journal then journal app.codec db ev else Unit);
  (case app.update ev model of (model2, cmds) ->
      saved2 = persist me app.fields db model2 saved;
      quit = perform me sessions cmds;
      told2 = broadcast me (M.values sessions) (version + 1) told;
      (if quit then _ = settle app.fields db model2 saved2; _ = goodbye (M.values sessions); O.None
       else O.Some (startTickers me (Rs cfg app model2 sessions nextSid db saved2 tickers (version + 1) told2)))).
```

The `advance` function processes a single event within the system's event loop by first journaling the event if configured, then updating the model and persisting the new state to the database. It broadcasts the updated version number to all active sessions and conditionally settles the model or terminates the session based on the command stream generated by the update.

```fprisc
