The provided `epoch` function iterates through three gradient folds using `Vec.fold` to compute sums of gradients for weights and bias, then applies the learning rate formula to update parameters. It returns the updated weights, bias, and the final accumulated gradient vector.

```sol
epoch n lr w1 w2 b v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (gW1 w1 w2 b) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (gW2 w1 w2 b) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (gB w1 w2 b) 0 v2;
