An actor is admitted when it is ready to execute, and if it is currently in the run queue (indicated by `acb in_rq`), it is never added to the backlog again. This admission rule prevents stale pushes from creating duplicate run queue entries.
```sol
// Example showing an actor in the run queue (acb in_rq)
