    // Once admitted and in_rq, the actor cannot be re-added to the backlog
    // even if a waker arrives late.
}
```

This rule prevents a deadlock scenario where a stale push from a waker creates a second run queue entry pointing to itself, causing the hart to spin indefinitely in the dequeue loop. By strictly enforcing that only admitted actors can be admitted, the system ensures that if a waker's message arrives late and flips an actor's state to READY, the actor can re-park and be re-woken before any push arrives, avoiding duplicate entries.

```sol
