The `words` function demonstrates memory allocation, writing, reading, and deallocation within FP-RISC. It allocates a 16-byte block, writes a bitwise negated integer to it, reads the value back to verify correctness, reallocates the block to 32 bytes (keeping the data), and finally frees the memory. The `main` function confirms that the total live allocations return to zero after these operations, proving that all temporary blocks are properly released.

