The `VEQ_INLINE` macro defines the maximum number of value pairs held on the C stack before the worklist for equality comparison moves to a dynamically allocated `fpr_alloc` block. This prevents stack overflow when comparing deeply nested structures. For example, setting `VEQ_INLINE 32` ensures that if a comparison requires more than 32 pending pairs, the system switches to heap allocation to handle the depth safely.

