@export "heap"

@builtin "main"
fun main = {
  let x = 42
  return x
}
```

The migration replaces the C implementation with an FP-RISC `heap.fpr` file that utilizes typed memory layouts (LANDED), which expand into ordinary definitions at parse time to reduce code size and enable tier-1 readability. For hosted systems, this migration supports stack safety by defining the stack as spanning the entire block it was given, where an overflow triggers a named panic from a guard page on POSIX and QOS Portable, whereas bare metal implementations currently lack guard pages.

```fprisc
// Example: Typed layout usage in heap.fpr
Block = Layout {
    size: u32,
    align: u32,
};

// Example: Stack safety check
func safe_stack_operation() -> u32 {
    let stack_ptr = get_stack_block();
    if (stack_ptr is out_of_bounds) {
        panic "Stack overflow detected";
    }
    return 0;
}
```

