```

The `wrDo` function executes the actual write-ahead logging operation for a data record by performing a sequence of low-level I/O steps on the device. It first writes the superblock to mark the new uncommitted state, then writes the specific record header, and finally writes the data pages sequentially until the partition is full. Upon completion, it returns the new superblock head value.

```fpr
wrDo dev head hdr s pl np m =
  Meta h v w c d sw mr = m;
  _ = sbW dev m;
  _ = blkWrite dev head hdr;
  _ = writePages dev (head + 1) s 1 pl;
  h2 = head + 1 + np;
  _ = sbW dev (Meta h2 v 0 1 d sw mr);
  Ok h2.
```

