The `uart.fpr` module defines the functional interface for the Universal Asynchronous Receiver-Transmitter (UART) device within the QOS operating system, specifically handling the low-level initialization and parameter configuration of the 16550-compatible UART hardware. It exposes two primary operations: `doOpen`, which claims device ownership and initializes the FIFO and interrupt lines, and `doParams`, which allows the current owner to configure the baud rate divisor and data format. The implementation ensures that only the owning process can modify parameters and sets the FIFO enable bit and disables interrupts during initial setup to prevent data loss during boot.

```fpr
doOpen me st from =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  case owner == 0 of
    False -> reply me from (UErr "uart is claimed") st
  | True -> doOpen2 me st from;

doOpen2 me st from =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  d2 = device "uart";
  _ = write (reg8 d2 3) 3;
  _ = write (reg8 d2 1) 0;
  reply me from UOk (St d2 from cap txq rxs sub fl 0);
```

To configure the UART divisor latch, call the `doParams` function as the owner of the device, passing the current state, the message, the source, and the desired divisor value. This function sets the DLAB register to 131 to enable the divisor latch, writes the lower byte of the divisor to register 0, writes the upper byte to register 1, and finally restores DLAB to 3 for normal 8N1 operation.

```fpr
doParams me st from d =
  St dev owner cap txq rxs sub fl armed = st;
  _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 131;
  _ = write (reg8 dev 0) (band d 255);
  _ = write (reg8 dev 1) (BITSHIFTR d 8);
  _ = write (reg8 dev 3) 3;
  reply me from UOk st.
```

