To retrieve a file's data, you must first obtain the unique ID associated with the file (typically managed by System.qa or Files.qa via a URL). Once the ID is known, the system aggregates all chunks sharing that ID to reconstruct the file content. The underlying storage uses a recursive chunk-based structure where each chunk contains a header, body, and hash; the system folds these chunks together to produce the final file data.

