The `poc.disk` file serves as a bootstrapping storage volume containing essential services, specifically the `System.qa` and other service quality assurance modules, which the bootstrapper reads to initialize the system. It implements the disk's recursive chunk-based storage model where data is append-only, metadata tracks the HEAD pointer and versioning flags, and compaction utilizes Merkle trees to merge and mark pages for deletion while maintaining idempotency.

