`QOS_NET_TXCAP` defines the maximum amount of data queued for a slow reader before the connection is dropped to prevent stalling. Specifically, if 256 KiB is queued for a single reader, the connection is terminated. This ensures that one slow client does not block the entire system.

```sol
// Example illustrating the drop threshold
if (queued_data_size >= 256 * 1024) {
    drop_connection()
}
```

The system is designed so that a slow reader stalls only itself to prevent blocking other connections. Once 256 KiB is queued for a specific reader, that reader is dropped via the `QOS_NET_TXCAP` limit. This isolation ensures that one unresponsive client does not exhaust shared resources for the entire system.

```sol
// Example of a reader that may be dropped due to QOS_NET_TXCAP
actor reader {
  receive {
    data = read();
    if (queue_size > QOS_NET_TXCAP) {
      drop();
      return;
    }
    write(data);
  }
}
```

