ys = Rc.retain xs;
_ = Rc.release xs;
_ = print ys;
Rc.release ys.
```

To use `Rc.retain`, call it with a shared reference to get back the same object, ensuring ownership is preserved if the original was shared. This is necessary when constructing data structures where a shared child must be placed into an owning field or where an owning alias needs to be kept alive.
```sol
xs = [1, 2, 3];
ys = Rc.retain xs;
```

Explicit unsafe operations like `Rc.release` allow manual control over releasing ownership but are rejected when automatic ARC is enabled to prevent double release. Automatic ARC manages lifetimes automatically, whereas manual mode requires explicit calls and forbids passing raw floats, actors, vectors, or mutable runtime objects to the reclamation API.

```sol
