The page-in mechanism is triggered by the wake path when a sender's CAS operation on a paged actor changes its state from BLOCKED to READY. The hart loop's dequeue routine detects the PAGED status and re-reads the latest chunk from the actor's identity (a per-sender SPSC channel) directly from memory. Since chunks are short-lived and whole-record, the system simply reads the existing data and switches the actor in, appending nothing to the log. This approach avoids disk I/O entirely because the chunk is already resident in memory as part of the actor's identity, and no write-back ordering is required due to the append-only heap discipline.

