The `diskapp.fpr` module defines the disk as a single append-only log where the current state is derived by replaying all records at their original byte offsets. To retrieve this state, one must reconstruct the memory layout by iterating through the log, applying each record's delta to a base state. Below is a Sol function demonstrating this replay logic:

```sol
replayLog log =
  state = createEmptyState();
  for (record in log) do
    state = applyDelta(state, record.seq, record.offset, record.length, record.payload);
  return state;
```

