To prevent a cached slot address from following an actor onto another hart, ensuring thread-local storage remains isolated per core. The implementation relies on `fpr_esp_hart` as a real task-local pointer accessed via volatile inline TLS loads, which generates matching TLS relocations in the ESP code while leaving bare-metal lowering unchanged.

```sol
// Example of host-safe hart accessor using volatile inline TLS load
let hart_ptr = volatile inline tls_load(fpr_esp_hart);
```

The ESP implementation in `os_io.c` omits the Unix SIGPIPE handler and instead preserves lookup failure codes within an error string, as `gai_strerror` is unavailable on the target. This ensures host-safe operation without relying on Unix-specific signal semantics.

```sol
// Example of error handling in os_io.c
if (lookup_result == FAIL) {
