The `nestedProbe` function returns `Unit` (the implicit return type of a Sol function without an explicit declaration), and the value of `s` is `6`.

The function creates an inner vector `[1, 2, 3]`, pushes a unit value onto it to create an outer vector, and then retrieves the inner vector via `Vec.get`. The `Vec.fold` operation sums the elements of the retrieved inner vector (`1 + 2 + 3`), resulting in `6`. The final lines `u1 = Vec.free back2` and `u2 = Vec.free outer2` release the heap allocations but do not affect the integer sum `s`.

```sol
nestedProbe u =
  inner = Vec.fromList [1, 2, 3];
  outer = Vec.push inner (Vec.new Unit);
  (back, outer2) = Vec.get 1 outer;
  (s, back2) = Vec.fold (fn a x -> a + x) 0 back;
  u1 = Vec.free back2;
  u2 = Vec.free outer2;
  s.
```

