The `pushOne` function executes the core rendering logic for a WebSocket session. It first extracts the application state from the session context, then invokes `G.render` to generate a new view (`s2`) and delta (`d2`) based on the current model. It checks if the static layout (`ls`) has changed by comparing it against the new state (`s2`); if unchanged, it sends a delta JSON update, otherwise it sends a full state JSON update. Finally, it returns a new session context with the updated view and delta to drive the next iteration of the loop.

```sol
pushOne st =
  Cs reg port cfg app cid mode buf sid ls ld model = st;
  App ini upd vw sbs = app;
  (s2, d2) = G.render (vw sid model);
  _ = case G.sameStatics ls s2 of
      True -> pushDelta cid (G.deltaJson ld d2)
    | False -> _ = netWrite cid (wsFrame 1 "\{\"s\":{G.jarr s2},\"d\":{G.jarr d2}}"); 0;
  Cs reg port cfg app cid mode buf sid s2 d2 model.
```

The `apply` method parses incoming raw JSON data to synchronize the client's internal state with the server. If the data contains an "s" key, it updates the sequence list `self.s` and delta list `self.d` while incrementing `self.fulls`. Otherwise, it iterates through the keys of `self.d` to update integer-indexed values in the delta list and increments `self.deltas`.

```python
def apply(self, raw):
    res = json.loads(raw)
    if "s" in res:
        self.s, self.d = res["s"], res["d"]
        self.fulls += 1
    else:
        for k, v in res["d"].items():
            self.d[int(k)] = v
        self.deltas += 1
    return res
```

