def flatten_elf(elf):
    """ELF64 PT_LOADs -> (base, entry_off, execsz, rwoff, image, memsz)."""
    if elf[:4] != b"\x7fELF":
        raise SystemExit("mkqa: not an ELF image")
    if elf[4] != 2:
        raise SystemExit("mkqa: only ELF64 (the QOS app targets are all 64-bit)")
    # ... (rest of the implementation handles segment parsing and image construction)
```

The function calculates the executable size (`execsz`) by finding the maximum virtual address of any PT_LOAD segment that has the `PF_X` (executable) permission flag set, relative to the base address. The read-write offset (`rwoff`) is determined by finding the minimum virtual address of any PT_LOAD segment that has the `PF_W` (write) permission flag set, defaulting to the total memory size if no writable segments exist.

