-- Subsequent reads will return the same snapshot data
read stdin; 
read stdin;
```

`Vec.filter` executes eagerly in-place using two cursors to compact rows, avoiding per-element branches by storing a branchless MASK column and restoring density later via `Vec.compact`. In contrast, `Vec.fold` fuses through a write-back mechanism where the map function's writes are stored into a column and immediately folded over, ensuring program-visible writes without separate allocation.

```fprisc
// Vec.filter example: In-place compaction with a mask
let v = Vec.filter f x
// v is dense; if not, Vec.compact v restores density

// Vec.fold example: Fused map and fold
let r = Vec.fold f z (Vec.map g v)
// g(v[i]) is written to a column and folded over in one pass
```

