The file `fprisc/std/store.fpr` defines core data access operations for the FP-RISC store, specifically providing functions to retrieve individual keys, extract paginated ranges of data, and perform distributed searches across shards. It implements high-level logic that delegates low-level requests to the store's front coordinator and shards, handling responses to return filtered lists and counts. For instance, the `page` function retrieves a specific range of keys from the store by first querying the front for shards and then fetching rows from those shards, while `search` allows filtering data based on a predicate across all shards concurrently.

```fprisc
page skip take store = case store of Store front _ ->
  me = myself 0;
  r = A.askSure me front (FPlan skip take);
  (n, parts) = (case r of FPlanIs c ps -> (c, keep ps) | _ -> (0, Nil));
  _ = drop r;
  (L.concatMap (fn part -> (case part of (sh, s, t) -> rowsFrom me sh (SPage s t))) parts, n).
```

The `page` function retrieves a specific range of items from a store by first querying the front for the shards involved via an `FPlan` request. It then iterates through the returned shards, asking each one for its specific data page using an `SPage` request, and finally concatenates all the results into a single list.

```sol
page : Int -> Int -> Store a -> (List a, Int) .
page skip take store = case store of Store front _ ->
  me = myself 0;
  r = A.askSure me front (FPlan skip take);
  (n, parts) = (case r of FPlanIs c ps -> (c, keep ps) | _ -> (0, Nil));
  _ = drop r;
  (L.concatMap (fn part -> (case part of (sh, s, t) -> rowsFrom me sh (SPage s t))) parts, n).

rowsFrom me sh q =
  r = A.askSure me sh q;
  rows = (case r of SRows xs -> keep xs | _ -> Nil);
  _ = drop r;
  rows.
```

The `page` function retrieves a list of values and a count from a store, skipping a specific number of items and taking a specific number of subsequent items. It operates by first querying the front for shards to plan a `FPlan` operation with the skip and take parameters. If the plan is valid, it iterates through the returned shards, requesting rows from each using `SPage`, and finally concatenates the results from all shards.

```fprisc
page skip take store = case store of Store front _ ->
  me = myself 0;
  r = A.askSure me front (FPlan skip take);
  (n, parts) = (case r of FPlanIs c ps -> (c, keep ps) | _ -> (0, Nil));
  _ = drop r;
  (L.concatMap (fn part -> (case part of (sh, s, t) -> rowsFrom me sh (SPage s t))) parts, n).
```

The `page` function returns a pair consisting of a list of values (`List a`) and an integer count (`Int`). It retrieves the specified number of items starting after the skip count, ordered by greatest key, by first querying the front for shards, then requesting page data from each shard, and finally concatenating the results.

```sol
page skip take store = case store of Store front _ ->
  me = myself 0;
  r = A.askSure me front (FPlan skip take);
  (n, parts) = (case r of FPlanIs c ps -> (c, keep ps) | _ -> (0, Nil));
  _ = drop r;
  (L.concatMap (fn part -> (case part of (sh, s, t) -> rowsFrom me sh (SPage s t))) parts, n).
