The file `qos/programs/terra2.fpr` defines the core logic for the Overwatch and Ambush mechanics in the Terra2 game scenario within the QOS operating system. It implements the `resolveAttack` function to handle these special attacks, which occur once per enemy turn and resolve before the main blow lands. The code specifies that an attacker who is defeated before striking deals no damage, utilizing `intercept` to apply half damage to the target and `ambush` to deal full damage from a revealed rear unit.

```fpr
resolveAttack m s c tz tc =
  m1 = intercept m s c tc;
  m2 = ambush m1 s c tz tc;
  a = slotOf (sideOf m2 s) 1 c;
  case alive a of
    False -> note m2 "the attacker fell before striking"
  | True -> landBlow (spend m2 s 1 c) s c tz tc a.atk.
```

The `ambush` function first checks if the target unit in the rear slot is alive, face-down (`down == 1`), and ready (`rdy == 1`). If these conditions are met, it triggers a `reveal` which sets the unit's `down` and `born` flags to 0. Immediately after revealing, the function executes `damageUnit` to deal the unit's attack value to the attacker. If the conditions are not met, the function returns the modifier unchanged without performing any actions.

```fprisc
ambush m s c tz tc =
  o = sideOf m (1 - s);
  u = slotOf o 2 tc;
  case alive u and u.down == 1 and u.rdy == 1 of
    True -> reveal m s c tc u
  | False -> m.

reveal m s c tc u =
  o = sideOf m (1 - s);
  m2 = setSide m (1 - s) (setSlot o 2 tc { u | down = 0, born = 0 });
  m3 = damageUnit m2 s 1 c u.atk;
  cue (note m3 "AMBUSH! {cName (uCard u)} hits for {u.atk}") Sfx.ambush.
```

