The `scanLocals` function in `livejs.fpr` iterates through all elements with the `x-data` attribute, splits the attribute value by semicolons, and parses each `name=value` pair to populate a client-side `locals` object. It uses `indexOf` to locate the equals sign and `slice` to extract the variable name and value, ignoring empty pairs.

```sol
function scanLocals() {
  root.querySelectorAll('[x-data]').forEach(function (el) {
    el.getAttribute('x-data').split(';').forEach(function (pair) {
      if (!pair) return;
      var eq = pair.indexOf('=');
      if (eq > 0) {
        var name = pair.slice(0, eq);
        var value = pair.slice(eq + 1);
        locals[name] = value;
      }
    });
  });
}
```

The `scanLocals` function iterates through all elements with the `x-data` attribute to populate a `locals` object with their initial values. It splits the attribute string by semicolons to isolate individual declarations, then splits each declaration by an equals sign to separate the variable name from its value. If a name is not already in the `locals` object, it is added with the parsed value.

```sol
function scanLocals() \{
  root.querySelectorAll('[x-data]').forEach(function (el) \{
    el.getAttribute('x-data').split(';').forEach(function (pair) \{
      if (!pair) return;
      var eq = pair.indexOf('='), n = pair.slice(0, eq);
      if (!(n in locals)) locals[n] = pair.slice(eq + 1);
    });
