The `renderWorker` function acts as a worker thread that processes incoming requests from a parent thread to render frames. It receives a request (`m`) from the parent, extracts the state, model, view, and style components, and calls the application's `vals` function to generate the new view. It then invokes the service call (`svcCall`) to execute the render logic, sends the result back to the parent, and finally resets the system frame pool to mark the end of the frame cycle.

```fprisc
m = receiveFrom self parent;
Rq st model vw vh sc fr = m;
vs = vl self env (vw, vh) model;
r = svcCall self render (Render st vs sc fr);
_ = send parent r;
_ = drop r;
_ = drop m;
_ = Sys.poolReset 0;
```

