Without parentheses, the arms following the inner `case` are syntactically attached to that inner case, causing the outer case to become non-exhaustive or the inner case to gain unreachable arms. This ambiguity is resolved at compile time by case coverage checks, which refuse the shape regardless of the types involved.
```fprisc
