The `rounds` function implements a recursive loop that decrements a counter `n` until it reaches zero. In each iteration, it spawns a server and a client concurrently using `spawnOn`, then synchronizes by receiving messages from both processes via `receive`, before recursing with the decremented counter.

```sol
rounds me poll n = if n == 0 then Unit else
  listener = need (TCP.listen "127.0.0.1" 0);
  _ = spawnOn 0 (server listener poll me);
  _ = spawnOn 1 (client (TCP.port listener) poll me);
  _ = receive me;
  _ = receive me;
  rounds me poll (n - 1).
```

