The file `std/mvu.fpr` provides the MVU driver as a library that implements a persistent render worker architecture, eliminating per-frame actor creation and ledger overhead. It enforces soft death by resetting the system pool at every frame boundary and utilizes a statics cache that only rebuilds when the model key changes. The design relies on two actors within the caller: a dispatch/input actor and an update actor, while drawing is handled as a render service.

```fpr
# Example of the Rv protocol used for rendering
sendTo (self, Rv {
  target = self;
  payload = {
    model = model;
    view = view;
  };
});
```

The MVU driver utilizes a single persistent actor to handle the render worker lifecycle, avoiding per-frame actor spawning. Instead of spawning new actors for each frame, the worker sends a request, and the frame loop manages the response cycle. The implementation below demonstrates a Sol function that initializes this persistent worker and handles the request-response pattern where the worker processes the render command and returns the result without dropping its own reference until the frame advances.

```sol
fun renderWorker() {
  // Initialize the persistent render worker
  // This actor lives for the life of the app
  let worker = spawn Actor {
    // Receive the render request
    receiveFrom msg {
      // Process the render request
      let result = doRender(msg.data)
      // Send the reply back to the caller
      send msg.reply(result)
      // Drop the worker's own ref to advance the frame
      drop self
    }
  }
  // The worker is now active and waiting for requests
  worker
}
```

The persistent render worker is a single actor that exists for the entire application lifetime, receiving frame requests rather than spawning new instances per frame. It manages soft death by triggering a system pool reset at every frame boundary, which enforces frame-per-actor memory semantics and allows the worker to self-heal after a drop lapse. This design eliminates the need for per-frame actor creation and ledger management.

```fprisc
// Conceptual representation of the worker's lifecycle and reset behavior
actor RenderWorker {
  // Persistent for app lifetime
  persistent: true

  onFrameStart:
    Sys.poolReset() // Soft death trigger at frame boundary

  onFrameEnd:
    dropSelfRef()   // Advance drops previous frame's reply
}
```

