The QOS loader reconstructs an image by parsing headers written for a different purpose, consuming two byte ranges, an entry, and a W^X boundary as defined by QAR2. It utilizes the system's existing tokenizer to parse the five numbers provided directly by QAR2. Failure modes are explicitly named as refusals rather than malformed-header errors, specifically: "image outside the window", "execsz reaches rwoff", and "sha mismatch".

```sol
load_image {
    parse QAR2;
    tokenizer system_tokenizer;
    range1 := bytes[0:2];
    range2 := bytes[2:4];
    entry := bytes[4:6];
    wx_boundary := bytes[6:8];

    if (range1 > window) then refuse "image outside the window";
    if (execsz >= rwoff) then refuse "execsz reaches rwoff";
    if (hash_mismatch) then refuse "sha mismatch";

    reconstruct image;
}
```

The QOS loader does not utilize ELF machinery, meaning it performs no relocation, dynamic linking, or symbol resolution at load time. Instead, it parses headers to reconstruct loads based on two byte ranges, an entry point, and a W^X boundary, utilizing named refusal failures like "image outside the window" to handle errors rather than malformed headers.
```sol
