A program targeting QOS must route all input and output obligations through the `Svc.read` and `Svc.write` functions, which operate over capability-checked URLs. The underlying hardware abstraction layer is managed by a C-side HAL table (`qos_hal_t`) that dispatches operations, ensuring the FP-RISC program cannot directly access hardware implementation details.

```fpr
import QOS;
import QOS.Svc;
import QOS.Caps;

proc main = 
    let url = QOS.make_url("stdio");
    let cap = QOS.check_cap(url);
    let data = QOS.read(Svc.read, cap);
    QOS.write(Svc.write, cap, data);
```

