The code ensures statistical correctness by performing two distinct vector folds. The first fold, `Vec.fold plus 0 raw`, calculates the sum of the raw inputs to derive the mean (`mu`). The second fold, `Vec.fold (sqDev mu) 0 raw1`, applies a JIT fold with the captured mean to compute the sum of squared deviations (`sq`) for the standard deviation (`sd`). Crucially, the training process uses `Vec.map (mkPt mu sd) (Vec.range 1 n)` to construct `pts`, which converts the original integer features into standardized floats using the pre-calculated statistics before passing them to the `train` function. This guarantees the model learns from the standardized distribution rather than the raw integers.

```sol
