(a, b, c, pts2) = train 120 n 0.3 0 0 0 pts;
```

To compute the mean and standard deviation, first convert the integers to zeros using `toZ`, then fold the vector to calculate the sum and divide by the count to get the mean. Next, fold the vector again using a squared deviation function that captures the mean, and finally take the square root of the result divided by the count.
```sol
