raw = Vec.map toZ (Vec.range 1 n);
(s0, raw1) = Vec.fold plus 0 raw;
mu = s0 / n;
(sq, raw2) = Vec.fold (sqDev mu) 0 raw1;
sd = Num.sqrt (sq / n);
```

The example computes the mean ($\mu$) by folding the range of numbers with the `plus` function and dividing the sum by the count $n$. The standard deviation ($sd$) is derived by first calculating the sum of squared deviations from $\mu$ using a JIT-fold with the `sqDev` function, then taking the square root of that sum divided by $n$. During deployment, these captured statistics ($\mu$ and $sd$) are passed to a `std` function which standardizes a fresh grid of inputs before the `predict` function applies the learned model coefficients.

```sol
