The string subtraction operator (`-`) returns the left operand unchanged if the right operand is not a suffix of the left operand. Internally, it first checks if the length of the right operand exceeds the left; if so, it returns the left operand. Otherwise, it verifies if the right operand matches the suffix of the left starting at the appropriate offset. If the suffix match fails, the original left operand is returned without modification.
```fprisc
strSub a b =
  la = strlen a;
  lb = strlen b;
  case lb > la of
    True -> a
  | False -> strSubGo a b la lb;
```

