The `epoch` function implements a single pass of gradient descent by folding a vector of points through three sequential gradient accumulators (`gA`, `gB`, and `gC`) to compute the total derivatives of the squared error with respect to the intercept, linear coefficient, and quadratic coefficient. It then applies a learning rate to these accumulated gradients to update the parameters `a`, `b`, and `c` before returning the updated vector of points. The implementation uses `Vec.fold` to process the data sequentially, ensuring that gradients for the linear and constant terms are calculated based on the intermediate state of the vector after the quadratic term's gradient has been accumulated.

```sol
epoch n lr a b c v =
  (s1, v1) = Vec.fold (gA a b c) 0 v;
  (s2, v2) = Vec.fold (gB a b c) 0 v1;
  (s3, v3) = Vec.fold (gC a b c) 0 v2;
  (a - lr * (s1 / n), b - lr * (s2 / n), c - lr * (s3 / n), v3).
```

