The `walk` function calculates the new coordinates using `dxOf` and checks if an enemy exists at those coordinates via `enemyAt`. If an enemy is found, it triggers an attack by calling `endTurn (hitEnemy ...)`. If no enemy is present, the function checks if the destination tile is blocked using `blocked`; if blocked, it ends the turn with a "blocked" message, otherwise it updates the player's position to the new tile.

```sol
walk m d =
  (dx, dy) = dxOf d;
  nx = m.px + dx;
  ny = m.py + dy;
  m1 = { m | dir = d };
  case enemyAt m1.ens nx ny of
    En i ex ey hp :: _ -> endTurn (hitEnemy m1 i nx ny)
