The QOS system initializes the UART by writing the value 3 to register 3 (the control register) to set the FIFO enable bit, followed by writing 0 to register 1 (the interrupt enable register) to disable interrupts until the device is armed. The FIFO enable bit is set to 0 during the open sequence because the real 16550 hardware requires the FIFO to be enabled in a context that owns the device from reset, whereas QEMU's simulation keeps the FIFO enabled regardless. Additionally, the system avoids writing to the FIFO Control Register (FCR) during the initial open to prevent resetting the receive FIFO prematurely, which could cause data loss if the user's first keystrokes are already buffered.

```fpr
_ = write (reg8 d2 3) 3;
