The reference counting mechanism fails because Rc is strictly limited to intra-actor usage. The documentation states that "Rc never crosses an actor boundary," meaning any attempt to share reference-counted data between actors violates the contract, as inc/dec operations are plain stores designed only for single-actor contexts.

