  { "my_func", &my_func },
  { 0, 0 }
};
```
Ensure this array is referenced correctly by the application descriptor or the generated C wrapper in `apps_data.c`.

The `genapps.py` tool reads a list of Sol application files specified via the `qa` argument, extracts their manifest IDs, and generates a C file containing arrays of binary blobs (`qa_blob_t`) and symbol-to-object mappings (`app_entry_t`). It constructs the `fpr_qa_blobs` array by pairing each application's ID with its raw bytes and length, and the `fpr_app_entries` array by pairing symbol names with pointers to their respective objects, ultimately writing these definitions to a file like `runtime/core/apps_data.c`.

```c
const qa_blob_t fpr_qa_blobs[] = {
  { "app_id_1", qa_0, sizeof(qa_0) },
  { "app_id_2", qa_1, sizeof(qa_1) },
  { 0, 0, 0 }
};

const app_entry_t fpr_app_entries[] = {
  { "my_symbol", &fpr_obj_my_symbol },
  { 0, 0 }
