_ = drop m4;
```

To calculate the average latency, you must first modulo the frame index by the latency ring size to determine the correct slot, then use `Vec.set` to update the ring and `Vec.fold` to sum the values. Finally, divide the sum by the ring size and 1000 to convert from 10 MHz clint ticks to tenths of milliseconds.
```fprisc
lv1 = Vec.set (imod n latN + 1) lat lv;
(lsum, lv2) = Vec.fold sumF 0 lv1;
ms10 = lsum / minI n latN / 1000;
```

The `mulMV` function computes the resulting vector by performing four fused multiply-add operations, where each component of the output vector is the dot product of a specific row of the matrix with the input vector. This operation is applied within `refSum` by generating a sequence of input vectors via `Std.fold`, transforming each into a matrix-vector product using `mulMV`, and then accumulating the scalar score of the result.

```sol
Std = use "../std/std";
refSum m lim = Std.fold 1 lim (fn i acc -> acc + score (mulMV m {x = i, y = i * 2 - 3, z = 7 - i, w = 1})) 0;
score r = r.x * 3 + r.y * 5 + r.z * 7 + r.w;
```

