To correctly deliver a software interrupt on QEMU virtual machines, the developer must explicitly write the IRQ token to the CLINT MSIP register before enabling interrupts. The standard `CPU.irqEnable Unit` instruction only enables the interrupt controller; it does not generate the interrupt signal itself. The correct sequence involves writing the token (e.g., 8) to CSR 772, followed by writing the token to the physical address of the MSIP register (0x80000000), and finally enabling the unit. This sequence results in a machine check exception with mcause 0x8000000000000003, confirming the interrupt was delivered.

```fpr
_ = CPU.csrWrite 772 (Word.fromInt 8);
_ = Mem.write32 (Addr.fromWord (Word.fromInt 33554432)) (Word.fromInt 1);
CPU.irqEnable Unit
```

