To determine the total width, one must first extract the fixed widths of all widgets and sum them using `sumFix`. Next, identify the count of flexible widgets using `hasFlex` or by iterating the list, then calculate the remaining space by subtracting the fixed sum from the total available width. Finally, distribute this remaining space among the flexible widgets based on their count, add it to the fixed sum, and use `vbuild` with the resulting list of widths to construct the layout. The `splitSizes` function handles the distribution of the remaining height to flexible items, which can be adapted for width calculation by swapping dimensions, while `vbuild` assembles the final widget list.

```fpr
totalWidth parts avail =
  (w, h) = (avail, 0);
  fixedSum = sumFix (modesOf parts);
  flexCount = length (modesOf parts);
  remaining = maxI 0 (avail - fixedSum);
  flexWidths = if flexCount == 0 then Nil else (remaining / flexCount) :: Nil;
  vbuild parts (append (map (fun x -> x) (if flexCount == 0 then [0] else [remaining])) (map (fun x -> x) (if flexCount == 0 then [0] else [0]))) 0
```

