An actor's pool is reclaimed only via a reset operation, which is triggered at the boundary of each turn. To prevent state accumulation, the actor sends its entire state to itself, resets the pool to discard all temporary data from the previous turn, receives the state back, and then drops the message before continuing. This ensures that every turn starts with a fresh memory environment.

```fprisc
boundaryR me st =
  _ = send me st;
  _ = Sys.poolReset 0;
  m = receiveFrom me me;
  st2 = keep m;
  _ = drop m;
  st2.
```

