The `grownSlack` function calculates the amount of unused space along an axis and divides it equally among all children marked with the `grows` attribute. It first computes the total width or height of the children and the number of gaps between them, then determines the available space by subtracting the total used space from the container's inner dimension. If at least one child has the `grows` attribute, the remaining slack is divided by the count of such children; otherwise, no slack is distributed.

```fprisc
grownSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  ng = countGrow kids;
  case ng > 0 of
    True -> idiv (avail - used) ng
  | False -> 0.
```

