The `splice` function calculates the edit distance by first finding the length of the longest common prefix between the old and new lists using the `common` function. It then identifies the length of the longest common suffix by reversing the remaining portions of both lists and finding their common prefix. The number of characters to remove is the difference between the remaining length of the old list and the suffix length, while the number of characters to insert is the difference between the remaining length of the new list and the suffix length. The function returns a formatted string representing these operations.

```fprisc
splice old new =
  prefix = common old new 0;
  a = L.drop prefix old;
  b = L.drop prefix new;
  suffix = common (L.reverse a) (L.reverse b) 0;
  remove = L.length a - suffix;
  insert = L.take (L.length b - suffix) b;
  "[{prefix},{remove},{J.render (J.strings insert)}]".
```

