Since the built-in `==` operator only performs tag-shallow comparison, you must implement a hand-rolled loop in userland to compare string contents safely. This is demonstrated in `base.sol`, where string helpers are explicitly constructed to handle this requirement, though the implementation is noted to be O(n²) by design.

```fpr
fn safe_eq(s1, s2) {
  if length(s1) != length(s2) then return false
  let i = 0
  while i < length(s1) {
    if charAt(s1, i) != charAt(s2, i) then return false
    i = i + 1
  }
  return true
}
```

