To prevent race conditions between stopping a poller and registering new waiters, the system requires publishing a Watch before announcing registration. The owner must wait for both announcements to complete before issuing the stop command, ensuring no new registration races the stop contract. This is implemented by sending a Watch first, then sending the registration, receiving the confirmation from the poller, and finally sending a cancellation flag if the note indicates a cancellation occurred.

```fprisc
waiter p fd boss me = case p of P.Poller a ->
  _ = need (send a (P.Watch fd me));
  _ = need (send boss me);
  note = receiveFrom me a;
  cancelled = case note of P.Cancelled -> True | _ -> False;
  _ = drop note;
  _ = need (send boss cancelled);
  Unit.
```

The program must publish a Watch before announcing registration, and the owner must wait for both the Watch announcement and the registration announcement before initiating the stop. This ensures no new registration races the stop contract. The implementation spawns multiple waiter processes, confirms they are registered, stops the poller, and verifies that all waiters receive a Cancelled signal.

```sol
waiter p fd boss me = case p of P.Poller a ->
  _ = need (send a (P.Watch fd me));
  _ = need (send boss me);
  note = receiveFrom me a;
  cancelled = case note of P.Cancelled -> True | _ -> False;
  _ = drop note;
  _ = need (send boss cancelled);
  Unit.

one p fd me =
  a = spawn (waiter p fd me);
  b = spawn (waiter p fd me);
  _ = receiveFrom me a;
  _ = receiveFrom me b;
  _ = P.stop p;
  check (receiveFrom me a) "first waiter not cancelled";
  check (receiveFrom me b) "second waiter not cancelled".
```

