The `marchSun` function utilizes the `negPos` helper to check if any coordinate is negative. If `negPos` returns true, the function immediately returns `(0, w)`, terminating the march to prevent the ray from aliasing back into the world due to integer division truncation. This ensures the fixed-step march respects the fixed-point values rather than the cell indices.
```fpr
marchSun w px py pz 0 = (0, w).
marchSun w px py pz k =
  nx = px + sunX / 2;
  ny = py + sunY / 2;
  nz = pz + sunZ / 2;
  marchAt w nx ny nz (k - 1) (nx / fx) (ny / fx) (nz / fx).

negPos px py pz = or2 (or2 (px < 0) (py < 0)) (pz < 0).
```

