The `quit` variable must be explicitly bound to the result of `perform me cmds` within the `case` expression so that the subsequent `if quit then O.None` check correctly identifies the termination condition. If `quit` is omitted or assigned incorrectly, the function will fail to compile or return an unexpected state because `perform` returns a `Bool` indicating whether the quit flag was set. The correct pattern ensures the boolean result propagates to the final state transition:

```fprisc
step me app ev st = case st of St model screen cols rows pending ->
  (case app.update ev model of (model2, cmds) ->
      quit = perform me cmds;
      _ = startSubs me (app.subs model2) (app.subs model);
