The client scans all elements possessing the `x-data` attribute, parses the semicolon-delimited key-value pairs, and stores them in a local dictionary. For instance, if an element has `x-data="tab=1;press=0"`, the client extracts `tab` and `press` into its `locals` object.
```fpr
function scanLocals() \{
  root.querySelectorAll('[x-data]').forEach(function (el) \{
    el.getAttribute('x-data').split(';').forEach(function (pair) \{
      if (!pair) return;
      var eq = pair.indexOf('='), n = pair.slice(0, eq);
      if (!(n in locals)) locals[n] = pair.slice(eq + 1);
    });
  });
}
```

The client must split the `x-data` attribute value by semicolons, then for each pair, find the index of the equals sign to separate the variable name from its initial value. The variable name is extracted as the substring before the equals sign, and the value is the substring after it. If the equals sign is missing, the pair should be skipped. The correct implementation uses `indexOf` to locate the delimiter and `slice` to extract the parts, ensuring only the value portion is stored in `locals`.

```sol
var eq = pair.indexOf('=');
if (eq < 0) return; // Skip if no '=' found
var name = pair.slice(0, eq);
var value = pair.slice(eq + 1);
locals[name] = value;
```

The client scans all elements with the `x-data` attribute, splits the attribute value by semicolons, and extracts key-value pairs to populate a local state object. If a variable name is not already present in the client's locals, it is initialized with the value from the attribute string.
