The client identifies elements containing the `x-data` attribute, splits the attribute value by semicolons to isolate key-value pairs, and stores each variable's value in a `locals` object keyed by the variable name. This process populates the client-side state without round-tripping to the server unless an event explicitly requests it.

```sol
function scanLocals() {
  root.querySelectorAll('[x-data]').forEach(function (el) {
    el.getAttribute('x-data').split(';').forEach(function (pair) {
      if (!pair) return;
