The `leadSlack` function calculates the available space by subtracting the total width of the children and their gaps from the container's width minus twice the padding, then divides the remainder by two. If any children are growing, the function returns zero.
```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

The `leadSlack` function determines the unused space along the primary axis (width for rows, height for columns) after accounting for padding, gaps between children, and the total width or height of the children. If there are children that can grow, the lead slack is set to zero. Otherwise, it calculates the difference between the available space and the used space, then divides that difference by two to distribute the remaining space evenly.

```fprisc
leadSlack row a kids w h p =
  (mw, mh, n) = msum row kids;
  g = gapOf a;
  gaps = case n > 1 of True -> g * (n - 1) | False -> 0;
  avail = case row of True -> w - 2 * p | False -> h - 2 * p;
  used = case row of True -> mw + gaps | False -> mh + gaps;
  case countGrow kids > 0 of
    True -> 0
  | False -> idiv (avail - used) 2.
```

