Stack overflow checks can be disabled by turning off the hardware stack guard in `sdkconfig.defaults` or by making the `hal_stack_guard` function a no-op in `hal.c`. The hardware guard is removed because actors run on their own stacks, causing every switch to appear as an overflow; this is also done because the ESP-IDF overflow check is absent for hart tasks. Disabling the hardware guard risks stack corruption, while removing the `hal_stack_guard` check risks silent corruption of blocks below an overrun actor stack since there is no MMU or wired-up PMP/watchpoint. Additionally, the idle-task watchdog checks can be disabled in `sdkconfig.defaults` on CPU-bound harts, though this risks a hung hart not being reported.

```sol
